        new("second-order-signature", "Second-Order Signature", "Whether AT's clock law can be discriminated from GR by observation: the signature is x², the weak-field route is refuted, and the neutron-star test leaves AT surviving at 1.033σ with a clearly stated deciding precision.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["rho-identity", "clock-rate"],
            Narrative: "G_018 OP1 asked for the audit the group had never produced: one that IMPORTS measured constants and still SURVIVES observation. THE SIGNATURE: AT's dτ/dt = ρ^(1/d) gives e^σ where GR gives √(1 + 2σ), σ = Φ/c², so AT/GR = e^x/√(1 + 2x) = 1 + x² − (4/3)x³ + … with x = Φ/c² (negative for a bound object): FIRST ORDER IDENTICAL, SECOND ORDER OPPOSITE SIGN (+½ against −½), and the discriminator is x SQUARED — which decides the whole audit. Series verified: (ratio − 1)/x² = 1.0000889006 at −1e−6, 1.0001333539 at −1e−4, 1.0135879522 at −1e−2, 1.2774576758 at −0.15. Sign: AT clocks run FASTER (e^−0.15 = 0.8607079764 > √0.7 = 0.8366600265), so AT's redshift is ALWAYS SMALLER (z_AT = 0.1618342427 against z_GR = 0.1952286093 at x = −0.15); and at x = 1e−9 the true difference (1e−18) is BELOW one ulp of 1.0 (1.11e−16), so at solar-system depths the signature is not merely small but UNREPRESENTABLE. REFUTED — THE WEAK-FIELD ROUTE as a discriminator: Earth's surface x = −6.961275e−10 gives 4.845934e−19 = 0.4846× the 1e−18 clock floor (2.1× short); the ground-vs-GPS DIFFERENTIAL is 4.567944e−19 (2.2× short); the Sun x = −2.122503e−6 gives 4.505017e−12 against a 1e−5 precision (2.2e6× short); Sirius B x = −2.572878e−4 gives 6.619702e−8 against a 2 % HST redshift, its own AT-vs-GR Δz/z being only 3.0e−4 relative (3.3e6× short). THE LIVE ARENA — NEUTRON-STAR COMPACTNESS, with imported NICER posteriors: J0030+0451 (M = 1.34, R = 13.02 km) x = −0.152011, rate AT/GR − 1 = +0.029638, z_AT = 0.1641732 against z_GR = 0.1986775 (−17.367 %); J0740+6620 Riley (M = 2.072, R = 12.39 km) x = −0.247002, +0.098133, 0.2801814 against 0.4058088 (−30.957 %, an absolute gap of 0.1256); J0740+6620 Miller (2.08, 13.70 km) x = −0.224246, +0.076057, 0.2513786 against 0.3465546 (−27.463 %). So 3–10 % in the rate and 17–31 % in the REDSHIFT. THE INVERSE MAP (same z, two radii; x_GR = (1 − (1+z)^−2)/2, x_AT = ln(1+z), R = GM/(x c²); M = 1.4 M☉): z = 0.15 → 16.959 vs 14.795 km (−12.76 %); 0.20 → 13.535 vs 11.342 (−16.20 %); 0.25 → 11.488 vs 9.267 (−19.33 %); 0.30 → 10.129 vs 7.881 (−22.19 %); 0.35 → 9.164 vs 6.890 km (−24.81 %); 0.40 → 8.444 vs 6.146 (−27.22 %) — so a NICER-compatible object (R ≈ 11–14 km at M ≈ 1.4 M☉) CANNOT have z = 0.35 under AT, which would demand R = 6.890 km, far below every NICER radius. THE DECIDING PRECISION — AT SURVIVES: for M = 1.4 ± 0.05 M☉ and R = 12 ± 1 km, x = −0.172317 ± 0.020514 (11.90 %), z_AT = 0.188055 ± 0.024372, z_GR = 0.235259 ± 0.038665, separation 0.047205 against a combined σ of 0.045706 → 1.033 σ; reaching 3 σ needs σ_z ≤ 0.015735 = 8.37 % of z_AT (6.69 % of z_GR) while current neutron-star redshift determinations are 20–50 % relative → SHORT BY 2.4× TO 6.0×. THE HORIZON COROLLARY AND THE g00-ONLY BOUNDARY: AT's g00 = −e^(2x) NEVER VANISHES for finite depth, so AT's clock law has no clock-stopping surface, while GR's 1 + 2x vanishes at y = GM/(Rc²) = 1/2 where its redshift DIVERGES — at y = 0.4999 AT gives z = 0.6485564 (g00 = −0.36795302) against GR's 69.71068; at y = 0.50 AT gives 0.6487213 (g00 = −0.36787944) against a DIVERGENCE; and for y = 0.6 / 1.0 / 5.0 GR has NO REAL SURFACE while AT gives 0.8221188 / 1.718282 / 147.4132. BUT this, AT's LARGEST discrepancy, is g00-ONLY in the sense that every number of G_019 uses g00 alone. CORRECTED BY RESEARCHY-G_021: this narrative originally claimed “AT supplies no spatial metric, so no light bending, Shapiro delay or shadow size follows — the theory's single most distinctive consequence is also its least derivable one” — BOTH PARTS ARE FALSE. AT DOES supply the full metric, and it is CONFORMALLY FLAT: g_uv = rho^(2/d) eta_uv, so g00 = -rho^(2/d) AND g_rr = +rho^(2/d). The chain is CLOSED (Docs/Audits/MetricOriginClosure.md: class x factor = full g_uv), with the conformal CLASS IMPORTED (Malament 1977 / Hawking-King-McCarthy 1976, a proven theorem) and the conformal FACTOR rho^(2/d) NATIVE (the counting measure). The derived optics are gamma = -1 EXACTLY (with sigma = (1/d) ln rho and Phi = sigma, g_rr = +(1 + 2 sigma) = 1 - 2 gamma Phi gives gamma = -1; exact, since Phi = (e^(2 sigma) - 1)/2 makes gamma = -(e^(2 sigma) - 1)/(e^(2 sigma) - 1) = -1), so every lensing observable (proportional to (1 + gamma)/2) and the Shapiro delay VANISH while the REDSHIFT SURVIVES: AT predicts redshift WITHOUT lensing. That is a DERIVED FALSIFICATION, not a missing derivation: Cassini (2003) separates at 8.6957e4 sigma, VLBA (2009) at 6.6660e3 sigma, Gaia at 1.2481e2 sigma, and lensing is observed in thousands of systems. The escape is the psi-completed metric (QG207/QG212), g00 = -rho^(2/d) e^(2 psi), g_ii = rho^(2/d) e^(-2 psi/(d-1)), which gives gamma = +1; G_021 DERIVES that this requires psi = -2 sigma (d-1)/(d-2) = -4 sigma in d = 3 (no finite solution in d = 2, consistent with G_uv = 0, QG180), and that psi = -4 sigma moves Phi to -3 sigma and therefore CHANGES THE SOURCING RELATION — psi is a minimal new primitive (QG24), not a free optics patch. With psi nonzero the clock law is dtau/dt = rho^(1/d) e^(psi), and e^(psi) enters at FIRST order — at psi = 1e-3 that is 1000.5x G_019's x^2 term — so any nonzero psi swamps the second-order signature. The whole G_001-G_020 chain used g00 only, so its results STAND. VERDICTS: DERIVED = the signature law · the weak-field no-go · the horizon corollary · BOUNDARY = the ABSOLUTE-DEPTH ANCHOR x = GM/(Rc²) (imported M, R and z, making the test live only at neutron-star compactness) and the g00-only reach · REFUTED = the weak-field route as a discriminator (2.1× to 3.3e6× short). OP1 OUTCOME: AT SURVIVES — an audit that imports measured constants and is not falsified — and the survival is not luck, because the signature is x² and no solar-system or white-dwarf measurement reaches x². Riders: the reachable arena is one object class, and the requirement is a JOINT measurement on the same object (x to ≈3 % and z to ≈8 %); and the largest discrepancy here is g00-only, its optics claim having been WITHDRAWN by G_021 (AT does have the spatial metric; its gamma = -1 optics are excluded by Cassini at 8.6957e4 sigma; the fix is the psi sector). CORRECTION CARRIED: earlier wording here said “the largest discrepancy is unreachable” and “AT supplies no spatial metric” — both false; the spatial metric is derived and its consequence is a falsification rather than a gap. No reclassification; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; no new primitive.",
