        new("photon-ontology-audit", "Photon Ontology Audit", "What would the photon BE in AT, and can the theory supply one without importing U(1)? BOUNDARY: the obstruction is representation-theoretic - spin-1 needs a three-dimensional irrep and the single ring's group (dihedral, order 192, irreps 4 one-dim + 47 two-dim) stops at dimension 2 - while the cubic substrate supplies T1(3). The graviton's traceless part needs a dimension-3 irrep for the SAME reason, so photon and graviton are blocked by the same missing substrate, which G_033 showed was absorbed into the assumed primitive eta. U(1) itself IS derived and compact (Z_96) but global; the '12 link-directions = 12 gauge generators' claim is falsified; and AT already has a link phase, so the missing primitive is the spacetime index and the dynamics.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["electromagnetism-inventory-audit", "field-equation-derivation-audit", "literal-verdict-audit"],
            Narrative: "What would the photon BE in AT? Trace Difference -> Actualization -> Spectrum -> ? and test massless, spin-1, gauge invariance, Maxwell limit, propagation. CRITICAL QUESTION: can AT supply a photon WITHOUT importing U(1), of the kind 96^3 provides elsewhere? ANSWER: BOUNDARY - the theory need not import U(1) as an axiom, and it cannot supply the photon without the cubic substrate. " +
            "(1) THE OBSTRUCTION IS REPRESENTATION-THEORETIC AND DECISIVE. The photon is spin-1 -> l = 1 -> THREE dimensions. The single ring's group is the DIHEDRAL GROUP OF ORDER 192 - verified ON THE PERMUTATIONS: rotation order 96, reflection order 2, s r s^-1 = r^-1, generated order 192 - whose irreps are 4 ONE-DIMENSIONAL and 47 TWO-DIMENSIONAL with 4*1 + 47*4 = 192 = the group order (checked for every even n from 4 to 200). MAXIMUM IRREP DIMENSION 2, so the VECTOR SECTOR IS IMPOSSIBLE ON THE RING. The ring's adjacency spectrum pairs k with 96-k (the 47 doublets) and is purely scalar: 45 distinct eigenvalues. " +
            "(2) THE SAME MISSING SUBSTRATE BLOCKS THE GRAVITON. M_011 found no vector sector on a single ring; M_012 found a genuine dimension-3 sector T1(3) with (chi, chi) = 1 on the cubic network C96 box C96 box C96. AND the graviton's traceless part is l = 2 -> E(2) + T2(3), a dimension-3 irrep for the SAME reason. G_033: the metric era NEVER INSTANTIATES 96^3, because it imports 3D space through the primitive ETA, which G_032 proved is an ASSUMED INPUT. The photon inherits exactly gravity's gap - and ONE construction would unblock both, which is the most useful result here. " +
            "(3) U(1) IS DERIVED AND COMPACT - BUT GLOBAL. U(1) = Z_96 = the rotation subgroup of Aut(C96(1..6)): no axiom needed, and because Z_96 is FINITE the emergent U(1) is COMPACT - the property that lets a compact U(1) with a conserved current carry a massless vector WITHOUT a Goldstone boson. But the symmetry is RIGID: the rotation IS an adjacency automorphism while 0 OF 6 site-local transpositions are. " +
            "(4) FALSIFIED: 'THE 12 LINK-DIRECTIONS ARE THE 12 GAUGE GENERATORS' (QG161, matching 1 + 3 + 8 = 12). The offsets {+-1..+-6} are NOT closed under addition - witness 1 + 95 = 0, outside the set - their additive closure inside Z_96 is 96 NOT 12, and the algebra is ABELIAN, against u(1)+su(2)+su(3) which is 11-DIMENSIONAL NON-ABELIAN. A cardinality match with no algebraic map. BUT the su(2)-from-doublets claim PASSES: the Lie closure of the doublet generators has dimension 3, so the WEAK sector has a real basis while '12 = 12' does not. " +
            "(5) A CORRECTION THAT MATTERS: AT ALREADY HAS A LINK PHASE. PhaseOrigin assigns 2*pi/96 per ring link, with a path phase over a full cycle of exactly 2*pi, a COMPACT loop holonomy, a two-slit law 2 + 2 cos(delta) (4.000 at delta = 0, 0.000 at pi) and a phased Born rule. So the missing primitive is NOT THE PHASE - it is the SPACETIME INDEX (these are 1-D ring links, not 4-D) and the DYNAMICS (the step is the fixed constant 2*pi/N, not a fluctuating field). " +
            "(6) AT'S MASSLESS CONTENT, AND ITS SPIN. The Laplacian mu_k = 2k - lambda_k has EXACTLY ONE zero eigenvalue - the constant mode, SPIN 0 - with gap 0.386351. The computed massless waves are BOTH SCALARS (the zero mode and the TemporalField scalar wave equation); the spin-2 Box psi_mu_nu = 0 is POSTULATED (Derived() = false, Postulated() = true), which CORRECTS E_001/E_002; SPIN-1 IS ABSENT. " +
            "(7) THE POLARISATION COUNT PINS THE GAP. A massless spin-1 has exactly TWO transverse polarisations: a scalar phase gives 1 (longitudinal), grad(rho) gives 1, a gauge-reduced A_mu gives 2, Proca gives 3. The cheap AT-native routes are excluded by COUNTING. " +
            "(8) THREE SELF-CORRECTIONS, ALL CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT'S OWN TESTS AND RECORDED RATHER THAN ABSORBED: (i) the site-dependent family p[i] = i + 1 + (a*i) mod 5 DEGENERATES to the rigid rotation at a = 5, reporting one phase that 'worked'; (ii) the degeneracy bound is ONE-SIDED - k <-> 96-k makes 49 an UPPER bound and the measured count is 45; (iii) AT DOES already have a link phase, found by reconnaissance. " +
            "THE NATIVE ROUTE, IF TAKEN: instantiate the cubic substrate instead of importing 3D space as eta (the SAME step gravity needs); promote the rigid rotation to a local one (an independent phase per link - genuinely new structure, since a site-dependent phase is not an automorphism); verify the longitudinal mode is removed (a compact U(1) with a conserved current can do this without a Goldstone, making AT's finite Z_96 an ADVANTAGE); and the Maxwell limit is then E_002's derivation, needing no new work. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from ten independent checks, never a literal (the G_027 discipline). No reclassification; E_001/E_002/M_011/M_012/G_032/G_033 are unchanged inputs; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; NO NEW PRIMITIVE IS ADDED - the audit identifies the ONE the theory would need. 7/7 PASSED, group E 20/20. VERDICTS: DERIVED (the obstruction, the dihedral relations, the compactness, the polarisation count, the link phase) / BOUNDARY (the vector sector, available only on an unbuilt substrate) / FALSIFIED (the 12-generator claim; three self-inflicted method errors) / ABSENT (the spin-1 massless mode).",
            Formula: "SpinLadder: l = 1 -> T1(3) (photon), l = 2 -> E(2)+T2(3) (graviton); D_96 irrep budget 4*1 + 47*4 = 192, max dim 2; U(1) = Z_96 = <r> subset Aut(C96(1..6)); link phase 2*pi/96; mu_k = 2k - lambda_k, one zero mode, gap 0.386351",
            CalculationId: "photon-ontology-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_003", "ResearchY-E_002", "ResearchY-E_001", "ResearchY-M_011", "ResearchY-M_012", "ResearchY-G_032", "ResearchY-G_033"],
            AuditIds: ["e003"]),

        new("vector-sector-audit", "Vector Sector Audit", "Can the D96^3 T1(3) sector support a genuine spin-1 field? BOUNDARY: the sector is a real vector sector but not yet a gauge field. l = 1 subducts to a single IRREDUCIBLE T1 of dimension 3 (the single ring's max irrep dimension is 2, so it has no vector sector at all), and a Lorentz 4-vector needs BOTH substrates (A1(1) + T1(3) = 4), so neither alone can carry one. The decisive computation is that two quadratic forms live on the SAME three-dimensional space: the identity form (rank 3, kernel 0 -> three states, a PROCA field, and it is the representation's natural invariant) and the curl form (rank 2, kernel 1 -> two states), the curl form annihilating the longitudinal mode exactly. An irreducible representation has no gauge orbit, so T1(3) alone yields a massive vector. Masslessness holds only in the continuum limit: the gap is 0.386351 at N = 96 but scales as 3591/n^2, a finite-size artefact. What is missing is the CHOICE OF KINETIC FORM that takes three states to two.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["photon-ontology-audit", "field-equation-derivation-audit", "literal-verdict-audit"],
            Narrative: "Can the D96^3 T1(3) sector support a genuine spin-1 FIELD? E_003 located the obstruction in representation theory; E_004 shows how far the representation takes you and where it stops. Requirements: vector degrees of freedom, two physical polarisations, gauge redundancy, massless propagation, Maxwell limit. ANSWER: BOUNDARY - the T1(3) sector is a real vector sector, and it is not yet a gauge field. " +
            "(1) REQUIREMENT 1 MET, ON D96^3 ONLY. l = 1 subducts onto the octahedral group as a SINGLE multiplet T1, dimension 3, multiplicity 1 - hence IRREDUCIBLE. The single ring's maximum irrep dimension is 2, so it has NO vector sector at all. " +
            "(2) A LORENTZ 4-VECTOR NEEDS BOTH SUBSTRATES - SHARPER THAN E_003. A_mu = (A_0, A_i) reduces as A1(1) + T1(3) = 4. The single ring supplies only the timelike A_0; the cubic substrate only the spatial A_i. NEITHER SUBSTRATE ALONE CAN CARRY A LORENTZ VECTOR. " +
            "(3) REQUIREMENT 2 MET GIVEN A REASON TO PROJECT. The transverse projector P = I - k k^T has rank 2 for every one of 12 momentum directions tested, so 3 components -> 2 physical states with 1 removed - IF there is a reason to remove it. " +
            "(4) REQUIREMENT 3 NOT MET - AND THIS IS THE DECISIVE COMPUTATION. Two quadratic forms live on the SAME three-dimensional space. The IDENTITY form V.V has rank 3 and kernel 0 -> THREE physical states, a PROCA field - and it is the representation's own NATURAL INVARIANT. The CURL form F_ij F_ij has matrix 2(I - k k^T), rank 2 and kernel 1 -> TWO states. Evaluated on the modes, the curl form ANNIHILATES the longitudinal mode EXACTLY (0.000e0, against 1.000000 for the identity). An irreducible representation has NO GAUGE ORBIT - gauge directions: 0 FROM THE REPRESENTATION, 1 FROM THE FIELD SPACE (the curl form's gradient kernel). So T1(3) ALONE DELIVERS A MASSIVE VECTOR. " +
            "(5) REQUIREMENT 4 MET IN THE LIMIT, NOT ON ANY LATTICE. The sector is gapped: 0.386351 at N = 96. But mu_min * n^2 settles to ~3591 (12.0 -> 0.02435 as n goes 12 -> 384; spread 0.84 % for n >= 96), so mu_min ~ 3591/n^2 -> 0. THE GAP IS A FINITE-SIZE ARTEFACT, NOT A PREDICTED MASS. The cubic gap is 3x the ring's by the Cartesian-product sum rule. " +
            "(6) REQUIREMENT 5 IMPORTED - E_002's derivation, from premises that are not AT's. " +
            "(7) WHAT IS MISSING IS NOW LOCATED EXACTLY: THE CHOICE OF KINETIC FORM THAT TAKES THREE STATES TO TWO. Not the phase (E_003 found AT already has one), not the group, and not the vector representation. D96^3 is NECESSARY AND SUFFICIENT AT THE LEVEL OF REPRESENTATION and INSUFFICIENT AT THE LEVEL OF DYNAMICS. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from nine independent checks, never a literal (the G_027 discipline). No reclassification; E_001/E_002/E_003/M_011/M_012/G_032/G_033 are unchanged inputs; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; NO NEW PRIMITIVE IS ADDED - the audit LOCATES the one the theory would need. 6/6 PASSED, group E 26/26. VERDICTS: DERIVED (T1(3) irreducible; the Lorentz split; the 1/n^2 gap law) / BOUNDARY (requirements 2 and 4, which hold only given a projection and only in the limit) / FALSIFIED (the identity form's three states - a massive vector) / POSTULATED (the gauge orbit, which no representation supplies).",
            Formula: "l = 1 -> T1(3), multiplicity 1; A_mu -> A1(1) + T1(3) = 4; rank(I) = 3 vs rank(2(I - k k^T)) = 2; curl form on a gradient = 0 exactly; mu_min ~ 3591/n^2",
            CalculationId: "vector-sector-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_004", "ResearchY-E_003", "ResearchY-E_002", "ResearchY-M_012", "ResearchY-G_033"],
            AuditIds: ["e004"]),

        new("propagation-origin-audit", "Propagation Origin Audit", "What is the minimal missing ingredient that turns T1(3) into a propagating photon sector and T2(3) into a propagating graviton sector? BOUNDARY: the first failing layer is KINEMATICS and the bottleneck is ONE object - a first-order derivative carrying a DIRECTION INDEX. Representation is satisfied and is the only layer that is; dynamics and gauge are missing but BLOCKED rather than absent, which refines E_004 to the second step.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["vector-sector-audit", "photon-ontology-audit", "field-equation-derivation-audit", "electromagnetism-inventory-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - THE FIRST FAILING LAYER IS KINEMATICS, AND THE BOTTLENECK IS ONE OBJECT: A FIRST-ORDER DERIVATIVE CARRYING A DIRECTION INDEX. Question: what is the minimal missing ingredient that turns T1(3) into a propagating photon sector and T2(3) into a propagating graviton sector? The four layers the question names are run IN ORDER and each is marked from a computation. " +
            "(1) THE REPRESENTATION LAYER IS SATISFIED, and it is the only one that is: T1 is 3 states with multiplicity 1 and the traceless rank-2 is E + T2 = 2 + 3 = 5, while the single ring tops out at 2 and can host neither. " +
            "(2) LOCALISATION ONE - THE INDEX SPACES COLLAPSE. A field strength needs two antisymmetrised indices and the graviton's field is a traceless symmetric rank-2: at a direction rank of 1 the antisymmetric square is EXACTLY 0 and the traceless symmetric is EXACTLY 0. Directions 1/2/3 give vector 1/2/3, antisymmetric 0/1/3 and traceless symmetric 0/2/5, so neither sector has anywhere to put a field strength and the sectors as they stand (3 and 5) need exactly three directions. " +
            "(3) LOCALISATION TWO - THE SUBSTRATE'S DERIVATIVE IS ONE-DIRECTIONAL. AT's radius-6 Laplacian IS a sum of six squares of first-order differences (verified through the first row of the circulant, residual 0.000E+000), so first-order operators exist - but all six strides lie along a single line: direction rank 1 against the 3 a vector index needs. Loop structure agrees: the ring has 481 independent loops, the cube would have 1 769 473 of which 2 654 208 are elementary plaquettes, so only the cube can carry a LOCAL field strength rather than a single global number. " +
            "(4) LOCALISATION THREE, AND SHARPEST - THE BUILT-IN CONNECTION IS EXACTLY PURE GAUGE. The built-in step is 2*pi/96 = 0.065449847, the holonomy around the ring is 6.283185 = 2*pi = the identity, and conjugating the covariant difference by the site-dependent phase returns the ordinary difference to within 2.45E-016 - periodic precisely BECAUSE the holonomy is one whole turn. The phase is removable, its field strength is identically zero, and the only gauge-invariant content a phase on a closed line could have is exactly the residue that vanishes. There is nothing in it to propagate. " +
            "(5) DYNAMICS AND GAUGE ARE MISSING BUT BLOCKED, not independently absent: a kinetic form is a functional of a field strength and a gauge orbit is the image of the derivative. That REFINES E_004, whose missing choice of kinetic form is the second step, and CONFIRMS E_003, whose spacetime index IS the direction index. " +
            "(6) THE BOTTLENECK IS UNIQUE, AND TWO RIVALS ARE REFUTED. The representation is refuted because it is complete. The exterior complex is refuted because the graviton is not a form at all: the photon's field strength lives in the antisymmetric square (dim 3) while the graviton's field is a traceless symmetric rank-2 (dim 5). What serves both is one first-order derivative carrying the direction index, and the shared count proves the sharing: 2 for the photon (3 - 1) and 2 for the graviton (5 - 3). " +
            "(7) THREE ERRORS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT ITSELF AND RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: the remainder operator is not a holonomy reduction (96 x 2*pi/96 can land below 2*pi and a remainder then returns a whole turn - replaced by counting turns); a REAL exponential was used where a COMPLEX phase was needed (residual 534 before the fix, 2.45E-016 after); and the shared PhotonOntologyAudit.RankOf indexes eight columns unconditionally so it cannot take a one-component direction vector, so ranking is done locally and the observation recorded. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the layer ladder and its ordering, the index-space collapse, the operator identity, the pure-gauge conjugation and holonomy, the shared count and the two refutations). No reclassification: E_001-E_004 all remain BOUNDARY. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PropagationOriginAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 33/33.",
            Formula: "layer ladder: representation SATISFIED (T1 = 3 x 1, E + T2 = 2 + 3 = 5), kinematics FIRST MISSING, dynamics and gauge BLOCKED; index spaces (directions 1/2/3) vector 1/2/3, antisym 0/1/3, traceless sym 0/2/5; L = sum_{r=1..6} D_r^T D_r (residual 0.000E+000); direction rank ring 1, cube 3, needed 3; loops ring 481, cube 1 769 473, plaquettes 2 654 208; built-in step 2*pi/96, holonomy 6.283185 = 2*pi, gauge conjugation residual 2.45E-016; shared count 3 - 1 = 2 and 5 - 3 = 2",
            CalculationId: "propagation-origin-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_005", "ResearchY-E_004", "ResearchY-E_003", "ResearchY-E_002", "ResearchY-E_001", "ResearchY-G_033", "ResearchY-G_042"],
            AuditIds: ["e005"]),
        new("connection-origin-audit", "Connection Origin Audit", "What AT structure could supply the missing direction index that E_005 located? DERIVED: the unique missing object between representation and field theory is the D96^3 EDGE CONNECTION, and it needs NO NEW PRIMITIVE. Of five candidates four are refuted on measured witnesses (ring derivative rank 1; occupancy gradients with an identically vanishing antisymmetric part; a flow that is a report, not a field; causal-order links that are not local); the edge connection passes all five, and one derivative acting on the vector sector reproduces both the photon's field strength and the graviton's sector.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["propagation-origin-audit", "vector-sector-audit", "photon-ontology-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE UNIQUE MISSING OBJECT BETWEEN REPRESENTATION AND FIELD THEORY IS THE D96^3 EDGE CONNECTION, AND IT NEEDS NO NEW PRIMITIVE. Question: what AT structure could supply the missing direction index E_005 located, subject to being local, directional, first-order, acting on T1 and T2, and requiring no new primitive? Five candidates are run against those five requirements with a computation behind every mark. " +
            "(1) FOUR ARE REFUTED. THE RING DERIVATIVE is local and genuinely first-order (its square IS the radius-6 Laplacian) but its direction rank is 1 against the 3 needed and the largest ring irrep is 2, so there is no vector sector. OCCUPANCY GRADIENTS fail for a sharper reason than rank: their domain is scalars, and on a uniform lattice a double gradient has an identically vanishing antisymmetric part (measured 1.11E-016) against a traceless part of 0.879, so a scalar-derived connection can never carry a field strength - the same mechanism that made E_005's built-in phase exactly pure gauge. ACTUALIZATION FLOW fails twice: AT's flow objects are report models and metrics rather than fields (a live scan finds 0 members returning a flow field) and a flow is one vector per site, not an index. CAUSAL-ORDER LINKS fail three requirements: the closure of the ring's own links reaches 95 of its 96 cells against a direct-link support of 2, it carries no index, and it has no dispersion relation. " +
            "(2) THE ONE THAT DERIVES, AND ITS FIVE MARKS. LOCAL: support 2 per row. DIRECTIONAL: rank 3, the three factor differences independent. FIRST-ORDER: the summed squared symbols equal the cube Laplacian's own symbol to 8.88E-016, and |sigma(k)|/k = 0.999583, 0.999996, 1.000000 while |sigma(k)|/k^2 = 9.996, 100.0, 1000.0 at k = 1e-1, 1e-2, 1e-3 - linear, not quadratic. " +
            "(3) ACTS ON T1 AND T2 - THE DECISIVE LINE, COMPUTED FROM THE OCTAHEDRAL CHARACTERS. The tensor square of the vector irrep is separated with (chi(g)^2 - chi(g^2))/2 for the antisymmetric part and (chi(g)^2 + chi(g^2))/2 for the symmetric part: ANTISYMMETRIC = T1 (multiplicity 1, dimension 3 - the photon's field strength, in the vector irrep itself, which is G_042's Hodge identity at d = 3) and SYMMETRIC = A1 + E + T2 (multiplicities 1, 1, 1; dimensions 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 - the trace plus the GRAVITON'S SECTOR). And 3 + 6 = 9 = 3 x 3. ONE DERIVATIVE ACTING ON THE VECTOR SECTOR REPRODUCES BOTH SECTORS. " +
            "(4) NO NEW PRIMITIVE: it is the tensor product of the ring's own difference operators, three times over, an operation AT already uses, and the cube's symmetry group and irrep spectrum are already computed in the project. " +
            "(5) THE LAYERS. representation SATISFIED (already: T1 is 3 and the traceless rank-2 is 5); KINEMATICS DERIVED HERE; dynamics STILL MISSING (0 members compute a field strength or its divergence, E_002); gauge STILL MISSING (the orbit is the image of the derivative, so it needs the field). " +
            "(6) THE BOUNDARY INSIDE THE VERDICT. A live scan of AT's sources (code only, comments and string literals stripped per line) finds 0 product-lattice constructions - not Kronecker, not TensorProduct, not ProductLattice, not CubeLattice - so the object is DERIVABLE BUT NOT INSTANTIATED, which is G_033's finding about the substrate reached from the code side; and 0 members compute a field strength, so nothing couples it. Derived, not built, and not coupled. " +
            "(7) FOUR ERRORS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT ITSELF AND RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. The product-lattice scan counted its own token list (rule 11), fixed by excluding the audit's own file. A helper named MembersThatComputeAFieldStrength matched E_002's own signature regex, so the coupling count read 1 instead of 0 - rule 11 again, in a place nobody would look; the helper is renamed and the incident is in the code comment. An over-claim that a gradient can never reach the symmetric traceless sector is FALSE - a Hessian's traceless part is 0.879 - and was replaced by the antisymmetric statement the measurement supports. And a linearity threshold of 10 sat just above the k = 0.1 sample's 9.996; the criterion now also requires the ratio to grow. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the candidate matrix and its measured witnesses, the operator identity and symbol linearity, the tensor-square character decomposition, the instantiation scan, and the layer states). REFINES E_005 - the ingredient need not be invented, only built and coupled - and RECLASSIFIES NOTHING (E_001-E_005 all keep their verdicts). No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/ConnectionOriginAudit.cs. 8/8 PASSED; group E 41/41.",
            Formula: "candidate matrix: {ring derivative, edge connection, occupancy gradients, flow, causal links} x {local, directional, first-order, acts on T1/T2, no new primitive}; edge connection: support 2 per row, direction rank 3, symbol identity 8.88E-016, |sigma(k)|/k -> 1, |sigma(k)|/k^2 -> infinity; tensor square of T1: antisymmetric = T1 (dim 3), symmetric = A1 + E + T2 (dims 1 + 2 + 3 = 6), 3 + 6 = 9; causal closure 95 of 96 cells against a direct support of 2; double gradient of a scalar: antisymmetric 1.11E-016, traceless 0.879; instantiation scan 0",
            CalculationId: "connection-origin-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_006", "ResearchY-E_005", "ResearchY-E_004", "ResearchY-E_002", "ResearchY-G_033", "ResearchY-G_042"],
            AuditIds: ["e006"]),
        new("field-strength-origin-audit", "Field Strength Origin Audit", "Can the D96^3 edge connection produce a non-zero field strength? BOUNDARY: the connection alone produces NOTHING - it is a product of lattice differences, and differences commute, so its curvature vanishes exactly and its link content is a gauge gradient that telescopes to zero - while the cube is the FIRST substrate on which a field strength can exist at all (the ring has zero elementary plaquettes, the cube 2 654 208). The first non-trivial quantity is the quantised plaquette flux F = 2 pi n / L, smallest non-zero value 2 pi / 96 = 0.065449847, exactly AT's phase quantum; the curvature is exactly the antisymmetrised difference, gauge invariant, and Bianchi-consistent. This audit also corrects E_005's plaquette count by a factor of L.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["connection-origin-audit", "propagation-origin-audit", "field-equation-derivation-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - BOTH HALVES OF THE ANSWER ARE EXACT: THE CONNECTION ALONE PRODUCES NOTHING, AND THE CUBE IS THE FIRST SUBSTRATE ON WHICH ANYTHING CAN EXIST AT ALL. Question: can the D96^3 edge connection that E_006 derived produce a non-zero field strength? Construct closed plaquette loops, a discrete curvature and a discrete curl; measure F != 0; compare a pure gauge configuration against a non-trivial loop. " +
            "(1) WHAT THE CONNECTION DOES BY ITSELF - NOTHING, EXACTLY. E_006's edge connection is a product of lattice differences, and differences commute on a uniform lattice: the commutator vanishes, measured at 1.73E-018 with an exhaustive scan at small size and a sampled scan of the full torus. The same fact in link language is that the connection's own content is a gradient, and a gradient link field has an exactly vanishing plaquette holonomy - 6.94E-017 - because the four contributions to the closed loop telescope. The edge connection is FLAT. " +
            "(2) WHY THAT IS ONLY HALF THE ANSWER, AND THE CENSUS THAT SETTLES IT. A field strength is the holonomy of a CLOSED TWO-DIMENSIONAL loop, so the question is really whether the substrate can carry a curvature at all. The ring has ZERO elementary plaquettes - it is one-dimensional whatever its link count, which is E_005's vanishing antisymmetric square stated concretely - so F has nowhere to live on it. The cube has one elementary plaquette per site AND per orientation pair: 3L^3 = 2 654 208 at L = 96, inside an independent cycle space of E - V + 1 = 1 769 473. " +
            "(3) THE FIRST NON-TRIVIAL FIELD QUANTITY IS THE QUANTISED PLAQUETTE FLUX. A link field linear in the transverse coordinate, A_1 = f y, carries the same curvature -f on every (1,2) plaquette; the requirement that the link be a phase on a closed torus forces f L to be a whole turn, so f = 2 pi n / L and the smallest non-zero field strength the substrate can carry is 2 pi / 96 = 0.065449847. That is EXACTLY the phase quantum AT already has - the number E_005 found to be pure gauge on the ring is, on the cube, the minimal real field strength. " +
            "(4) THE APPARATUS IS EXACT RATHER THAN APPROXIMATE. For an Abelian connection the four link phases of a closed loop simply add, so the discrete curvature IS the antisymmetrised difference: the curl and the holonomy agree with residual 0.00E+000. The curvature is gauge invariant under a site-dependent gauge transformation, 1.11E-015. The discrete BIANCHI identity holds exactly, because the twelve link contributions to the six faces of an elementary cube cancel in pairs: 0.00E+000 on the flux field and 8.33E-017 on pure gauge. And the minimal flux field is periodic on the torus, 2.45E-016, which is the origin of the quantisation. " +
            "(5) CORRECTION TO E_005. That audit reported 3L^2 = 27 648 elementary plaquettes while its own cycle count already used the correct 3L^3 edges, so its two numbers disagreed by a factor of L. Recounted independently here and corrected to 2 654 208 in the code, in the test and in eight texts. E_005's verdict and all of its other numbers are unchanged, and the corrected value strengthens its point since the cube's plaquette supply is a thousand times the ring's supply of zero. " +
            "(6) THE VERDICT IS BOUNDARY FOR A SPECIFIC REASON. Everything that DETECTS a field strength is derived here - the plaquette, the curvature, the curl, the quantisation, gauge invariance and Bianchi - and the first non-trivial quantity is exhibited with its value. But the CONNECTION DOES NOT PRODUCE IT: it takes a chosen fluctuation, and nothing in AT yet selects one. That is the dynamics layer E_005 located and E_006 left open. Layers: kinematics DERIVED (E_006) but flat on its own; field-strength detection DERIVED HERE; dynamics STILL MISSING. " +
            "(7) TWO SYNTAX ERRORS in the first draft of this audit's own core were caught by the compiler and are recorded rather than hidden. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the commutator and pure-gauge residues, the cycle census, the quantisation and periodicity of the minimal flux, the curl-versus-holonomy identity, gauge invariance and the two Bianchi checks). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING OF ITS OWN, but CORRECTS ONE NUMBER in E_005 without changing that audit's verdict. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FieldStrengthOriginAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 48/48.",
            Formula: "ring elementary plaquettes = 0; cube elementary plaquettes = 3L^3 = 2 654 208; independent cycles = 3L^3 - L^3 + 1 = 1 769 473; commutator of differences = 1.73E-018; pure gauge field strength = 6.94E-017; curvature = antisymmetrised difference (residual 0.00E+000); minimal non-zero flux F = 2 pi n / L = 2 pi / 96 = 0.065449847; gauge invariance residual 1.11E-015; Bianchi residual 0.00E+000 (flux) and 8.33E-017 (pure gauge); periodicity residual 2.45E-016",
            CalculationId: "field-strength-origin-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_007", "ResearchY-E_006", "ResearchY-E_005", "ResearchY-E_002", "ResearchY-G_042"],
            AuditIds: ["e007"]),
        new("field-excitation-audit", "Field Excitation Audit", "What AT mechanism produces a non-zero field strength F? DERIVED - a dichotomy exact on both sides: every gradient is exactly pure gauge, and F != 0 requires a NON-DIFFERENCE coupling. A link phase written as the difference of any single-valued scalar telescopes to zero around every plaquette (2.50E-016 worst across four coupling functions on a non-separable organisation), settling occupancy, actualization and deficit gradients at once; the moment the coupling is not a difference F stops vanishing (0.626 / 0.778 / 1.126 for nonlinear couplings, 1.063 for a purely site-local one, with the verified closed form F = h(rho(x+mu)) - h(rho(x+nu))). The winding-phase defect candidate collapses into the same answer because it is pure gauge.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["field-strength-origin-audit", "connection-origin-audit", "propagation-origin-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - A DICHOTOMY THAT IS EXACT ON BOTH SIDES: EVERY GRADIENT IS EXACTLY PURE GAUGE, AND F != 0 REQUIRES A NON-DIFFERENCE COUPLING. Question: what AT mechanism produces a non-zero field strength F, subject to being local, gauge-compatible, acting on T1 and T2, and requiring no new primitive? Candidates: occupancy gradients, actualization gradients, deficit gradients, non-uniform rho, topological defects. " +
            "(1) THE NEGATIVE SIDE IS A THEOREM. A link phase written as the DIFFERENCE of any single-valued scalar has an exactly vanishing holonomy around every closed plaquette, because the four contributions telescope. H(rho) is still a single-valued scalar, so EVERY gradient of EVERY function of EVERY organisation is exactly pure gauge. Measured on a deliberately NON-SEPARABLE organisation for H = rho, rho^2, exp(rho) and sin(rho), the worst residual is 2.50E-016. That settles three of the five candidates at once: occupancy gradients, actualization gradients and deficit gradients cannot produce a field strength, ever, for any coupling function. " +
            "(2) THE POSITIVE SIDE IS EQUALLY EXACT. h(rho) times Delta rho with h constant gives 2.22E-016, because that IS the gradient; h = rho, h = rho^2 and h = exp(rho) give 0.626, 0.778 and 1.126; and a purely SITE-LOCAL coupling h(rho(x)) gives 1.063 (rho^2: 1.595; a directional variant mu*h(rho(x)): 2.583), with a CLOSED FORM verified against the plaquette sum at residual 3.33E-016: F_mu_nu = h(rho(x+mu)) - h(rho(x+nu)). So NON-UNIFORM RHO is the surviving candidate - and it survives precisely because it is read LOCALLY rather than through its gradient. " +
            "(3) THE TOPOLOGICAL-DEFECT CANDIDATE COLLAPSES INTO THE SAME ANSWER. The natural winding-phase construction is PURE GAUGE: U_mu = exp(i Delta_mu theta) IS g(x)^-1 g(x+mu) by construction, so every plaquette equals one - measured over ALL of them, the branch cut included, at 6.11E-016. The wrapped variant does light up 16 plaquettes, but every value is a WHOLE TURN, and a whole turn is the identity: the largest is 6.283185 against a full turn of 6.283185, and the signed total is 0. A genuine defect therefore needs an INDEPENDENTLY ASSIGNED link configuration, which is exactly the non-difference structure already found - ONE mechanism, not two. " +
            "(4) ALL FOUR REQUIREMENTS HOLD FOR THE SURVIVOR. LOCAL: support 2, a single site or one link. GAUGE-COMPATIBLE: a site-dependent gauge transformation moves F by 5.55E-016. ACTS ON T1 AND T2: F lives in the antisymmetric square, which at d = 3 IS the vector irrep, while the symmetric square is A1 + E + T2, so one source feeds both sectors. NO NEW PRIMITIVE, measured against AT's own code rather than asserted: the organisation has 30 computed members, the link phase 5, and the winding 1 - AT literally computes a winding number, as InternalStateAnalyzer.ComputeWindingNumber in the oscillator line - with the plaquette apparatus coming from E_007. " +
            "(5) WHAT REMAINS OPEN IS STATED PLAINLY. The audit locates the CLASS of mechanism and excludes its rivals exactly; it does not derive WHICH coupling, nor what makes the organisation non-uniform in the first place. That selection is the dynamics layer E_005 located and E_006 and E_007 left open. " +
            "(6) TWO ERRORS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT'S OWN TESTS AND RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. A SEPARABLE test field made the product form look like F = 0, because a separable organisation cancels that curvature identically - the reading was roundoff and it nearly became a false theorem; re-probing with a NON-SEPARABLE organisation gave 0.626, and the core now uses one while the test asserts the product form lights up. And a requirement line built with .Replace placeholders left one unsubstituted, so the report printed its own source text; caught by the test. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the gradient residuals across four coupling functions, the F = 0 versus F != 0 table, the closed form against the plaquette sum, the pure-gauge vortex and its whole-turn wrapped variant, and the four requirement checks). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_005-E_007 keep their verdicts, and this audit supplies the source E_007 said had to be chosen. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FieldExcitationAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 55/55.",
            Formula: "gradient couplings Delta_mu H(rho): max |F| = 2.22E-016, 2.50E-016, 2.22E-016, 2.22E-016 (H = rho, rho^2, exp, sin) -> F = 0; product h(rho)Delta rho: h = 1 -> 2.22E-016, h = rho -> 0.626, h = rho^2 -> 0.778, h = exp -> 1.126; site-local h(rho(x)): h = rho -> 1.063, rho^2 -> 1.595; directional mu*h(rho(x)) -> 2.583; closed form F_mu_nu = h(rho(x+mu)) - h(rho(x+nu)) verified at 3.33E-016; phase-gradient vortex at 6.11E-016; wrapped vortex 16 plaquettes, largest 6.283185 (one whole turn), signed total 0; gauge invariance 5.55E-016; mechanism inventory: organisation 30, phase 5, winding 1",
            CalculationId: "field-excitation-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_008", "ResearchY-E_007", "ResearchY-E_006", "ResearchY-E_005", "ResearchY-E_003"],
            AuditIds: ["e008"]),
        new("coupling-function-audit", "Coupling Function Audit", "What determines h(rho)? DERIVED - h is not free: AT already computes it. AT's own clock law, GpsCorrectionOrigin.ClockRate(d, rho) = rho^(1/d) (G_016b, d tau/dt = rho^(1/d)), supplies the function, ClockExponent(d) = 1/d the exponent and AT's phase quantum 2 pi / 96 the unit, so h(rho) = (2 pi / 96) rho^(1/d) has ZERO free parameters. The constant is refuted (F = 0, because it IS the gradient E_008 excluded); rho, rho^2 and exp(rho) work but each carries one free parameter; the 'actualization law' candidate is the same law under another name. Sweeping the exponent, exactly one value gives zero - the constant - so the requirement does not select the exponent; the clock law does. The derived field strength is purely electric and gauge invariant, and the magnetic half remains an input.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["field-excitation-audit", "field-strength-origin-audit", "photon-ontology-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - H IS NOT FREE, AND AT ALREADY COMPUTES IT: h(rho) = (2 pi / 96) rho^(1/d), WITH ZERO FREE PARAMETERS. Question: what determines h(rho), the coupling function E_008 showed must be a non-difference? Candidates: a constant, rho, rho^2, exp(rho), a derived occupancy law, an actualization law; requirements: produces non-zero F, compatible with T1 and T2, no new primitive; measured: field strength, gauge structure, minimality. " +
            "(1) THE COUPLING IS AT'S OWN CLOCK LAW. AT computes the proper-time rate of a clock as GpsCorrectionOrigin.ClockRate(d, rho) = rho^(1/d) - G_016b's clock law, d tau/dt = rho^(1/d) - whose exponent is fixed by the substrate dimension through SubstrateDimensionAudit.ClockExponent(d) = 1/d, and whose unit is AT's phase quantum 2 pi / 96 (E_003). Read as a link phase that IS the coupling function of E_008. A live scan finds 5 AT members computing a clock rate, exponent or law, so the law is the theory's own rather than the audit's. " +
            "(2) THE CANDIDATES, MEASURED. The constant is REFUTED: max |F| = 0.000E+000, because a constant times a difference is still a difference, which E_008 proved invisible. rho, rho^2 and exp(rho) work - 0.751, 2.216 and 3.362 - but each carries ONE free parameter, since its ansatz had to be supplied. The derived occupancy law carries ZERO and produces 1.793E-002. The actualization law is the SAME law under a second name: a degeneracy, verified by comparing the two candidate functions and by the absence of any AT member named for an actualization law. " +
            "(3) THE HONEST NEGATIVE, WHICH IS THE AUDIT'S ANSWER TO DERIVING RATHER THAN CHOOSING. Sweeping h = rho^p over seven exponents, the field strength vanishes at EXACTLY ONE, p = 0, because a constant coupling IS the gradient; every other exponent works: 1/6 gives 0.145, 1/3 gives 0.274, 1/2 gives 0.390, 1 gives 0.751, 2 gives 2.216 and 3 gives 5.062. So the requirement 'produces non-zero F' rules the constant OUT and leaves everything else INDISTINGUISHABLE. The exponent is not selected by the requirement; it is selected by the CLOCK LAW. " +
            "(4) MINIMALITY IS COUNTABLE AND DECIDES IT. Every other candidate carries a free parameter - the constant its value, and the power and exponential candidates their ansatz - while the clock-law candidate carries none. The minimum over the candidates is 0, attained by exactly two of them, and those two are one law. " +
            "(5) THE GAUGE STRUCTURE AND THE BOUNDARY. With A_0 taken from the clock law and no spatial phase, the field strength is PURELY ELECTRIC: max |F_0i| = 1.424E-002 against max |F_ij| = 0.000E+000, which is zero identically. The electric field is exactly minus the gradient of the clock rate, verified against the closed form at 0.000E+000; it is invariant under a site-dependent gauge transformation (1.11E-016); and it satisfies the discrete Bianchi identity automatically (0.00E+000). The clock law fixes the TIME-LIKE component of the coupling and says nothing whatever about the spatial ones, so the MAGNETIC half of the field strength is still an input. " +
            "(6) TWO ERRORS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT'S OWN TESTS. Taking rho^(1/3) of E_008's organisation gave NaN, because that organisation is a generic scalar that goes negative and a one-third power requires a non-negative argument: the DOMAIN is a real constraint on the coupling, satisfied automatically by a density, and now measured (MinimumOccupancy) rather than assumed. E_008's own results are unaffected, since its couplings were polynomials and exponentials defined on both signs. And the first version of the 'not a difference' check compared the derived LOCAL coupling against another LOCAL coupling and expected zero - a conceptual error, because a local function of rho is never a difference whatever function it is; the comparison now runs against E_008's DIFFERENCE form. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the clock law's exponent and unit, the candidate table with its free-parameter counts, the exponent sweep, the minimality count, the purely electric split, the closed form, gauge invariance and Bianchi). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_005-E_008 keep their verdicts, and this audit derives the coupling E_008 had to choose. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/CouplingFunctionAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 62/62.",
            Formula: "h(rho) = (2 pi / 96) * rho^(1/d), d = 3: 0.065449847 * rho^(1/3), zero free parameters; constant: max |F| = 0.000E+000 (refuted); rho: 0.751; rho^2: 2.216; exp(rho): 3.362 (each 1 free parameter); derived occupancy law: 1.793E-002 (0 free parameters); exponent sweep h = rho^p: 0 -> 0, 1/6 -> 0.145, 1/3 -> 0.274, 1/2 -> 0.390, 1 -> 0.751, 2 -> 2.216, 3 -> 5.062; purely electric: max |F_0i| = 1.424E-002, max |F_ij| = 0.000E+000; electric field closed form residual 0.000E+000; gauge invariance 1.11E-016; Bianchi 0.00E+000; AT members computing a clock law: 5",
            CalculationId: "coupling-function-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_008", "ResearchY-E_007", "ResearchY-E_003", "ResearchY-G_016"],
            AuditIds: ["e009"]),
        new("magnetic-sector-audit", "Magnetic Sector Audit", "What AT structure can generate a non-zero F_ij? REFUTED: magnetic components do NOT emerge from occupancy dynamics alone, and the measurement that decides it is a scaling one. E_009's purely-electric result was a choice, not a theorem - completing the coupling covariantly (A_mu = h(rho) Delta_mu rho, the only vector a scalar can build) switches the magnetic sector on at 1.422E-003 with the derived coupling and 0.000E+000 for the linear one, so the sector exists because the clock law is nonlinear - but refining the lattice at a fixed physical profile the covariant form falls as a^2.92 and the site-local form as a^0.99, so both vanish in the physical limit, which is the same standard E_004 applied to the spectral gap. What survives is an independently assigned uniform flux, which reads 0.785398 at every lattice size.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Refuted, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["coupling-function-audit", "field-excitation-audit", "field-strength-origin-audit", "vector-sector-audit"],
            Narrative: "REFUTED - MAGNETIC COMPONENTS DO NOT EMERGE FROM OCCUPANCY DYNAMICS ALONE, AND THE MEASUREMENT THAT DECIDES IT IS A SCALING ONE. Question: what AT structure can generate a non-zero F_ij, subject to being local, gauge-compatible, requiring no new primitive and acting on T1 and T2? " +
            "(1) E_009'S PURELY-ELECTRIC RESULT WAS A CHOICE, NOT A THEOREM. E_009 set the spatial components of the coupling to zero because the clock law says nothing about them, and said so. Completing the coupling COVARIANTLY - A_mu = h(rho) Delta_mu rho, which is the only vector a scalar can build - switches the magnetic components on: max |F_23| = 1.422E-003 at L = 8 with the derived coupling, against 0.000E+000 for the linear coupling, which is exactly the gradient E_008 excluded. The magnetic sector exists PRECISELY BECAUSE THE CLOCK LAW IS NONLINEAR; a linear coupling telescopes and leaves nothing. The same configuration also carries an electric part, 2.203E-003. " +
            "(2) BUT IT IS A FINITE-SIZE ARTEFACT, AND THAT IS DECIDED BY REFINING THE LATTICE AT A FIXED PHYSICAL PROFILE. The covariant form's magnetic field falls as a^2.92 - 1.42E-003, 2.06E-004, 2.61E-005 and 3.32E-006 at L = 8, 16, 32 and 64 - and the site-local form's falls as a^0.99 - 9.91E-003, 5.05E-003, 2.55E-003 and 1.27E-003. BOTH VANISH IN THE PHYSICAL LIMIT. This programme already set exactly this standard for masslessness in E_004, where the spectral gap was called an artefact because mu_min n^2 settles to a constant, and by it the occupancy-derived magnetic curvature is a DISCRETISATION FIELD: a real number on the substrate's own lattice and nothing at all as the substrate is refined. " +
            "(3) WHAT SURVIVES IS WHAT IS NOT A FUNCTION OF THE ORGANISATION. E_007's uniform flux, with the physical strength held fixed by taking the number of turns proportional to the lattice size, reads 0.785398 at EVERY size tested - L = 8, 16, 32 and 64 - because a link phase proportional to the coordinate is not built from the organisation in any sense. That field is local (support 2), gauge-compatible (residual 1.78E-015), Bianchi-consistent, needs no new primitive, and acts on T1 and T2 through E_006's tensor square - but it is INDEPENDENTLY ASSIGNED, which is exactly the non-gradient structure E_008 identified for the field strength in general. " +
            "(4) SO THE ANSWER IS NO. The occupancy supplies the electric half exactly - E_009 derived that half - while the magnetic half requires a spatial link field that is not a function of the organisation. The open item therefore sharpens rather than closes: what assigns the spatial phase, if not the occupancy? " +
            "(5) THREE ERRORS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT'S OWN TESTS. E_007's flux is an ELECTRIC field under this audit's convention that direction 1 is the clock's direction - its A_1 = f y sits in the (1,2) pair - so measuring it as magnetic correctly returned zero; the magnetic analogue is A_2 = f z, and the distinction is now in the code. The WRAP belongs on the SUM of the four link phases and not on each term: the unwrapped version read the seam artefact 5.497787, wrapping each term separately moved the artefact rather than removing it, and wrapping the sum gives the correct Abelian holonomy, 0.785398 uniformly. And a cross-audit check that compared two different profiles was not a check at all; run on E_009's own organisation it reproduces that audit's published 1.424E-002 exactly. " +
            "OUTPUT: REFUTED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the covariant completion and its linear control, the lattice-refinement scaling with fitted exponents, the surviving uniform flux, the gauge and Bianchi residuals, and the four requirement checks). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_005-E_009 keep their verdicts, and this audit supplies the reason E_009's magnetic half cannot be filled by the organisation. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/MagneticSectorAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 69/69.",
            Formula: "covariant completion A_mu = h(rho) Delta_mu rho: max |F_23| = 1.422E-003 with the derived coupling h = (2 pi / 96) rho^(1/3), 0.000E+000 with the linear coupling; electric part 2.203E-003; lattice-refinement scaling at fixed physical profile: covariant a^2.92 (1.42E-003, 2.06E-004, 2.61E-005, 3.32E-006 at L = 8, 16, 32, 64), site-local a^0.99 (9.91E-003, 5.05E-003, 2.55E-003, 1.27E-003); independently assigned uniform flux A_2 = f z: 0.785398 at every L; gauge residual 1.78E-015; wrapped holonomy = wrap of the SUM of the four link phases",
            CalculationId: "magnetic-sector-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_010", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_007", "ResearchY-E_004", "ResearchY-E_006"],
            AuditIds: ["e010"]),
        new("flux-origin-audit", "Flux Origin Audit", "What generates the surviving non-trivial loop flux F = 2 pi / 96? DERIVED: the origin is D96's own CLOSED TOPOLOGY together with the COMPACTNESS OF THE PHASE, and the number is the substrate's cycle length speaking. A closed cycle makes the holonomy gauge-proof - a single-valued gauge function telescopes to zero around it (2.498E-016 at L = 96, 0.000E+000 at L = 17), the exact complement of E_008's theorem for contractible loops - and a compact phase quantises it: only f L = 2 pi n survives, while half a sector is not periodic. The quantum is the cycle length: 2 pi / L = 0.065449847 at L = 96, with quantum times L the same at every length, reproducing E_007's figure. Occupancy structure, winding number and actualization process are refuted; assigning the integer sector is a boundary condition.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["magnetic-sector-audit", "field-strength-origin-audit", "field-excitation-audit", "photon-ontology-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE ORIGIN IS D96'S OWN CLOSED TOPOLOGY TOGETHER WITH THE COMPACTNESS OF THE PHASE, AND 2 PI / 96 IS THE SUBSTRATE'S CYCLE LENGTH SPEAKING. Question: what generates the surviving non-trivial loop flux F = 2 pi / 96 that E_007 exhibited, subject to surviving the continuum limit, being gauge compatible, local, and acting on T1 and T2? Candidates: occupancy structure, D96 topology, winding number, actualization process, boundary assignment. " +
            "(1) INGREDIENT ONE - A CLOSED CYCLE MAKES THE HOLONOMY GAUGE-PROOF. A gauge function is single-valued, so its contribution around a closed cycle telescopes to zero: measured 2.498E-016 at L = 96 and 0.000E+000 at L = 17. This is the exact complement of E_008's theorem that a CONTRACTIBLE loop's gradient flux can be gauged away - the same algebra with the opposite conclusion, decided by whether the loop closes. The cycle is what makes the flux survive. " +
            "(2) INGREDIENT TWO - A COMPACT PHASE QUANTISES THE FLUX. The link variable is a phase, so its value at the far end of the cycle must equal its value at the near end; for a uniform field A_1 = f y that forces f L = 2 pi n. Periodicity residuals are 2.4E-016, 4.9E-016 and 7.3E-016 for n = 1, 2 and 3, while a flux HALF A SECTOR away from a whole turn is NOT periodic and therefore not allowed - the audit checks the rejecting direction too, because a condition that rejects something is worth more than one that accepts everything. " +
            "(3) THE QUANTUM IS THE CYCLE LENGTH AND NOTHING ELSE. Measured across cycle lengths 8, 16, 32 and 96, the quantum 2 pi / L is 0.785398163, 0.392699082, 0.196349541 and 0.065449847, with the quantum times the length equal to 6.283185307 every time. At L = 96 it is 0.065449847 - exactly the figure E_007 measured, reproduced by this audit to 1E-15 rather than quoted. A number that comes out of the length of a loop is not a free parameter; it is a property of the loop. " +
            "(4) THE CANDIDATES SORT THEMSELVES. OCCUPANCY STRUCTURE is refuted by E_010's measurement: every occupancy-derived curvature scales away, with exponents 2.92 and 0.99. D96 TOPOLOGY is the origin. WINDING NUMBER is refuted twice over: a winding is a gradient, so its curvature vanishes identically by E_008's theorem, AND its holonomy around a closed cycle is a whole turn, which is the identity - measured at 2.45E-016 from it; a winding is precisely the thing that leaves nothing behind. ACTUALIZATION PROCESS is refuted because it supplies the time-like component only (E_009), which contributes nothing to a purely spatial field strength. BOUNDARY ASSIGNMENT is the honest survivor of the negative half: every integer sector is allowed and nothing in AT selects one, so the quantisation is derived while the integer is a label, exactly as in gauge theory on a torus. " +
            "(5) WHAT EXACTLY SURVIVES IS MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. At fixed sector the CYCLE holonomy is 6.283185307, one whole turn and hence the identity; the PLAQUETTE holonomy exp(i f) is genuinely non-trivial at 6.544E-002. So the flux's content is LOCAL CURVATURE, NOT A TOPOLOGICAL CHARGE. And held at fixed sector the field strength falls as 1/L - 0.785398163, 0.392699082, 0.196349541 and 0.065449847 at L = 8, 16, 32 and 96 - so what genuinely survives the refinement is the EXISTENCE of a non-trivial loop configuration at every size, not its magnitude. The origin is identified; the magnitude is a property of how coarse the loop is. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the telescoping sum at two cycle lengths, the periodicity residuals including the rejecting case, the quantum-versus-length series, the reproduction of E_007's figure, the cycle and plaquette holonomy distances, and the four requirement checks). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_007-E_010 keep their verdicts, and this audit explains the number E_007 exhibited and E_010 could not attribute to the organisation. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FluxOriginAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED; group E 76/76.",
            Formula: "gauge contribution around a closed cycle telescopes to 2.498E-016 (L = 96) and 0.000E+000 (L = 17); periodicity residual 2.4E-016 / 4.9E-016 / 7.3E-016 for n = 1/2/3, half-sector NOT periodic; quantum 2 pi / L = 0.785398163 (8), 0.392699082 (16), 0.196349541 (32), 0.065449847 (96), with quantum x L = 6.283185307 at every length; cycle holonomy 6.283185307 = one whole turn, 2.45E-016 from the identity; plaquette holonomy 6.544E-002; field strength at fixed sector falls as 1/L",
            CalculationId: "flux-origin-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_011", "ResearchY-E_010", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_008", "ResearchY-E_007", "ResearchY-E_003"],
            AuditIds: ["e011"]),
        new("flux-excitation-audit", "Flux Excitation Audit", "What AT mechanism populates a non-trivial flux sector? BOUNDARY: nothing inside AT populates it. The occupancy route is re-measured and falls as a^1.97; summing plaquette holonomies over the whole torus counts every link twice with opposite signs, so the reduced fluxes must sum to a multiple of 2 pi - which FORBIDS a single half-turn flux (residual 3.141593) and ALLOWS a balanced pair (pi, -pi) exactly. The pair's amplitude is pi at every lattice size, so a surviving non-trivial flux exists; what does not exist is anything that creates it.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["flux-origin-audit", "magnetic-sector-audit", "field-strength-origin-audit", "field-excitation-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - NOTHING INSIDE AT POPULATES THE SECTOR, AND THE CONSTRAINT ON WHAT MAY POPULATE IT IS EXACT. Question: what AT mechanism populates a non-trivial flux sector, given that it must create F != 0, survive the continuum limit, and need no new primitive? Candidates: occupancy defects, topological defects, winding sectors, boundary conditions, actualization transitions. " +
            "(1) THE ORGANISATION CANNOT, AND THAT IS RE-MEASURED RATHER THAN CITED. The occupancy route A_mu = h(rho) Delta_mu rho loses its curvature as the substrate is refined: max |F| is 1.691E-002, 4.442E-003, 1.124E-003 and 2.820E-004 at L = 8, 16, 32 and 64, a fitted exponent of 2.00. The occupancy MOVES flux around; it cannot PUT ANY IN - which is E_010's conclusion reached again on this audit's own construction. " +
            "(2) THE FLUX CONTENT IS AN ASSIGNMENT WITH A GLOBAL CONSTRAINT, and this is the sharpest result of the audit. Summing plaquette holonomies over the WHOLE torus counts every link TWICE with opposite signs, so the reduced fluxes must sum to a multiple of 2 pi - measured at 0.00E+000 for a uniform field. The consequence is concrete rather than formal: a SINGLE half-turn flux VIOLATES the constraint, at a residual of 3.141593, while a BALANCED PAIR (pi, -pi) obeys it exactly, at 0.000E+000. A single fluxon is forbidden BY THE SHAPE OF THE SUBSTRATE, and the smallest non-trivial configuration is a pair. The constraint is a GLOBAL BALANCE: the partner may sit on another slice, because a SLICE's product is FREE - a slice's boundary is a NON-CONTRACTIBLE CYCLE, and with one half-turn on it the product sits 2.000000 away from the identity. " +
            "(3) THE PAIR MEETS THE REQUIREMENT THE OCCUPANCY ROUTE FAILS. Its amplitude is pi at EVERY lattice size tested - 3.141593 at L = 8, 16, 32 and 64 - against the occupancy route's fourfold fall per doubling. So a non-trivial flux with a SURVIVING amplitude exists at every scale; what does not exist is any AT mechanism that CREATES one. " +
            "(4) THE CANDIDATES SORT THEMSELVES. OCCUPANCY DEFECTS are REFUTED on the scaling. TOPOLOGICAL DEFECTS are BOUNDARY: a balanced pair IS a legitimate non-trivial configuration with a surviving amplitude, but nothing in AT creates one. WINDING SECTORS are REFUTED twice over by earlier results: a scalar winding is a gradient, so its curvature vanishes identically (E_008), and its closed-cycle holonomy is a whole turn, which is the identity (E_011). ACTUALIZATION TRANSITIONS are REFUTED because the process supplies the time-like component only (E_009), which cannot add flux content to a spatial slice. BOUNDARY CONDITIONS are BOUNDARY, and that is the answer: the sector is populated by an ASSIGNMENT, exactly as E_011 found for the origin of the quantum. " +
            "(5) ONE CLAIM WAS WITHDRAWN WHILE DOING THIS, and it is recorded because the first draft was confident about it. The draft held that the product of holonomies around a single SLICE is the identity, so a single half-turn flux would be impossible for that reason. The identity is true for the WHOLE TORUS and FALSE for a slice, whose boundary is a non-contractible cycle. The first version of the probe appeared to confirm the wrong claim, and the reason is instructive: it FOLDED the configuration at the seam before summing, which silently destroys exactly the quantity under test. The audit now measures the whole-torus sum, which is the constraint that actually forbids the single fluxon. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the whole-torus product, the slice product, the forbidden single fluxon, the allowed pair, the occupancy scaling with its fitted exponent, the requirement checks and the no-new-primitive census). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_007-E_011 keep their verdicts; this audit supplies the refinement that what E_011 called a boundary ASSIGNMENT is itself subject to a global constraint. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FluxExcitationAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "whole-torus product of reduced holonomies = identity (0.00E+000 from it); slice product with one half-turn is FREE, 2.000000 from the identity (a slice's boundary is a non-contractible cycle); single half-turn flux constraint residual 3.141593 -> FORBIDDEN; balanced pair (pi, -pi) residual 0.000E+000 -> ALLOWED; occupancy route max |F| = 1.691E-002, 4.442E-003, 1.124E-003, 2.820E-004 at L = 8, 16, 32, 64, fitted exponent a^1.97; balanced pair max |F| = 3.141593 at every lattice size",
            CalculationId: "flux-excitation-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_012", "ResearchY-E_011", "ResearchY-E_010", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_008", "ResearchY-E_007"],
            AuditIds: ["e012"]),
        new("flux-population-audit", "Flux Population Audit", "What mechanism populates the ALLOWED balanced flux sectors, given that a single fluxon is forbidden and a balanced pair is allowed? BOUNDARY for the population, with the mechanism's FORM DERIVED. Locality forces the shape: one link phase incremented changes the plaquette content only in pairs - 4 minimum, never 1, signed sum 0.000E+000 - so the single fluxon is unreachable by any local move, P(single) = 0.0 and P(pair) = 1.0. The pair cannot be gauged away (6.939E-017) and cannot decay one member at a time (residual 3.141593), but it has no lifetime: the flux has no potential, and the update rule's spatial part is exactly zero.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["flux-excitation-audit", "flux-origin-audit", "coupling-function-audit", "magnetic-sector-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - THE FORM OF ANY POPULATING MECHANISM IS DERIVED AND THE POPULATION IS A BOUNDARY, THE TWO LEVELS KEPT APART AS THE D_028/D_040 RULE REQUIRES. Question: what populates the allowed balanced flux sectors, given E_012's two findings - a single fluxon forbidden, a balanced pair allowed? Requirements: local, gauge compatible, survives the continuum limit, no new primitive. Candidates: occupancy rearrangement, defect pairs, boundary conditions, actualization transitions, spectral transitions. " +
            "(1) THE PAIRING IS FORCED AND THE MEASUREMENT IS EXACT. Increment ONE link phase on the lattice and the plaquette content changes only in pairs: for each orientation containing that direction, the plaquette at the site and the plaquette before it move by +delta and -delta. Measured over three directions, three increments and four lattice sizes - 36 configurations - the minimum number of plaquettes any local move touches is 4, the moves that touch a single plaquette number 0, and the signed sum of what a move changes is 0.000E+000. So E_012's forbidden case is not merely DISALLOWED, it is UNREACHABLE BY ANY LOCAL MOVE, and the sector population probability becomes a computed pair of numbers: P(single) = 0.0 exactly, P(pair) = 1.0 for every non-gradient local move. " +
            "(2) STABILITY IS EXACT AND IS NOT A LIFETIME. The pair's content is gauge invariant - adding a pure gauge field changes the plaquette content by 6.939E-017, machine precision, because for an Abelian connection the curvatures add - so no gauge transformation can remove it. Neither member can decay alone: reducing one to zero leaves a residual of 3.141593, forbidden by E_012's constraint, while annihilating the pair leaves 0.000E+000. The pair reads 3.141593 at every lattice size tested (L = 8, 16, 32, 64). " +
            "(3) THE LIFETIME IS UNDEFINED RATHER THAN LONG. The only AT law that could ever time anything is the clock law, and the flux is invisible to it: the sensitivity to the flux is 0.000E+000 while the sensitivity to the organisation is 1.061E-001 (the control). With no potential every flux value is degenerate, so a lifetime is an input and not a prediction. " +
            "(4) THE ACTIVATION IS MISSING, MEASURED THREE WAYS. The AT update rule's own field strength has a spatial part of 0.000E+000 against a time-like part of 1.424E-002 (E_009, re-measured here), so the actualization cannot populate the spatial sector. A live census finds 0 AT members coupling a spectral index to a link phase, against 25 lines touching a link field and a non-zero count touching a spectral index - so the zero is a DISJOINTNESS and not an absence. And the occupancy's constant-coupling limit is an exact gradient with plaquette content 6.939E-017, the floating-point floor of a telescoping sum: it can move flux, it can never manufacture any. " +
            "(5) THE CANDIDATES SORT THEMSELVES. OCCUPANCY REARRANGEMENT is REFUTED - its curvature scales away as a^1.97 and its gradient limit has no plaquette content. DEFECT PAIRS are DERIVED, forced rather than chosen. BOUNDARY CONDITIONS are BOUNDARY: the amount and the initial pattern are unselected and the lifetime is undefined. ACTUALIZATION TRANSITIONS are REFUTED because the update rule is purely electric. SPECTRAL TRANSITIONS are REFUTED because the two sectors are disjoint. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the pair-creation census, the balance of the signed sum, the population probabilities, the gauge residual, the single-member and annihilation residuals, the amplitude series, the clock-law sensitivity with its control, the update rule's sector split, the census with both controls and the gradient limit), and it has a live branch: if AT ever gains a spatial activation the population stops being a boundary and becomes derived. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_007-E_012 keep their verdicts; this audit refines E_012 rather than repeating it - that audit established that nothing creates a pair, this one that anything which ever does must be a pair, because the alternative is not forbidden but unreachable. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FluxPopulationAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "one link phase incremented: minimum plaquettes changed 4, moves touching a single plaquette 0, signed sum 0.000E+000 (36 configurations over 3 directions, 3 increments, L = 8/16/32/64); P(single) = 0.0, P(pair) = 1.0; pair amplitude 3.141593 at every L; pure gauge field changes the content by 6.939E-017; single member decayed alone residual 3.141593 (forbidden), pair annihilated residual 0.000E+000; clock law sensitivity flux 0.000E+000 vs organisation 1.061E-001; update rule max |F_ij| = 0.000E+000 vs max |F_0i| = 1.424E-002; census 0 spectral-link members vs 25 link-field lines; occupancy exponent a^1.97",
            CalculationId: "flux-population-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_013", "ResearchY-E_012", "ResearchY-E_011", "ResearchY-E_010", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_008"],
            AuditIds: ["e013"]),
        new("sector-selection-audit", "Sector Selection Audit", "What selects the flux sector label n, and why is n != 0? BOUNDARY: the origin of sector occupation is an EXTERNAL ASSIGNMENT, and the negative is proved rather than declared. One operation - adding a quantum of uniform field to a compact phase - generates the whole family (0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3) and inverts exactly; no AT law depends on the sector (blindness residual 4.163E-017 against a control of 1.000000 quanta); the whole-torus constraint permits every label at machine precision; and no operation of the configuration space takes a non-zero label to zero, so n = 0 is not special either.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["flux-population-audit", "flux-excitation-audit", "flux-origin-audit", "coupling-function-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - THE ORIGIN OF SECTOR OCCUPATION IS AN EXTERNAL ASSIGNMENT, AND THE NEGATIVE IS PROVED RATHER THAN DECLARED. Question: what selects the flux sector label n, and why is n != 0, given that n exists, n is quantised and n survives refinement? Candidates: boundary conditions, topological constraints, actualization process, initial conditions, occupancy arrangement. " +
            "(1) THE FAMILY IS GENERATED BY ONE OPERATION, AND THE OPERATION IS AN ASSIGNMENT. Adding a single quantum of uniform field, A_1 -> A_1 + (2 pi / L) y, is a legitimate change of a COMPACT phase: the real field at the far end is 6.283, not zero, but the phase is the same to 2.449E-016 - exactly how E_011's quantisation arose. Applied to the vacuum it produces the whole family, 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3, with the strength following 2 pi n / L (0.785398, 0.392699, 0.196350, 0.098175 at L = 8, 16, 32, 64 - an 8x fall while the LABEL stays 1 at every size), and it inverts to 0.000E+000. The sectors are one orbit under an assignment, not a family the dynamics wanders through. " +
            "(2) NOTHING IN AT DEPENDS ON THE SECTOR, measured through LINEARITY rather than asserted. The occupancy's own curvature contribution is read as the difference between two curvatures - what the organisation adds ON TOP of the sector - and comes out 2.203E-003 in the trivial sector and 2.203E-003 in the unit sector. The update rule's two parts and the clock law read identically as well, giving a blindness residual of 4.163E-017 against a control of 1.000000 quanta, which shows the sector is visible to a curvature measurement whenever a measurement wants to see it. A theory with no potential for a label has no way to prefer a value of that label. " +
            "(3) THE CONSTRAINT PERMITS EVERY SECTOR, so no selection argument can be built on it. E_012's whole-torus residual is at machine precision for every integer tested at every lattice size: 3.553E-015 for n = -3, 1.776E-015 for n = -1, 0.000E+000 for n = 0, 1.776E-015 for n = 1, 7.105E-015 for n = 3. The constraint that FORBIDS the single fluxon therefore does not restrict the uniform family at all. " +
            "(4) NO OPERATION COLLAPSES A NON-ZERO SECTOR TO ZERO, which is the sharpest way to say that n = 0 is not special either. Translation preserves the label (1.000000 at shifts of one and three cells); reflection reverses it (-1.000000, the orientation being reversed); negation reverses it too. Nothing produces zero, so the question WHY N != 0 has exactly the same status as WHY N = 0. " +
            "(5) THE CANDIDATES SORT THEMSELVES. BOUNDARY CONDITIONS are the origin. TOPOLOGICAL CONSTRAINTS are REFUTED, because the constraint permits every value. THE ACTUALIZATION PROCESS is REFUTED, because its field strength is purely electric (0.000E+000 spatial against 1.424E-002 time-like) and cannot weight a spatial sector. INITIAL CONDITIONS are BOUNDARY, and they are the SAME origin under another name - when the assignment is made is not a different mechanism from where - a degeneracy recorded rather than resolved. OCCUPANCY ARRANGEMENT is REFUTED twice over: sector-blind through linearity, and scaling away as a^1.97. " +
            "(6) A BUG WAS CAUGHT BY THE AUDIT'S OWN UNIFORMITY CHECK. The first version read the label from the UNREDUCED plaquette, so the one cell that wraps around reported 1.257E+001 and a perfectly uniform sector looked non-uniform. Both the label and the uniformity check now read the REDUCED phase - the same seam E_012 and E_013 each had to handle. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the generating series, the phase-versus-real periodicity, the invertibility, the uniformity residual, the blindness table through linearity, the constraint across seven labels and four sizes, the operation table, and the control) and it has a LIVE BRANCH: a single sector-dependent law anywhere in AT would move the occupation to DERIVED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_011-E_013 keep their verdicts; this audit locates the occupation E_011 left as a label. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/SectorSelectionAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "one quantum of uniform field A_1 -> A_1 + (2 pi / L) y: label shift +1, family 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 from the vacuum, invertibility 0.000E+000, phase periodicity 2.449E-016 against a real field of 6.283 not periodic, uniformity residual 8.882E-016; label 1 at L = 8/16/32/64 with strength 0.785398, 0.392699, 0.196350, 0.098175; blindness residual 4.163E-017 across four laws against a control of 1.000000 quanta; occupancy contribution 2.203E-003 at n = 0 and 2.203E-003 at n = 1; whole-torus residual <= 7.105E-015 for every n in -3..3; operations from n = 1: translation 1.000000, reflection -1.000000, negation -1.000000",
            CalculationId: "sector-selection-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_014", "ResearchY-E_013", "ResearchY-E_012", "ResearchY-E_011", "ResearchY-E_010", "ResearchY-E_009"],
            AuditIds: ["e014"]),
        new("sector-weight-audit", "Sector Weight Audit", "Can AT assign a probability or weight to flux sectors n? BOUNDARY over a DERIVED FLATNESS: the measure is exactly flat, so the sector is completely free. The measure is counted rather than argued - every configuration of a finite model binned by holonomy class gives exactly k^(L-1) per bin (1024, 1024, 1024, 1024 at (k,l) = (4,6)), with P(n) = 0.250000000 for every n - and the equality is a theorem because the shift between sectors is a bijection. Entropy, free room and multiplicity structure are one quantity under three names and assign the uniform weight; the occupancy measure is sector-blind, the actualization count does not exist, and the topological charge is the same for every sector.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["sector-selection-audit", "flux-population-audit", "flux-origin-audit", "flux-excitation-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY OVER A DERIVED FLATNESS - THE MEASURE ON SECTORS IS EXACTLY FLAT, SO THE FLUX SECTOR IS COMPLETELY FREE. Question: can AT assign a probability or weight to flux sectors n, and does any AT-derived quantity prefer n = 0 or |n| > 0? Candidates: occupancy measure, actualization count, entropy, free room, multiplicity structure, sector topology. " +
            "(1) THE MEASURE IS COUNTED RATHER THAN ARGUED. On a finite model - a periodic chain whose link phases take k equally spaced values - every configuration is enumerated and binned by holonomy class, and every bin holds exactly the same number: 1024 per bin out of 4096 at (k,l) = (4,6), 1296 of 7776 at (6,5), 512 of 4096 at (8,4), 15625 of 78125 at (5,7). The bin counts at (4,6) are 1024, 1024, 1024, 1024, so P(n) = 0.250000000 for every n and P(n)/P(m) = 1.000000. " +
            "(2) THE EQUALITY IS A THEOREM, NOT A COINCIDENCE OF THE SIZES TESTED. The shift that adds one quantum to a single link is a BIJECTION of the configuration set and moves the holonomy class by exactly one - verified on every model - so the bins must be equal and the enumeration merely confirms it. A measure that is uniform as a consequence of an invertible rearrangement is not an accident of the model. " +
            "(3) THREE OF THE SIX CANDIDATES ARE ONE QUANTITY UNDER THREE NAMES. Entropy, free room and multiplicity structure are all the number of configurations per sector: the largest entropy spread across sectors is 0.000E+000 and the smallest free-room ratio is 1.000000. They do assign a weight, and the weight they assign is the UNIFORM one - a weight with no preference in it, which is why the audit records them as derived yet useless for selection. " +
            "(4) THE OTHER THREE ARE REFUTED, EACH ON ITS OWN MEASUREMENT. The OCCUPANCY MEASURE is sector-blind: the organisation's own weight function reads identically in two different sectors, a spread of 0.000E+000, while a control shows the sectors differ by 1.000000 quanta - so the blindness is a property of the weight and not of the sectors. The ACTUALIZATION COUNT does not exist: the update rule's spatial part is 0.000E+000 against a time-like part of 1.424E-002, and the label is a function of the spatial links only, so no number of update steps changes it and the dynamics has no transition to count. SECTOR TOPOLOGY gives the same answer for every sector: E_011's cycle holonomy phase distance is 4.899E-016 throughout, because the holonomy is the identity for every n, so the topological charge is zero for the trivial sector and the non-trivial ones alike - while the strength differs, which is precisely why topology cannot weight it. " +
            "(5) THE FREE-ENERGY DIFFERENCE BETWEEN SECTORS IS ZERO. A Boltzmann weight would need an action; AT's sector-blindness residual from E_014, reused rather than recomputed, IS the free-energy difference, and it is 4.163E-017. " +
            "(6) THE HONEST SPLIT IS THE RESULT. The RATIO of the weights is derived exactly - P(n)/P(m) = 1, by bijection and by enumeration - while the ABSOLUTE NORMALISATION is not: a flat measure over a label that runs over the integers needs a regulator, AT supplies none, and the weight of a single sector is therefore undefined without an input. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the enumerated bin counts on four models, the bijection census, the entropy spread and free-room ratio, the occupancy weight spread with its control, the update rule's sector split, the topology table with its holonomy distances and strengths, the reused free-energy residual, and the control that the sectors are distinguishable) and it has a LIVE BRANCH in every direction: a non-flat multiplicity, a sector-dependent occupancy weight, a label-changing update or a sector-dependent invariant would each make the weight DERIVED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_011-E_014 keep their verdicts; this audit closes every counting-based route to a preferred sector. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/SectorWeightAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "enumerated bin counts: (k,l) = (4,6) 1024, 1024, 1024, 1024 of 4096; (6,5) 1296 of 7776; (8,4) 512 of 4096; (5,7) 15625 of 78125; P(n) = 0.250000000, P(n)/P(m) = 1.000000; the shift is a bijection moving the class by one (verified on every model); entropy spread 0.000E+000, free-room ratio 1.000000; occupancy weight spread 0.000E+000 against a control of 1.000000 quanta; update rule spatial 0.000E+000, time-like 1.424E-002; cycle holonomy phase distance 4.899E-016 for every n; sector-blindness residual 4.163E-017",
            CalculationId: "sector-weight-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_015", "ResearchY-E_014", "ResearchY-E_013", "ResearchY-E_012", "ResearchY-E_011", "ResearchY-E_009"],
            AuditIds: ["e015"]),
        new("sector-population-principle-audit", "Sector Population Principle Audit", "Do any existing AT quantities break the flat sector measure of E_015? REFUTED: none does, and the audit validated its detector before believing it. Two synthetic breakers confirm the method can find one - a non-uniform local potential (1.6E-001) and a recipe-phase bridge (3.3E-001) - while the trivial weight and a phase-uniform potential give 0.000E+000. Three candidates are recipe-side and factorise (free room 4096, 4096, 4096, 4096; census 0); two are phase-side and sector-symmetric (multiplicity by E_015's bijection; a purely electric update). A coarse-observable prediction was withdrawn: a half-period symmetry forces it flat. A breaker would need a potential for the link phase or a recipe-phase coupling - both new primitives.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Refuted, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["sector-weight-audit", "sector-selection-audit", "flux-population-audit", "coupling-function-audit"],
            Narrative: "REFUTED - NO EXISTING AT QUANTITY BREAKS THE FLAT MEASURE, AND THE AUDIT VALIDATED ITS DETECTOR BEFORE BELIEVING IT. Question: does any quantity the theory already contains tilt the flat sector measure E_015 established, without introducing new primitives? Candidates: occupancy free room, multiplicity structure, D96 hierarchy, compression laws, actualization rate. " +
            "(1) THE DETECTOR IS VALIDATED FIRST. The search is a sector-restricted sum of a weight over every configuration of a finite model, so a breaker shows as a non-zero relative spread of those sums. Synthetic breaker one - a weight with a NON-UNIFORM local factor on the link phase, which is what a potential for the phase IS - breaks flatness at 1.6E-001; synthetic breaker two, a BRIDGE between the recipe sector and the phase sector, breaks the conditional recipe marginal at 3.3E-001. The controls confirm the other direction: the trivial weight gives 0.000E+000 and a potential that does not depend on the phase gives 0.000E+000. The machinery can detect a breaker. " +
            "(2) THE FIVE CANDIDATES FAIL FOR TWO DISTINCT REASONS, AND THE SPLIT IS THE USEFUL PART. THREE ARE RECIPE-SIDE QUANTITIES: occupancy free room, the D96 hierarchy and the compression laws all read the substrate and the recipes, while the sector labels the PHASE half, so their sector sums factorise into a phase count times a recipe quantity - free room per sector 4096, 4096, 4096, 4096 at (k,l) = (4,6), spread 0.000E+000, factorisation residual 0.000E+000. A quantity that never takes the phase as an argument cannot see the label, and the live census confirms the absence of any bridge: 0 AT members couple a spectral index to a link phase, E_013's count reused rather than recounted. " +
            "(3) TWO ARE PHASE-SIDE AND BOTH ARE SECTOR-SYMMETRIC. The multiplicity is equal by E_015's bijection, reused here (spread over the sectors 0.000E+000), and the update rule's spatial part is 0.000E+000 against a time-like part of 1.424E-002, so the actualization rate cannot read the label at all; E_014's sector-blindness residual stands at 4.163E-017. " +
            "(4) A PREDICTION WAS WITHDRAWN, AND IT IS THE INSTRUCTIVE PART. The first draft expected the conditional distribution of a coarse phase observable to differ across sectors, on the reasoning that the shift between neighbouring sectors moves one link's value by one. Measured, it does NOT: the global HALF-PERIOD SHIFT maps the lower half of the phase range onto the upper half while leaving the class unchanged whenever (k/2)L is a multiple of k, so the mean is FORCED to L/2 in every class and the conditional spread is 0.000E+000. That is a SYMMETRY, not a coincidence, and it is recorded as a withdrawn prediction rather than quietly deleted. " +
            "(5) THE REAL NEAREST MISS IS A WEIGHT RATHER THAN AN OBSERVABLE. A phase-reading weight breaks the class sums at 1.6E-001, so nothing about the configuration space prevents a non-flat measure - what prevents it is that AT supplies no such weight: no potential for the link phase (E_013) and no bridge into the recipe sector (the census above). " +
            "(6) WHAT A BREAKER WOULD HAVE TO BE, STATED SO IT CAN BE TESTED LATER: either a POTENTIAL for the link phase - a weight with a non-uniform local factor, broken by the validated detector at 1.6E-001 - or a COUPLING between the recipe sector and the phase sector, broken by the same machinery at 3.3E-001 while the live census scores it at 0. Both are NEW PRIMITIVES, which is why the goal as posed is refuted while the question of a breaker remains open in principle and closed in practice. " +
            "OUTPUT: REFUTED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the two synthetic breakers and the two controls, the free room and multiplicity spreads measured over the SECTORS, the factorisation residual with its census input, the update rule's sector split, the topology-independent blindness residual, the withdrawn-prediction measurement and the control that the sectors are distinguishable) and it has a LIVE BRANCH: a phase-reading AT quantity with a non-uniform local factor, or a non-zero recipe-phase census, would move it to DERIVED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: E_011-E_015 keep their verdicts; this audit closes the search E_015's flat measure invited. No group-G registry claim, so the claim counts are unchanged. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/SectorPopulationPrincipleAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "detector: trivial weight 0.000E+000, phase-uniform potential 0.000E+000, NON-uniform local potential 1.6E-001, recipe-phase bridge 3.3E-001; free room per sector at (k,l) = (4,6): 4096, 4096, 4096, 4096, spread 0.000E+000; multiplicity spread over the sectors 0.000E+000; factorisation residual 0.000E+000; census of recipe-phase couplings 0; update rule spatial 0.000E+000 against time-like 1.424E-002; sector-blindness residual 4.163E-017; conditional coarse-observable spread 0.000E+000 (forced flat by the half-period symmetry)",
            CalculationId: "sector-population-principle-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-E_016", "ResearchY-E_015", "ResearchY-E_014", "ResearchY-E_013", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_012"],
            AuditIds: ["e016"]),
        new("rho-accessibility-audit", "Rho Accessibility Audit", "Can the hidden 47 dimensions of rho ever influence an observable? OBSERVABLE: a validated hidden step - a sum-neutral direction in the kernel of the contraction observables - changes a contraction by 5.116E-013 and still moves the clock-rate multiset (3.764E-003), the acceleration multiset (3.010E-003) and the field strength (6.327E-004), while the flux sector stays untouched (0.000E+000; 0 members couple the two sectors). The first identification was WITHDRAWN: the hidden directions are not the symmetry orbit (span 84, not 47) but the kernel of the contractions. G_040's 48 is a ceiling over states, not the value at every state (kernel 53, retained 43).", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["rho-observable-audit", "flux-population-audit", "coupling-function-audit", "rho-realization-audit"],
            Narrative: "OBSERVABLE - THE HIDDEN 47 REACH THE LOCAL LAWS, AND THE AUDIT'S FIRST IDENTIFICATION OF THEM WAS WITHDRAWN. Question: can the hidden 47 dimensions of rho ever influence an observable - clocks, acceleration, flux sectors, field strengths - or are they permanently gauge-like? G_040 gives the split: 95 state dimensions = 48 retained magnitudes + 47 intra-doublet orientations, one angle per two-dimensional irrep, and D96 has exactly 47 of those. " +
            "(1) THE FIRST ANSWER WAS WRONG AND IS RECORDED AS WITHDRAWN. The draft identified the hidden directions with the ORBIT of the substrate's symmetry, on the reasoning that a symmetry move is the textbook motion that changes nothing invariant. The measurement refused it: the orbit span is 84 dimensions, not 47. A symmetry move IS gauge-like, but for a DIFFERENT reason - it relabels the cells - and conflating the two would have made the argument rest on a false premise. " +
            "(2) THE HIDDEN SET IS THE KERNEL OF THE CONTRACTIONS, BUILT AND VALIDATED. A direction orthogonal to the contraction gradient rows, made SUM-NEUTRAL so a step along it stays on the simplex, changes a contraction by 5.116E-013 - nothing, by construction. Sum-neutrality is not decoration: a first version of the step renormalised the perturbed state, which moved it along OBSERVABLE directions as well and made a hidden step change a contraction by 2.061. " +
            "(3) SYMMETRY MOVES ARE RELABELLING-ONLY, WHICH IS THE GAUGE CONTROL. Over the whole group orbit the multisets are unchanged - clocks 0.000E+000, acceleration 0.000E+000, field strengths 5.140E-016, flux sectors 0.000E+000 - while the ADDRESSED reports move (1.719E-001, 1.603E-001, 5.823E-002). The controls hold: the addressed pattern itself sees the move at 4.937E-001, and moving the phase moves the flux label by 1.000000. " +
            "(4) THE DECISIVE MEASUREMENT IS THE VALIDATED HIDDEN STEP, AND THREE OF THE FOUR MOVE. The clock-rate multiset by 3.764E-003, the acceleration multiset by 3.010E-003, the field strength by 6.327E-004 - with no contraction changed anywhere. The FLUX SECTOR does not move at all (0.000E+000): its label is carried by the link phases rather than by rho, and 0 AT members couple the two sectors (E_013's census). So clocks, acceleration and field strengths are OBSERVABLE to the hidden content and the flux sector is HIDDEN - exactly what the theory's own decoupling requires. " +
            "(5) ONE NUMBER IS RECORDED AGAINST G_040 RATHER THAN SMOOTHED AWAY. The kernel measures 53 dimensions at the audited state against the ceiling of 47, retaining 43 against 48. G_040's 48 is therefore a CEILING OVER STATES and not the value at every state: a refinement of G_040, not a contradiction, and both numbers are reported side by side. " +
            "OUTPUT: OBSERVABLE. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the split and its doublet identity, the withdrawn orbit measurement, the validated hidden step with its sum-neutrality, the symmetry-move multisets with their addressed controls, the flux census, and the kernel-versus-ceiling retention) and it has live branches: a multiset that moved under a symmetry move would be OBSERVABLE for a different reason, and a failure of the hidden-step construction would leave the question open. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 keeps its verdict and gains a refinement note on the state-dependence of its ceiling; the flux sector's HIDDEN status follows from E_013's decoupling rather than being a new claim. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/RhoAccessibilityAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "95 = retained 48 + hidden 47 (doublet count 47); orbit span 84 (NOT the hidden set); validated hidden step: contraction change 5.116E-013, clock-rate multiset 3.764E-003, acceleration 3.010E-003, field strength 6.327E-004, flux 0.000E+000; symmetry moves: clocks 0.000E+000, acceleration 0.000E+000, fields 5.140E-016, addressed 1.719E-001 / 1.603E-001 / 5.823E-002; controls: addressed pattern 4.937E-001, phase moves the label 1.000000; kernel 53 against G_040's ceiling 47 (retained 43 against 48)",
            CalculationId: "rho-accessibility-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_046", "ResearchY-G_040", "ResearchY-E_013", "ResearchY-G_039", "ResearchY-E_009"],
            AuditIds: ["g046"]),
        new("kernel-observable-audit", "Kernel Observable Audit", "Which observable detects the kernel directions directly? DERIVED: AT's own clock law read at each cell, with the minimal basis one reading per kernel dimension. The kernel is built at the audited state - contraction rank 42, kernel 53 against G_040's ceiling of 47 - and every basis direction changes no contraction (5.684E-013). The clock responds at 1.726E-002 (acceleration 3.298E-002, field strength 6.479E-003) while every contraction stays at 5.684E-013, the reading map has full rank 53 on the 53-dimensional kernel with directions 2.338E-002 apart, and the basis is 53 readings from a maximum of 96 cells.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["rho-accessibility-audit", "rho-observable-audit", "coupling-function-audit", "flux-population-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE FIRST OBSERVABLE IS AT'S OWN CLOCK LAW READ AT EACH CELL, AND THE MINIMAL BASIS IS ONE READING PER KERNEL DIMENSION. Question: which observable detects the kernel directions directly, given requirements that it respond to hidden directions, distinguish kernel states and be independent of the contraction observables? G_046 identified the hidden set as the kernel; this audit names the reading and sizes the instrument. " +
            "(1) THE KERNEL IS BUILT AT THE AUDITED STATE. The contraction rows plus the simplex direction span 43 dimensions, so the kernel measures 53 against G_040's ceiling of 47 - both numbers reported so that an audit at a different state can compare - and every kernel basis direction changes no contraction (5.684E-013). " +
            "(2) THE READING IS THE ADDRESSED CLOCK-RATE PATTERN, with no new primitive: the clock law the theory already has, read per cell rather than in aggregate. It responds at 1.726E-002, the acceleration at 3.298E-002 and the field strength at 6.479E-003, while every contraction stays at 5.684E-013. " +
            "(3) THAT PAIR OF NUMBERS IS THE INDEPENDENCE MEASUREMENT. A quantity that stayed fixed while the contractions moved would be a function of them; this one moves while they are fixed. The contractions retain 43 dimensions where the clock resolves 53, so the reading adds information they cannot carry. " +
            "(4) IT DISTINGUISHES KERNEL STATES WITH FULL RANK. The reading map restricted to the kernel has rank 53 on a 53-dimensional kernel, and the acceleration resolves it too; two different kernel directions differ by 2.338E-002, so no two kernel states are conflated. " +
            "(5) THE RANK IS THE MINIMAL OBSERVABLE BASIS, and the minimality is STRUCTURAL rather than fitted: a single cell's clock rate has a gradient pointing along one direction, so resolving d kernel dimensions requires d independent cell readings, and the addressed clock pattern supplies exactly that many - 53 readings from a maximum of 96 cells. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the kernel construction and its zero contraction response, the three candidate responses, the reading ranks, the distinguishing separation and the basis size against the measured kernel) and it has live branches: a reading that responded while a contraction moved would be REFUTED, and a reading of lower rank than the kernel would be BOUNDARY. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 keep their verdicts; the ceiling-versus-state distinction is carried forward rather than resolved in the audited state's favour. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/KernelObservableAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "state 96 (simplex 95); contraction rank 42 (43 with the simplex direction); kernel 53 against G_040's ceiling 47; contraction change along every kernel direction 5.684E-013; clock response 1.726E-002, acceleration 3.298E-002, field strength 6.479E-003; reading rank on the kernel: clock 53, acceleration 53; separation between neighbouring kernel directions 2.338E-002; minimal basis 53 readings from 96 cells",
            CalculationId: "kernel-observable-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_047", "ResearchY-G_046", "ResearchY-G_040", "ResearchY-E_009", "ResearchY-E_013"],
            AuditIds: ["g047"]),
        new("clock-completeness-audit", "Clock Completeness Audit", "Is the clock pattern the maximal observable of rho? MAXIMAL - and tied with two others. On the 95-dimensional simplex tangent space the clock, acceleration and field-strength patterns each have observable dimension 95 with information retained 1.000 (and kernel rank 53), while the contraction observables retain 43 / 0.453. The clock's completeness is checked by an explicit inverse - rho = rate^d with a residual of 4.441E-016 - and the control shows the completeness lives in the addressing: aggregating the same law gives observable dimension 1. Ordering: clock 95 = acceleration 95 = field 95 > contractions 43.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["kernel-observable-audit", "rho-accessibility-audit", "rho-observable-audit", "coupling-function-audit"],
            Narrative: "MAXIMAL - THE CLOCK PATTERN RESOLVES THE WHOLE STATE AND IS INVERTIBLE, BUT IT IS MAXIMAL AND TIED WITH TWO OTHERS, AND THE CONTRACTION OBSERVABLES ARE THE ONLY READING MEASURED HERE THAT LOSES INFORMATION. Question: is the clock pattern the maximal observable of rho, comparing the clock, acceleration, field-strength and contraction readings on kernel rank, information retained and observable dimension? " +
            "(1) THE FOUR READINGS ARE MEASURED ON THE 95-DIMENSIONAL SIMPLEX TANGENT SPACE. Clock 95 / 1.000 / kernel rank 53; acceleration 95 / 1.000 / 53; field strength 95 / 1.000 / 53; contraction observables 43 / 0.453 / 0. " +
            "(2) THE CLOCK PATTERN IS COMPLETE AND INVERTIBLE, NOT MERELY OF FULL RANK. The organisation is recovered from the rates as rho = rate^d with a residual of 4.441E-016, so the full rank is a property rather than a sampling coincidence. The control keeps the headline honest: aggregating the same law gives observable dimension 1 out of 95, so the completeness lives in ADDRESSING the cells rather than in the law alone - the same distinction that separates G_040's ceiling from this floor. " +
            "(3) THE ACCELERATION PATTERN TIES AT THE TOP, and this is the result a chain-shaped answer would have missed. Neighbouring differences lose the global constant on an ARBITRARY vector, but the state lives on the SIMPLEX, which already excludes it, so on the tangent space the difference map is injective and its dimension is 95 as well. " +
            "(4) THE FIELD-STRENGTH PATTERN TIES TOO, AND THE AUDIT'S OWN PREDICTION OF PARTIALITY WAS WITHDRAWN AND RECORDED. The draft expected a shortfall because the coupling is evaluated at each cell and the pattern is nonlinear in the organisation; the measurement refused it - the tangent map is diagonal-plus-difference with a positive coupling, hence generically invertible, dimension 95. " +
            "(5) THE CONTRACTIONS ARE REDUNDANT AND THE ONLY READING THAT LOSES ANYTHING: 43 dimensions against the addressed readings' 95, a proper sub-algebra of what the clock already resolves, which is exactly what G_040's ceiling of 48 always was - the ceiling of the NON-ADDRESSED readings. " +
            "(6) THE ORDERING IS NEITHER A CHAIN NOR TOTAL EQUIVALENCE: clock 95 = acceleration 95 = field 95 > contractions 43, so 'clock > acceleration > contraction' is refuted on BOTH its strict inequalities and 'all are equivalent' is refuted by the contractions. What remains is a two-level structure with the addressed readings complete and the non-addressed one not. " +
            "OUTPUT: MAXIMAL. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the ranks of four readings on the tangent space and on the kernel, the explicit inverse of the clock map, the aggregation control, the tier membership and the ordering string) and it has live branches: a clock dimension below the state dimension would be PARTIAL, and a clock no better than the contractions would be REDUNDANT. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040, G_046 and G_047 keep their verdicts; G_040's ceiling is placed as the ceiling of the non-addressed sub-algebra rather than of observation. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/ClockCompletenessAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "state dimension 95; clock 95 / 1.000 / kernel 53; acceleration 95 / 1.000 / 53; field strength 95 / 1.000 / 53; contractions 43 / 0.453 / 0; clock invertibility residual (rho = rate^d) 4.441E-016; aggregated rate observable dimension 1; minimal basis 95 readings; ordering clock 95 = acceleration 95 = field 95 > contractions 43",
            CalculationId: "clock-completeness-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_048", "ResearchY-G_047", "ResearchY-G_046", "ResearchY-G_040", "ResearchY-E_009"],
            AuditIds: ["g048"]),
        new("clock-primacy-audit", "Clock Primacy Audit", "Is the clock pattern the unique lossless observable of rho? LOSSLESS but NOT UNIQUE: three of the four readings are information-equivalent to rho. Clock 95 / 1.000 with a closed-form inverse (rho = rate^d, residual 4.441E-016); acceleration 95 / 1.000 with 0 collisions at residual 0.000E+000; field-strength 95 / 1.000 with 0 collisions at 0.000E+000; contractions 43 / 0.453 with 52 dimensions missing. The uniform test - inversion by projected gradient descent from displaced starts with the audited state as the control, which recovers itself - found zero collisions for every full-rank reading, so the hypothesis that rank hides lossiness is not confirmed.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["clock-completeness-audit", "kernel-observable-audit", "rho-accessibility-audit", "coupling-function-audit"],
            Narrative: "LOSSLESS BUT NOT UNIQUE - THE CLOCK PATTERN IS INFORMATION-EQUIVALENT TO RHO, AND THREE OF THE FOUR READINGS COMPARED ARE TOO; WHAT DISTINGUISHES THE CLOCK IS A CLOSED-FORM INVERSE. Question: is the clock pattern the unique lossless observable of rho, comparing the clock, acceleration, field-strength and contraction readings on invertibility, retained information, rank and kernel? " +
            "(1) THE FOUR READINGS AND THE UNIFORM INVERSION TEST. Clock 95 / 1.000 with a closed-form inverse rho = rate^d at a residual of 4.441E-016; acceleration 95 / 1.000 with zero collisions at a best residual of 0.000E+000; field-strength 95 / 1.000 with zero collisions at 0.000E+000; contractions 43 / 0.453 with 52 dimensions missing. Lossless readings: three, so the clock is NOT unique. " +
            "(2) THE TEST IS HONEST IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Each reading's inverse is attempted by projected gradient descent on the simplex from three deterministic displaced starts, with the audited state itself as the CONTROL: the control recovers the state, so the machinery is known to be able to succeed before its failures are believed. A configuration that leaves the positive simplex is rejected rather than scored, because the rate law is rho^(1/d) and a negative cell would make the reading NaN - a first version of the search followed those NaNs and had to be hardened. " +
            "(3) A PROOF WAS WITHDRAWN AND A HYPOTHESIS WAS NOT CONFIRMED. The audit set out to show that RANK DOES NOT IMPLY INVERTIBILITY, and its first instrument was an explicit COLLISION: reflecting the state through its own mean reverses every difference, and the acceleration pattern uses ABSOLUTE differences, so the reflection should collide. The measurement REFUSED it - the reflection reverses the differences of RHO while the pattern is built from differences of the RATE, and the cube root is not linear - so the reflected pair sat 1.951E-002 apart. The collision is recorded as withdrawn. Its replacement - the search - found ZERO collisions for all three full-rank readings and converged back onto the audited state from every displaced start, so full rank and invertibility COINCIDED for these four readings at this state: recorded as an EMPIRICAL OUTCOME, NOT a theorem, because full rank is necessary and happened to be sufficient here. " +
            "(4) THE CONTRACTIONS ARE LOSSY BY DIMENSION, needing no search: 43 of 95 dimensions retained, 52 unrecoverable in principle. " +
            "(5) WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE GOAL. Time is A primary observable of the organisation - the clock pattern is lossless - and it is NOT the unique one: three of the four readings compared are information-equivalent to rho. The distinguishing property the measurement leaves to the clock is INVERTIBILITY IN CLOSED FORM, one call per cell as rho = rate^d, where the other two lossless readings must be inverted numerically. That is a real asymmetry and it is not the asymmetry the question proposed. " +
            "OUTPUT: LOSSLESS. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the four ranks, the closed-form residual, the collision counts and best residuals from a control-checked search, and the tier membership) and it has live branches: a collision found for the clock pattern would make it LOSSY, and a failed control would make the search untrustworthy and the verdict PARTIAL. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040, G_046, G_047 and G_048 keep their verdicts; G_048's ranking is completed by the invertibility test that its ranks could not supply. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/ClockPrimacyAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "clock 95 / 1.000, closed form rho = rate^d residual 4.441E-016, 0 collisions; acceleration 95 / 1.000, 0 collisions, best residual 0.000E+000; field-strength 95 / 1.000, 0 collisions, best residual 0.000E+000; contractions 43 / 0.453, 52 dimensions missing; control start recovers the state: True; withdrawn collision: reflected pair 1.951E-002 apart; lossless readings: 3; the clock is unique: False",
            CalculationId: "clock-primacy-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_049", "ResearchY-G_048", "ResearchY-G_047", "ResearchY-G_040", "ResearchY-E_009"],
            AuditIds: ["g049"]),
        new("kernel-structure-audit", "Kernel Structure Audit", "What physical structure do the 53 kernel directions represent? DERIVED: the kernel is the PHASE SECTOR. One hidden quadrature per populated doublet (G_040's intra-doublet orientation), both quadratures of each of the 5 empty channels, and the alternating mode - 47 + 5 + 1 = 53 - with the visible 42 being the magnitudes. The contractions are circulant, so the kernel is a union of whole Fourier modes (no mode split); the dihedral prediction of whole doublets was refuted by 42 half-hidden doublets, and the short-wavelength prediction by the interleaving of hidden and visible modes (correlation -0.0279).", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["clock-primacy-audit", "clock-completeness-audit", "kernel-observable-audit", "rho-observable-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE KERNEL IS THE PHASE SECTOR OF THE ORGANISATION: ONE HIDDEN QUADRATURE PER POPULATED DOUBLET, BOTH QUADRATURES OF EACH EMPTY CHANNEL, AND THE ALTERNATING MODE, 47 + 5 + 1 = 53. Question: what physical structure do the 53 kernel directions represent, measured through basis vectors, symmetry classes, the multiplicity relation and the clock, acceleration and field signatures? " +
            "(1) TWO HYPOTHESES WERE REFUTED BEFORE THE RIGHT ONE WAS NAMED. The first argued from the DIHEDRAL symmetry that the kernel must be a union of whole 2-dimensional doublets, and the measurement refused it: 42 of the 47 doublets are HALF hidden, because a real 2-dimensional irreducible admits a 2x2 commutant. The correct argument is the SHARPER one - the contraction observables are CIRCULANT, hence diagonal in the individual Fourier modes - so it is TRANSLATION invariance, not reflection symmetry, that forbids mixing; measured per mode, no mode is split anywhere. The second expected the hidden modes to be the SHORT-WAVELENGTH ones, since distance-class contractions average over cells; the measurement refused that too - the hidden and visible modes are INTERLEAVED channel by channel (separated in frequency: False) with the clock-signature correlation against frequency at -0.0279. " +
            "(2) THE COUNT RELATION NAMES THE KERNEL. Hidden 53 Fourier modes, visible 42 (53 + 42 = 95 with the constant mode being the simplex direction), 42 half-hidden doublet channels, and 5 EMPTY channels whose set is IDENTICAL to the doubly-hidden ones: 47 (one hidden quadrature per populated doublet - G_040's intra-doublet orientation) + 5 (both quadratures of each empty channel) + 1 (the alternating mode) = 53. The visible 42 are the MAGNITUDES of the populated channels. " +
            "(3) THIS RECONCILES G_040 EXACTLY. G_040's loss of 47 is the GENERIC case - 47 orientations and no empty channel - while this state hides five extra channels' worth because the state carries nothing in them: the same structure, evaluated at a different state. " +
            "(4) THE SIGNATURES COVER EVERY HIDDEN MODE. All 53 hidden modes carry a response from all three lossless readings (clock, acceleration, field), so the interpretation does not depend on which reading one uses; what the signatures do NOT show is any frequency ordering, which is what withdrew the wavelength-band reading. " +
            "(5) WHAT THE KERNEL IS NOT is also measured: not a gauge orbit (G_046 measured the symmetry orbit at 84 dimensions), not a numerical artefact (every mode whole to 1E-3 or better), and not the whole remainder of the state (the visible 42 are real named content). " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the per-mode classes, the count relation, the empty-channel identity, the signature coverage and the two refused hypotheses) and it has live branches: a split mode would be REFUTED, and a state with no empty channels would still be DERIVED through the generic 47. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040, G_046, G_047 and G_049 keep their verdicts; G_040's 'intra-doublet orientation' is now measured directly rather than inferred from a dimension count. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/KernelStructureAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "hidden Fourier modes 53, visible 42 (total 95); half-hidden doublet channels 42; empty channels 5, identical to the doubly-hidden set; count relation 47 + 5 + 1 = 53; no mode split anywhere; hidden and visible modes interleaved (separated in frequency: False); clock-signature against frequency correlation -0.0279; every hidden mode carries all three signatures",
            CalculationId: "kernel-structure-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-G_049", "ResearchY-G_047", "ResearchY-G_046", "ResearchY-G_040"],
            AuditIds: ["g050"]),
        new("phase-sector-audit", "Phase Sector Audit", "Do the 53 phase-sector directions carry physical or gauge information? PHYSICAL: all 53 are observable and none is gauge. Stepping along each mode in turn moves the clock-rate multiset for all of them (smallest 2.136E-003), the acceleration multiset (4.859E-004) and the field multiset (5.204E-005), each first-order in the step. The flux sector is silent for all 53 because its label reads the link phases and 0 members couple them to the organisation - a decoupling, not a gauge signature - and the criterion excludes it deliberately. The control, a symmetry-orbit move, leaves every multiset at 0.000E+000, so the test recognises a real gauge direction and finds none.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["kernel-structure-audit", "clock-primacy-audit", "clock-completeness-audit", "flux-population-audit"],
            Narrative: "PHYSICAL - ALL 53 PHASE DIRECTIONS ARE OBSERVABLE, NOT ONE IS GAUGE, AND THE AUDIT'S REAL CONTRIBUTION IS THE DISTINCTION THAT MAKES THE WORD GAUGE MEAN SOMETHING. Question: do the 53 phase-sector directions carry physical or gauge information, measured through the clock, acceleration, field and flux-sector responses? " +
            "(1) THE RESPONSES ARE UNIFORMLY NON-ZERO. Stepping along each of the 53 modes in turn, the clock-rate MULTISET moves for all of them, and so do the acceleration and field multisets: the smallest clock response over the whole sector is 2.136E-003, the smallest acceleration response 4.859E-004 and the smallest field response 5.204E-005. The multiset is the right object to read, because it is what a law reports about the system rather than which cell carries what - the distinction G_048 used to separate a relabelling from a change. " +
            "(2) THE RESPONSES ARE FIRST-ORDER, WHICH SEPARATES PHYSICAL FROM NEARLY GAUGE. A direction whose readings moved only at second order would be invisible to linear response, which is as close to gauge as a non-gauge direction can be; the audit halves the step and measures the ratio, and every direction scales as the step, which is what a first-order response does. " +
            "(3) THE FLUX RESPONSE IS ZERO FOR ALL 53, AND THE AUDIT INSISTS ON SAYING WHY. The flux label is carried by the LINK phases, and the census of AT members coupling them to the organisation is 0: no move of the organisation of any kind can change the label. That is a DECOUPLING, not a gauge signature, and the criterion used for the verdict therefore EXCLUDES it - a direction is gauge when the readings that CAN see it report nothing, not when a decoupled probe happens to be silent. Had the audit counted the flux silence as gauge-ness, every direction in the theory would have been called gauge the moment one decoupled probe was added, which is the error this measurement exists to prevent. " +
            "(4) THE CONTROL IS AN ACTUAL GAUGE DIRECTION. A move along the substrate-symmetry orbit leaves every multiset unchanged at 0.000E+000, so the test can recognise a gauge direction when it sees one - and it finds none among the 53. " +
            "(5) WHAT THE ANSWER SAYS. The quadratures that complete each channel's magnitude are not hidden from OBSERVATION; they are hidden from the INVARIANT ALGEBRA of distance contractions that G_040 was studying. The organisation's phase is physics, and it is invisible to the measurements that were built to ignore it. " +
            "OUTPUT: PHYSICAL. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the per-direction responses with their minima, the halving test for first order, the symmetry-orbit control and the coupling census) and it has live branches: a direction silent to all responsive readings would be GAUGE, and a mixture would be MIXED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_046 to G_050 keep their verdicts; G_050's phase sector is now shown to be physical rather than formal. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseSectorAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "53 phase directions; smallest clock multiset response 2.136E-003, acceleration 4.859E-004, field 5.204E-005; every direction observable and first-order (halving ratio 0.5); physical 53, gauge 0; symmetry-orbit gauge control 0.000E+000; AT members coupling the link sector to the organisation 0; directions silent to the flux sector 53 of 53",
            CalculationId: "phase-sector-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_051", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-G_049", "ResearchY-G_048", "ResearchY-E_013"],
            AuditIds: ["g051"]),
        new("amplitude-phase-audit", "Amplitude Phase Audit", "Can rho be decomposed uniquely into an amplitude sector (42) and a phase sector (53)? DERIVED: the split is unique, orthogonal and exact, and the interface is an identity. Amplitude 42 + phase 53 = 95 with sector overlap 4.418E-015 and reconstruction at 2.442E-015; rebuilding the amplitude subspace from a different spanning set reproduces the projection to 3.349E-012; the contraction row space has rank 43 = the 42 amplitude modes plus the mean and is orthogonal to every phase mode (7.111E-014), so (phase) = kernel (53) and (amplitude) = row space minus the mean. Linear functionals split exactly (2.220E-016); AT's readings carry a cross term (clock 1.128E-006, acceleration 4.588E-007, field 2.812E-008) that scales as s-squared (0.2498 / 0.2503 / 0.2502), so the split is exact to first order and the residual is curvature.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-sector-audit", "kernel-structure-audit", "kernel-observable-audit", "rho-observable-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE SPLIT IS UNIQUE, ORTHOGONAL AND EXACT, AND THE INTERFACE IS AN IDENTITY RATHER THAN AN APPROXIMATION. Question: can rho be decomposed uniquely into an amplitude sector (42) and a phase sector (53), measured through orthogonality, invertibility, reconstruction accuracy and the clock, acceleration and field responses, and does every observable split into an amplitude plus a phase contribution? " +
            "(1) THE SPLIT EXISTS AND IS UNIQUE. The amplitude sector is the span of the 42 VISIBLE Fourier modes and the phase sector the span of the 53 HIDDEN ones; the two are orthogonal to 4.418E-015, they fill the 95 dimensions exactly, and adding the projections returns the state's deviation at 2.442E-015. Uniqueness is not inferred from orthogonality: the audit REBUILDS the amplitude subspace from a different deterministic spanning set and recomputes the projection, and the two agree to 3.349E-012 - so the decomposition is canonical rather than an artefact of the modal basis one happens to choose. " +
            "(2) THE INTERFACE IS AN EXACT IDENTITY, AND THIS IS THE ANSWER TO THE GOAL. The contraction observables span the simplex direction plus the amplitude sector and nothing else: the dimensions agree (43 = 43), every contraction row is orthogonal to every phase mode to 7.111E-014, and together those force the spans to be equal. So (phase sector) = kernel of the contraction observables (53 dimensions) and (amplitude sector) = the contractions' row space minus the mean (42 = 43 - 1), with 42 + 53 = 95. The interface is not described; it is the boundary itself, and it is computable. " +
            "(3) THE SPLIT OF AN OBSERVABLE IS A DIFFERENT QUESTION. A LINEAR functional splits exactly - the mean occupancy's additivity residual is 2.220E-016 - while AT's own readings do not, because the clock rate is a cube root of the occupancy and the field strength multiplies a nonlinear coupling by an occupancy difference. The audit measures the shortfall and then its ORDER: halving the step drops the clock cross term (1.128E-006) by a factor of four and the field one (2.812E-008) by four, so the discrepancy is SECOND ORDER - a curvature effect, not a failure of the decomposition. In the linear-response sense the split is exact for every observable. " +
            "(4) EVERY READING TAKES FROM BOTH SECTORS: the clock's amplitude contribution is 1.168E-003 against a phase contribution of 1.031E-003, and the acceleration's 3.464E-004 against 1.937E-004 - so the interface is a real partition of the response rather than a one-sided story. " +
            "(5) TWO HARNESS BUGS WERE CAUGHT BY THE MEASUREMENTS AND ARE RECORDED. The alternative spanning set used 30 combinations for a 42-dimensional subspace and could therefore never reproduce the projection, which measured 0.172 - a defect of the CHECK, not of the decomposition. And additivity was first measured on the MAXIMA of the responses, which is not additive even when every component is, producing a spurious first-order residual (0.499); it is now measured on the response VECTORS with an unclamped step, which gives the true 0.25. The audit also stopped routing the additivity steps through the perturbation helper, whose shift-and-rescale clamping makes the map nonlinear in the step. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED, with the honest qualification stated: rho decomposes uniquely into amplitude and phase, and the split of an observable is exact when the observable is linear and exact to first order otherwise. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the sector dimensions and overlap, the reconstruction residual, the basis-independence residual with its spanning-set rank, the interface dimensions and overlap, the linear additivity residual and the measured order of each cross term). RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_051 keep their verdicts; G_050's phase sector is now shown to be the exact kernel interface rather than merely a named set. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/AmplitudePhaseAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "amplitude 42 + phase 53 = state 95; sector overlap 4.418E-015; reconstruction residual 2.442E-015; basis-independence residual 3.349E-012 against a spanning set of rank 42; contraction row-space rank 43 = 42 amplitude modes + the mean; contraction-phase overlap 7.111E-014; linear additivity residual 2.220E-016; cross terms clock 1.128E-006, acceleration 4.588E-007, field 2.812E-008 with halving ratios 0.2498, 0.2503, 0.2502; contributions: clock amplitude 1.168E-003 vs phase 1.031E-003, acceleration 3.464E-004 vs 1.937E-004",
            CalculationId: "amplitude-phase-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_052", "ResearchY-G_051", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-G_047", "ResearchY-G_040"],
            AuditIds: ["g052"]),
        new("phase-sector-dynamics-audit", "Phase Sector Dynamics Audit", "Do phase modes have independent physical effects beyond amplitudes? DERIVED: yes, and the reason is geometric. The two perturbations are orthogonal (2.168E-018) and both move all three readings (clock 6.678E-003 vs 6.772E-003, acceleration 8.904E-004 vs 7.024E-004, field 1.128E-004 vs 9.971E-005), so independence is tested by imitation: projecting each reading's phase response onto the span of its responses to all 42 amplitude directions leaves a non-reproducible fraction of 1.0000 / 1.0000 / 0.9926. Geometrically an amplitude move leaves the probe channel's angle at machine zero (2.220E-015) while changing its magnitude by 3.464E-001, and a phase move turns the angle by 3.463E-001 - so the amplitude sector is exactly the no-rotation sector. The first uniquely phase-sensitive observable is the quadrature functional (2.000E-002 on the phase move against 3.272E-015 on every amplitude move).", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["amplitude-phase-audit", "phase-sector-audit", "kernel-structure-audit", "kernel-observable-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - PHASE MODES HAVE EFFECTS THAT NO AMPLITUDE MOVE REPRODUCES, AND THE REASON IS GEOMETRIC: THE AMPLITUDE SECTOR IS EXACTLY THE NO-ROTATION SECTOR AND THE PHASE SECTOR TURNS THE FOURIER CONTENT. Question: do phase modes have independent physical effects beyond amplitudes, and which observable is uniquely phase-sensitive? " +
            "(1) THE TWO PERTURBATIONS ARE ORTHOGONAL AND BOTH ARE REAL. A unit direction in the 42-mode visible span and one in the 53-mode hidden span overlap by 2.168E-018, and all three readings respond to both - the clock at 6.678E-003 and 6.772E-003, the acceleration at 8.904E-004 and 7.024E-004, the field at 1.128E-004 and 9.971E-005. So the question is NOT whether the phase is silent but whether its effect can be MIMICKED, which is what the audit tests. " +
            "(2) THE INDEPENDENCE TEST IS A REPRODUCIBILITY TEST. The audit builds the span of each reading's responses to ALL 42 amplitude directions - a span it verifies has rank 42 - projects the phase response onto it, and measures what is left: the non-reproducible fraction is 1.0000 for the clock, 1.0000 for the acceleration and 0.9926 for the field, so essentially all of the phase effect is unreachable from the amplitude sector. " +
            "(3) THE GEOMETRIC READING IS THE PHYSICAL ANSWER. In a channel's quadrature plane the amplitude move changes the magnitude by 3.464E-001 and the angle by 2.220E-015 - machine zero - while the phase move changes the angle by 3.463E-001 and the magnitude by 6.059E-002. The draft expected a clean resize-versus-rotate split with a factor of a hundred and the measurement is sharper in one place and weaker in another, so the criterion was corrected to what is measured; the sharp statement is that the amplitude sector is EXACTLY the no-rotation sector. The reason the phase move changes the magnitude at all is reported too: the state carries content in both quadratures of a populated channel, so adding to the hidden one lengthens the vector as well as turning it. " +
            "(4) THE FIRST UNIQUELY PHASE-SENSITIVE OBSERVABLE IS THE QUADRATURE FUNCTIONAL - the projection of the state onto a hidden mode. It is EXACTLY ZERO on every one of the 42 amplitude directions (3.272E-015) and non-zero on the phase direction (2.000E-002), and it is not an invented object: it is the coordinate G_050 named when it called the kernel the quadrature carrying each channel's phase. " +
            "(5) WHAT THE AUDIT DOES NOT CLAIM. AT's own laws are NOT uniquely phase-sensitive: the clock, acceleration and field readings each take a contribution from both sectors, so the observable that isolates the phase exactly is the quadrature projection rather than one of the theory's existing laws. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the perturbation overlap, the three response pairs, the amplitude-span rank, the three non-reproducible fractions, the channel geometry and the quadrature responses) and it has live branches: a reproducible phase effect would be BOUNDARY, and a failure of the geometry would remove the physical reading of the result. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_052 keep their verdicts; G_052's interface is now shown to separate two dynamically distinct sectors rather than two bookkeeping halves. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseSectorDynamicsAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "perturbation overlap 2.168E-018; responses clock 6.678E-003 vs 6.772E-003, acceleration 8.904E-004 vs 7.024E-004, field 1.128E-004 vs 9.971E-005; amplitude-response span rank 42 of 42; non-reproducible fractions 1.0000 (clock), 1.0000 (acceleration), 0.9926 (field); channel 1 amplitude magnitude change 3.464E-001 and angle change 2.220E-015; channel 1 phase angle change 3.463E-001 and magnitude change 6.059E-002; quadrature functional response 2.000E-002 on the phase move against 3.272E-015 on every amplitude move",
            CalculationId: "phase-sector-dynamics-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_053", "ResearchY-G_052", "ResearchY-G_051", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-G_047"],
            AuditIds: ["g053"]),
        new("phase-determination-audit", "Phase Determination Audit", "What fixes the 53 phase coordinates? BOUNDARY - freely assigned. The conservation theorem disposes of two candidates at once: invariant gradients lie in the amplitude-plus-mean subspace (G_052), so an invariant-driven flow cannot change the phase coordinates (1.431E-015). Symmetry does not fix them - its invariants ARE the amplitudes plus the mean, so a symmetry move changes them by 2.540E-001 while an amplitude move changes them by 3.232E-015. The clock and field functionals are phase-sensitive (gradient phase fractions 3.768E-003 and 8.572E-002), but no AT process runs such a flow (spatial part 0.000E+000, coupling census 0). Multiplicity fails because the 45-level spectrum is Laplacian-fixed, not state-dependent.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-sector-dynamics-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit", "phase-sector-audit", "flux-population-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - FREELY ASSIGNED: NOTHING IN AT FIXES THE 53 PHASE COORDINATES, AND THE AUDIT STATES EXACTLY WHAT WOULD HAVE TO BE ADDED. Question: what fixes the phase coordinates, and is the phase sector dynamically determined or freely assigned? Candidates: symmetry, occupancy, multiplicity, attractor structure, actualization history, boundary assignment. " +
            "(1) THE CONSERVATION THEOREM DISPOSES OF TWO CANDIDATES AT ONCE. The contraction functionals are invariant, so their gradients lie in the invariant subspace, which G_052 measured to be exactly the amplitude modes plus the mean. A flow along such a gradient can therefore never leave that subspace: the phase coordinates are CONSTANTS OF THE MOTION of any invariant-driven dynamics - measured at 1.431E-015, with an invariant gradient's phase component at 7.625E-012. The reachable structure and the actualization history both amount to flows of that kind, so neither can pin the phases. " +
            "(2) SYMMETRY DOES NOT FIX THE COORDINATES - IT IS DEFINED BY NOT SEEING THEM. The invariants of the substrate's symmetry are the amplitude modes plus the mean, so the phase coordinates are precisely its non-invariant content: a symmetry move changes them by 2.540E-001, while an amplitude move changes them by 3.232E-015 by orthogonality. " +
            "(3) SENSITIVITY IS NOT DETERMINATION, AND BOTH HALVES ARE MEASURED SEPARATELY. The clock functional's gradient carries a phase fraction of 3.768E-003 and the field functional's 8.572E-002, so a process that extremised either law WOULD move the phase coordinates - but no AT process does: the update rule's spatial part is 0.000E+000 and the census of members coupling the link sector to the organisation is 0, which E_009 and E_013 established and this audit re-measures. " +
            "(4) MULTIPLICITY FAILS FOR A BLUNTER REASON. The substrate's spectrum is the recorded one - 45 levels, 96 modes - and is fixed by the Laplacian rather than by the state, so the degenerate structure cannot pin 53 state-dependent numbers. The audit also refuses to count the one determination that is trivially true: the addressed state determines its own projections, which is a tautology rather than a mechanism, and is recorded as such. " +
            "(5) WHAT REMAINS IS BOUNDARY ASSIGNMENT, and it is the answer: the phase coordinates are an assignment, the same shape of answer the flux sector label received in E_014, with one difference worth stating - there the assignment was inert and here it is physically ACTIVE, since G_051 and G_053 showed the laws genuinely depend on it. " +
            "(6) A BUG WAS CAUGHT BY THE MEASUREMENT. DerivedSectorSplit returns ELECTRIC first and the audit's accessor read it as the SPATIAL part, which made the update rule look as though it carried a spatial field (1.424E-002) and flipped the verdict to DERIVED; the spatial part is genuinely 0.000E+000, and the mislabelling is recorded rather than quietly corrected. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the phase-coordinate changes under amplitude and symmetry moves, the invariant-flow change and its gradient's phase component, the two law gradients' phase fractions, the update-rule split, the coupling census and the spectrum) and it has live branches: an AT process coupling to the phases would make the determination DERIVED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_053 keep their verdicts; the phase sector's status is now complete - named, physical, independent and freely assigned. The four requirements are checked in the suite: no new primitive, and the clock, acceleration and field laws preserved (read, not modified). G-group registry gains this audit as a Boundary claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseDeterminationAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase coordinates 53; amplitude moves change them by 3.232E-015; symmetry moves by 2.540E-001; invariant-driven flow by 1.431E-015 (invariant gradient's phase component 7.625E-012); clock functional phase fraction 3.768E-003; field functional phase fraction 8.572E-002; update rule spatial part 0.000E+000; coupling census 0; spectrum 45 levels, 96 modes",
            CalculationId: "phase-determination-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-G_053", "ResearchY-G_052", "ResearchY-G_051", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-E_014"],
            AuditIds: ["g054"]),
        new("phase-selection-principle-audit", "Phase Selection Principle Audit", "Can any existing AT quantity assign a preferred phase state? BOUNDARY: none can, and the deficiency is measured. A scalar functional's gradient is one vector, so it constrains at most one phase direction; six candidates measure a constraint rank of 3, leaving 50 of the 53 phase directions free. Three candidates constrain nothing at all - free room (the simplex constraint, projection 3.952E-014), actualization density (its scalar level, 4.104E-016) and the flux sector (decoupled, 0.000E+000) - while entropy (3.334E-004), the clock functional (1.241E-002) and the field functional (1.678E-003) each contribute one direction. No sensitive candidate is stationary at the audited state, so nothing is extremised either.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-determination-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit", "phase-sector-audit", "sector-weight-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - NO EXISTING AT QUANTITY CAN ASSIGN A PREFERRED PHASE STATE, AND THE AUDIT MEASURES EXACTLY HOW MUCH OF THE PHASE SECTOR IS LEFT FREE. Question: does any of entropy, free room, actualization density, the flux sector, the clock functional and the field functional break the phase degeneracy, and why this phase instead of another? " +
            "(1) THE COUNTING ARGUMENT IS THE WHOLE AUDIT AND IT IS EXACT. A quantity that could assign a preferred phase must be a SCALAR functional, and the gradient of a scalar is ONE vector, whose projection into the 53-dimensional phase sector therefore constrains AT MOST ONE phase direction. Six candidates cannot pin 53 directions however they are combined, and the bound is measured rather than assumed: the rank is 3, so the DEFICIENCY is 50 directions that no combination of these quantities can ever constrain. " +
            "(2) THREE OF THE SIX CONSTRAIN NOTHING AT ALL, which is a stronger statement than weakness. Free room is the simplex constraint, whose gradient is the constant direction - and the constant is the simplex direction, orthogonal to every non-constant mode, so its phase projection is zero (3.952E-014, the mode-sum floor rather than a value). The flux sector is decoupled from the organisation altogether, with a coupling census of 0. The actualization density's scalar level is that same constant. " +
            "(3) THE OTHER THREE DO CONTRIBUTE, each along ONE direction: entropy 3.334E-004, the clock functional 1.241E-002 and the field functional 1.678E-003. The phase sector is therefore not uniformly unselectable; it is unselectable in all but a measured handful of directions. " +
            "(4) THE CRITICAL QUESTION IS ANSWERED IN ITS OWN TERMS. Asked why this phase instead of another, the theory has no answer for the 50 unconstrained directions, because nothing it contains is sensitive to them; for the directions the candidates do see, the answer would be that the quantity is extremal there - and the audit tests whether the audited state is a critical point. It is not: the largest phase directional derivatives are 2.808E-004 (entropy), 1.038E-002 (clock) and 6.252E-004 (field), all non-zero, so nothing is extremised at this state either. " +
            "(5) WHAT WOULD BREAK THE DEGENERACY is stated positively: a set of 53 independent scalar functionals, or one non-scalar structure whose gradient spans the phase sector. AT has neither, which is why the answer is a BOUNDARY with a number attached rather than a shrug. " +
            "(6) THREE DEFECTS WERE CAUGHT BY THE MEASUREMENTS AND ARE RECORDED. The first is a cancellation: free room's gradient is exactly the constant direction, yet differencing a functional of order 96 with a step of 1E-6 leaves a floor of 2.540E-008 and made a phase-BLIND candidate look phase-sensitive - the gradients are now ANALYTIC where they are trivial (free room, actualization density, flux, clock) and differenced only where genuinely nonlinear, with the step raised to 1E-4. The second is the exact-zero floor, now stated with its origin: the zeros sit at about 4E-14 because a phase mode's own sum vanishes only to about 1E-16 and is multiplied by 96 unit components, so the 1E-9 classification threshold is six orders above the floor and four below the smallest genuine response. The third is a delegate-identity bug: locating a candidate by ReferenceEquals on its method group threw immediately, since a method group converts to a new delegate on every evaluation, and the lookup is now by name. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the six phase projections with their classes, the measured constraint rank against the counting bound, the deficiency, and the directional derivatives that decide criticality) and it has live branches: a rank reaching 53 would make a preferred phase DERIVED, and a rank of zero would REFUTE the question as void. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_054 keep their verdicts; G_054's free assignment is now quantitative rather than qualitative. G-group registry gains this audit as a Boundary claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseSelectionPrincipleAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimensions 53; candidates 6; phase projection norms: entropy 3.334E-004, free room 3.952E-014, actualization density 4.104E-016, flux sector 0.000E+000, clock functional 1.241E-002, field functional 1.678E-003; constrained directions 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1; measured constraint rank 3; deficiency 50; largest phase directional derivatives 2.808E-004, 4.263E-010, 4.441E-012, 0.000E+000, 1.038E-002, 6.252E-004; exact-zero floor about 4E-14",
            CalculationId: "phase-selection-principle-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_055", "ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-G_052", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-E_015"],
            AuditIds: ["g055"]),
        new("non-scalar-selection-audit", "Non-Scalar Selection Audit", "Can any existing non-scalar AT structure span the 53-dimensional phase sector? DERIVED: the gradient-based structures do. The phase rank - the rank of a structure's derivative along the 53 phase directions - is 53 for the occupancy-gradient vector field, the connection AT builds from it and the T1/T2 sector coupling, against G_055's scalar ceiling of 3, a factor of 17. The reason is structural: differentiation is injective on every non-constant mode, and the phase sector contains only non-constant modes (53 of 53 directions have a non-zero derivative). The edge-holonomy network read from the link phases is decoupled (census 0) and the causal-order tensor from signs is piecewise constant, so both measure 0. Spanning is sensitivity, not determination: no AT process runs such a flow, so the phases remain freely assigned.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-selection-principle-audit", "phase-determination-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit", "field-excitation-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE PHASE SECTOR IS SPANNED IN FULL BY AN EXISTING AT STRUCTURE, WHICH OVERTURNS G_055's CEILING WITHOUT OVERTURNING ITS CONCLUSION. Question: can any non-scalar AT structure span the 53-dimensional phase sector, among the phase vector field, the connection structure, the T1/T2 sector coupling, the edge-holonomy network and the causal-order tensor? " +
            "(1) THE MEASUREMENT IS THE PHASE RANK. The rank of a structure's derivative along the 53 phase directions generalises G_055's count exactly: a scalar has one output so its rank cannot exceed 1, whereas a structure with m outputs reaches the smaller of m and 53. G_055's scalar ceiling of 3 is the bar to clear. " +
            "(2) THE GRADIENT-BASED CANDIDATES REACH THE FULL RANK. The occupancy-gradient vector field, the connection AT builds from it and the T1/T2 sector coupling all measure 53 of 53, a factor of 17 above the ceiling, and the reason is STRUCTURAL rather than numerical: differentiation is injective on every non-constant mode and the phase sector contains only non-constant modes - measured as 53 of 53 phase directions with a non-zero derivative - so a field built from differences necessarily sees all of them. " +
            "(3) THE DECOUPLED AND PIECEWISE-CONSTANT CANDIDATES REACH ZERO AND ARE REPORTED RATHER THAN OMITTED. The edge-holonomy network read from the LINK phases is decoupled from the organisation, with a census of zero, so it cannot see a phase at all; the audit also notes that the holonomy built from the occupancy-derived connection is not a sixth route but the connection candidate under another name. The causal-order tensor, built from the sign of occupancy differences, is piecewise constant, so its derivative vanishes almost everywhere - an order structure cannot span a continuous sector. " +
            "(4) TWO HONESTY NOTES ARE RECORDED. The coupling's T1 half vanishes identically (measured norm 0.000E+000, because the two shifts commute), so its rank comes from the symmetric half: a candidate whose antisymmetric half is zero is weaker than its name suggests. And the candidate table carries NO VERDICT LITERALS - each verdict is computed from the measured rank against the ceiling, as this project's rule 6 requires. " +
            "(5) SPANNING IS NOT SELECTING, AND THIS IS THE CLAUSE THAT KEEPS THE SERIES CONSISTENT. A phase rank of 53 says the structure WOULD move if a process drove it; G_054 measured that no AT process does, with an update-rule spatial part of zero and a coupling census of zero. So the phases remain freely assigned exactly as G_054 concluded, and what changes is the reason the audit can give for G_055's deficiency: it was a deficiency of SCALARS, not of AT. AT contains structures sensitive to every phase direction and runs none of them. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the five measured phase ranks, the comparison with G_055's ceiling, the injectivity measurement and the T1 norm) and it has live branches: a largest rank at or below the ceiling would be REFUTED, and a rank above the ceiling but below 53 would be BOUNDARY. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_055 keep their verdicts; G_055's deficiency is explained rather than contradicted, and G_054's free assignment stands. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/NonScalarSelectionAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimensions 53; scalar ceiling (G_055) 3; phase ranks: phase vector field 53 (96 outputs), connection structure 53 (96), T1/T2 sector coupling 53 (288), edge-holonomy network 0, causal-order tensor 0; phase directions with a non-zero derivative 53 of 53; coupling T1-half norm 0.000E+000; no AT process runs a phase flow (True)",
            CalculationId: "non-scalar-selection-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_056", "ResearchY-G_055", "ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-G_052", "ResearchY-E_013"],
            AuditIds: ["g056"]),
        new("residual-phase-audit", "Residual Phase Audit", "What is special about the 11 unreachable phase directions? DERIVED: they are not special directions of the substrate at all - they are the modes the canonical state does not occupy, and the split is a property of shift-invariance. The kernel relation is exact: a contraction row is A_d rho with A_d the distance-d relation, and A_d is circulant, so on a single mode e of channel c it acts as lambda_d(c) times the state's content in e, with lambda_0(c) = 1; hence hidden if and only if zero occupancy, measured over all 95 non-constant modes. Occupied modes 42, occupied span 43, kernel 53. The eleven are channels 14, 19, 24, 32, 40 (both quadratures each) plus the alternating mode. The accounting closes 7 + 4 = 11 with disjoint parts: the substrate has 45 levels and Sigma(m-1) = 51 modes are empty for any one-vector-per-level state (the free room); only two levels are degenerate - index 13, eigenvalue 12.0, multiplicity 5, channels 16, 32, 48, and index 35, eigenvalue 14.0, multiplicity 6, channels 8, 24, 40 - leaving 9 modes empty of which 7 are in the eleven; and two levels carry a construction weight of exactly zero (indices 8, 31), emptying channels 14 and 19 in both quadratures: 4 more. Reachability was measured on both halves: the difference and centred difference are circulant (projection 9.512E-015 and 3.675E-015, rank 0), while the connection h(rho) Delta rho and the T1/T2 coupling are state-dependent and reach all eleven (projection 2.968E-003 and 1.455E-001, rank 11). Rebuilding from the last basis vector of each level moves the set to channels 8, 14, 16, 19, 24, 32 and 12 directions, so the eleven are not substrate-invariant; only the degeneracy count of 51 modes is. The symmetry group has order 192, the eleven form an invariant set as a span, the alternating mode's orbit is 2 and channel 32's cosine has orbit 3.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-evolution-audit", "kernel-structure-audit", "rho-observable-audit", "phase-dynamics-closure-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE ELEVEN UNREACHABLE PHASE DIRECTIONS ARE NOT SPECIAL DIRECTIONS OF THE SUBSTRATE AT ALL, AND THE SPLIT IS SHIFT-INVARIANCE. Question: what is special about the 11 unreachable phase directions of G_060 - identify the alternating mode, the empty channels, the kernel relation and the symmetry properties, test whether any existing AT operator can reach them, and explain the 53 = 42 + 11 split? " +
            "(1) THE KERNEL RELATION IS EXACT RATHER THAN APPROXIMATE. A contraction row is A_d rho with A_d the distance-d relation on the ring, and A_d is CIRCULANT, so on a single Fourier mode e of channel c the row acts as <A_d rho, e> = lambda_d(c) <rho, e> with lambda_0(c) = 1 because the identity is one of the distance classes. The row therefore vanishes on e EXACTLY when the state has no content in it. Measured over all 95 non-constant modes, hidden if and only if zero occupancy. So the phase directions are hidden not because the contractions are blind to them but because the STATE says nothing about them, and the kernel of 53 is the orthogonal complement of the state's 43-dimensional span (the mean plus 42 occupied modes). " +
            "(2) WHY THE STATE OCCUPIES ONE MODE PER LEVEL, AND WHY ELEVEN ARE LEFT. The canonical state takes exactly ONE basis vector per level, always basis[0], so a level of multiplicity m receives content in one of its modes and leaves m-1 empty. Summed over the substrate's 45 levels that forces Sigma(m-1) = 51 empty modes - the free room, 96 minus 45 - for ANY state built this way. Only two levels are degenerate: index 13 with eigenvalue 12.0, multiplicity 5 and channels 16, 32, 48, and index 35 with eigenvalue 14.0, multiplicity 6 and channels 8, 24, 40. Those two leave 9 modes empty, and 7 of the eleven lie among them - the six quadratures of channels 32, 24 and 40 plus the alternating mode - while the other two fall in channels the level does occupy and are among the 42. Two further levels carry a CONSTRUCTION WEIGHT OF EXACTLY ZERO (indices 8 and 31), which empties their channels 14 and 19 in BOTH quadratures: four more directions. Seven plus four is eleven, and the parts are disjoint because channels 14 and 19 are not in a degenerate level. " +
            "(3) CAN AN EXISTING AT OPERATOR REACH THEM? YES AND NO, AND BOTH HALVES ARE MEASURED RATHER THAN ARGUED. A circulant operator is diagonal in the Fourier basis and can never mix channels: from the state's own span it reaches each occupied channel's other quadrature (42) and can never enter a channel the state does not occupy - the difference and the centred difference give projection 9.512E-015 and 3.675E-015 with rank 0. AT's state-dependent operators are NOT circulant: the connection it builds is a MULTIPLICATION by h(rho) composed with the difference, and multiplication by a non-constant function DOES mix channels - the connection and the T1/T2 coupling give projection 2.968E-003 and 1.455E-001 with rank 11, reaching every one of the eleven. " +
            "(4) THE DECISIVE EXPERIMENT, AND THE ELEVEN MOVE. Rebuilding the same construction from the LAST basis vector of each level rather than the first gives empty channels 8, 14, 16, 19, 24, 32 and 12 directions, because the alternating mode becomes occupied and channels 8, 16, 24 and 32 lose their content. So the eleven are NOT substrate-invariant: they are coordinates rather than structure. What IS invariant is the count the degeneracy forces - 51 modes empty for any such state - while the two extra come from a weight that vanishes, which is a property of a CHOSEN FORMULA rather than of the substrate. " +
            "(5) SYMMETRY. The group has order 192; the eleven form a symmetry-invariant set AS A SPAN (a rotation carries a mode into a combination of its quadratures, so the test must be a span test - a first version compared images with the eleven VECTORS and reported False); the alternating mode's orbit is the smallest at 2, because a shift by two fixes it, and channel 32's cosine has orbit 3, because its rotation angle is 2*pi/3. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the occupancy of every mode, the kernel dimension against the occupied span, the level multiset and the construction weights, the four operator responses with their ranks, and the alternative construction) and it has live branches: an operator that IS circulant reaching any of the eleven would be BOUNDARY, and an accounting that did not close would be REFUTED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_060 keep their verdicts; G_060's 42-of-53 is explained as shift-invariance, and G_050's phase sector is identified with the state's orthogonal complement. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/ResidualPhaseAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimension 53; the eleven = channels 14, 19, 24, 32, 40 (both quadratures each) plus the alternating mode (channel 48); every occupancy at the 1E-15 floor; hidden iff zero occupancy = True over all 95 non-constant modes; occupied modes 42, occupied span 43, kernel 53, sum 96; levels 45, Sigma(m-1) = 51; degenerate levels index 13 (eigenvalue 12.0, multiplicity 5, channels 16, 32, 48) and index 35 (eigenvalue 14.0, multiplicity 6, channels 8, 24, 40); vanishing construction weights at level indices 8 and 31 giving channels 14 and 19; accounting 7 from degeneracy + 4 from vanishing weights = 11, disjoint; reaches: difference 9.512E-015 rank 0, centred difference 3.675E-015 rank 0, connection 2.968E-003 rank 11, T1/T2 coupling 1.455E-001 rank 11; alternative state basis[^1] empty channels 8, 14, 16, 19, 24, 32 and 12 directions; symmetry group order 192, eleven invariant as a span, alternating mode orbit 2, channel 32 cosine orbit 3",
            CalculationId: "residual-phase-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_061", "ResearchY-G_060", "ResearchY-G_050", "ResearchY-G_040", "ResearchY-G_046"],
            AuditIds: ["g061"]),
        new("phase-evolution-audit", "Phase Evolution Audit", "Can the difference-generated phase push be promoted to an actual update rule? DERIVED: the promotion exists and it is the norm-preserving form, while the form the question names is the one that fails. Every candidate is circulant, so one complex multiplier per channel is the whole update. rho + eps*D*rho has |mu|^2 = 1 - 2 eps x (1 - eps), so its symmetric part is negative semi-definite: it is dissipative, and its attractor is the constant - measured, the deviation norm falls 1.005E+000 to 2.424E-001 over 20000 steps, so the flow reaches the phase-free state. The phase survives only where |mu| = 1: the backward difference (1.000002..1.002000) and the centred difference (1.000000..1.000001) amplify every non-constant mode and leave the simplex in a measured number of steps; the difference's own exact flow exp(eps D) contracts; and the unitary form (the exact flow of the centred difference) has |mu| = 1.000000000 exactly, sustaining all 42 reachable phase directions while conserving the deviation norm (1.005011E+000) and the sum and keeping every cell positive over 20000 steps. The reachable rank is 42 of 53 by two independent routes, and the 11 unreachable directions are channels 14, 19, 24, 32, 40 (both quadratures) and the alternating mode, which the centred difference annihilates so that form's fixed-point set is 2-dimensional. The positivity guard never fires (agreement to 5E-15 with the unclipped step).", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["flow-source-audit", "phase-dynamics-closure-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit", "kernel-structure-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE PROMOTION EXISTS, AND IT IS THE NORM-PRESERVING FORM; THE FORM THE QUESTION NAMES IS THE ONE THAT FAILS. Question: can the difference-generated phase push (G_059) be promoted to an actual update rule - testing rho(t+1) = rho(t) + eps*D*rho and five other AT-native forms - and does any AT-native update generate non-trivial phase dynamics? " +
            "(1) EVERY CANDIDATE IS CIRCULANT, SO NOTHING IS ESTIMATED. The difference is a function of the shift, so each update is diagonal in the Fourier basis with one complex multiplier per channel; the audit drives its analysis, its iteration, its stability and its reachable rank from that number, and it computes the rank twice - per channel and by a Krylov scan - with the routes agreeing. " +
            "(2) THE QUESTION'S OWN UPDATE IS STABLE, AND THAT IS WHY IT FAILS. rho + eps*D*rho has |mu|^2 = 1 - 2 eps x(1 - eps) with x = 1 - cos delta_c, so it contracts for 0 < eps < 1: the difference's symmetric part is negative semi-definite, making this a DISSIPATIVE step rather than the skew step its name suggests. Its attractor is the kernel of D, which is the CONSTANT. Measured over 20000 steps the deviation norm falls from 1.005E+000 to 2.424E-001, so the flow is attracted exactly to the phase-free state - the closure with G_059, whose canonical state has no phase content because this is where the flow stops. " +
            "(3) A CLAIM IS WITHDRAWN. A first draft asserted that the phase content decays monotonically. Measured, it OSCILLATES on the way down - 0.065 at 100 steps and 0.303 at 1000 while the envelope keeps falling - so the audit reports the deviation norm as the envelope and the phase content as the oscillation. " +
            "(4) THE PHASE SURVIVES ONLY WHERE |mu| = 1, AND EXACTLY ONE FORM HAS IT. The backward difference (1.000002 .. 1.002000) and the centred difference (1.000000 .. 1.000001) amplify every non-constant mode and leave the simplex in measured numbers of steps (backward: 796, 80 and 9 at eps = 1E-3, 1E-2 and 1E-1); the difference's own exact flow exp(eps D) contracts like the forward step; and the UNITARY form - the exact flow of the CENTRED difference - has |mu| = 1.000000000 exactly, sustains all 42 phase directions, conserves the deviation norm exactly (1.005011E+000 at every horizon tested) and the sum, and keeps every cell positive over 20000 steps at every eps tested. " +
            "(5) THE RANK IS BOUNDED BY THE SUBSTRATE AT 42 OF 53. A circulant update cannot mix a quadrature pair with the constant, so from a phase-free state it can only reach a channel's OTHER quadrature: the 42 half-hidden channels give 42, and the 11 directions left are the DOUBLY-HIDDEN channels 14, 19, 24, 32 and 40 (both quadratures - no visible quadrature at all, so a phase-free state has nothing there to act on) plus the ALTERNATING MODE, a channel with no partner quadrature that every circulant merely rescales. No update of this family can reach them at any step size. " +
            "(6) FIXED POINTS ARE COUNTED IN MODES. The constant is fixed by every form; the CENTRED family additionally fixes the ALTERNATING MODE, because (S - S^-1) e_48 = 0, so those forms have a 2-dimensional fixed-point set and one of the eleven unreachable directions is in their kernel; and the control - the actualization, which supplies no rho-generator at all - fixes all 96. A first version counted CHANNELS and reported 49 for the identity, which moves nothing. " +
            "(7) THREE DEFECTS ARE RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. The AT-native positivity guard, carried because rho is a density, divided by the clipped mean and exploded where the clip removed most of the state, and it annihilated a zero-mean probe outright - a defect in the PROBE, not a finding about AT, since feeding a density guard a deviation is not a state; it now restores the mass by a bounded uniform shift. The rank scan counted 63 and then 54 directions inside a 53-dimensional space, because a Gram-Schmidt residual on nearly dependent vectors is not a reliable rank in a 96-dimensional state space and a relative gate is tighter than the arithmetic; it is now taken in the phase sector's own coordinates. And the difference-of-orbits construction carries a MEASURED 2.329E-008 relative leak into the unreachable directions, identical for the linear and the clipped update - which is how the audit knows the leak is its own arithmetic - so reachability is measured from the LINEAR response, which has no such floor. The guard's inactivity is itself measured: its orbit agrees with the unclipped step to 5E-15, with minimum cell 7.086E-001 over 4000 steps. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the multipliers and their moduli, the stability split over the phase-bearing channels, the two rank routes, the fixed-point dimensions and the simplex budgets) and it has live branches: no update generating phase dynamics would be REFUTED, and a stable sustaining form that fails the simplex would be BOUNDARY. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_059 keep their verdicts; G_059's phase-free canonical state is explained as the attractor of the stable difference flow, and G_057's phase-static process is unaffected because the actualization still supplies no generator. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseEvolutionAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimension 53; updates and their |mu| at eps = 1E-3 (min .. max): forward difference 0.998000000 .. 0.999997861; backward difference 1.000002143 .. 1.002000000; centred (skew) difference 1.000000000 .. 1.000000500; exact flow exp(eps D) 0.998001999 .. 0.999997859; unitary (Cayley of the skew part) 1.000000000 .. 1.000000000; positivity-clipped difference 0.998000000 .. 0.999997861; actualization control 1.000000000; reachable phase rank 42 of 53 by two independent routes for every difference form and 0 for the control; reachable amplitude rank 42; unreachable 11 = channels 14, 19, 24, 32, 40 (both quadratures) plus the alternating mode; forward step deviation norm 1.005E+000 -> 2.424E-001 over 20000 steps; unitary deviation norm conserved at 1.005011E+000; unitary minimum cell over 20000 steps 0.693 .. 0.770; backward difference off-simplex after 796 / 80 / 9 steps at eps = 1E-3 / 1E-2 / 1E-1; centred difference off-simplex after 399 steps at eps = 1E-1; fixed-point dimensions 1 (constant), 2 (constant + alternating mode for the centred family), 96 (control); positivity guard agreement with the unclipped step 5E-15; difference-of-orbits leak 2.329E-008",
            CalculationId: "phase-evolution-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_060", "ResearchY-G_059", "ResearchY-G_058", "ResearchY-G_057", "ResearchY-G_052"],
            AuditIds: ["g060"]),
        new("flow-source-audit", "Flow Source Audit", "What AT object can produce a non-zero push rank? DERIVED: the source is the DIFFERENCE ITSELF, and it is derived rather than argued. The cyclic difference's Fourier multiplier is 1 - e^(-i delta_c), so its action on a single visible mode returns exactly the multiset {|sin delta_c|, 2 sin^2(delta_c/2)} - one amplitude part, one phase part, no third term - verified on all 42 visible modes to 1E-12. The phase share is cot(delta_c/2): phase-heavy at channel 1 (30.6:1), amplitude-heavy at channel 47 (0.033:1), residue range 2.141E-003 .. 1.998E+000. A filter cannot create phase content at all, because its multiplier is real and symmetric under c -> -c. The canonical state has no phase content (9.246E-015, the floor), so the phase sector is where a source SENDS the state; that explains G_054's excluded tautology and names G_052's reconstruction residual as the phase part itself. Three candidates create phase content and are fixed only at the uniform state; three only amplify and move exactly the phase-bearing states. No candidate is a pure phase source and no two coincide. G_057's recorded 0.000E+000 is returned from two side conditions rather than measured; the uniform reading is 0.000E+000 so its conclusion holds, while the local clock-rate reading is 6.969E-003.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-dynamics-closure-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit", "phase-flow-audit", "kernel-structure-audit"],
            Narrative: "DERIVED - THE SOURCE IS THE DIFFERENCE ITSELF, AND IT IS DERIVED RATHER THAN ARGUED. Question: what AT object can produce a non-zero push rank, among occupancy imbalance, phase imbalance, amplitude-phase coupling, actualization pressure, spectral mismatch and boundary assignment? Given G_058 that all admissible dynamics have identical local rank, so a rank cannot separate them. " +
            "(1) THE MEASURE IS THE PUSH VECTOR, NOT A RANK. A candidate is a source when its push - a direction in the 96-dimensional state space - has a non-zero PHASE part, split by G_052's identity into mean, amplitude and phase. The phase floor is 1E-9. " +
            "(2) THE CANONICAL STATE HAS NO PHASE CONTENT: 9.246E-015, the floating-point floor, so it lies in the mean-plus-visible span. The phase sector is therefore not where the state IS but where a source SENDS it. This explains what G_054 recorded and refused to count - its addressed-state determination was a tautology because the phase coordinates are zero, so the statement was 0 = 0 - and it names G_052's own reconstruction residual (2.442E-015) as the phase part itself. " +
            "(3) THE MECHANISM IS EXACT RATHER THAN QUALITATIVE. A cyclic difference is circulant, so it is diagonal in the Fourier basis with multiplier 1 - e^(-i delta_c), delta_c = 2 pi c / 96: a rotation COMPOSED WITH A RESCALE. Its action on a single visible mode returns exactly the multiset {|sin delta_c|, 2 sin^2(delta_c/2)} - one amplitude part, one phase part, no third term - and the audit tests this against all 42 visible modes, where it holds to 1E-12. The phase share is cot(delta_c/2), so the difference is a phase source at channel 1 (30.6 to 1) and an amplitude source at channel 47 (0.033 to 1). A FILTER cannot create phase content at all: a real, c-symmetric multiplier is exactly what preserves the visible subspace, which is why the filter-shaped candidates measure at the floor. " +
            "(4) A CLAIM IS WITHDRAWN. The first draft called the difference a PURE rotation carrying the visible sector into the phase sector with no residue. The measurement refused it: the residue reaches 1.998E+000, the near-maximum 2 sin^2(delta/2), at channel 47. The exact multiset replaced the claim. " +
            "(5) CREATING AND AMPLIFYING ARE SEPARATED BY MEASUREMENT over a 192-state deterministic family. Three candidates CREATE phase content from any non-uniform state - occupancy imbalance, the local clock-rate reading of the actualization pressure, and the seam pair - and their only fixed point is the uniform state (191 of 192 states moved). Three only AMPLIFY it - phase imbalance, the amplitude-phase coupling, the spectral mismatch - and they move exactly the 106 phase-bearing states and no others. At the canonical state only the three creating sources push. " +
            "(6) NO CANDIDATE IS A PURE PHASE SOURCE: every one that pushes the phase pushes amplitude as well, the phase-heaviest being the boundary assignment at a ratio of 7.296E-001. No two candidates coincide (0 degenerate pairs), so the six names describe distinct directions. " +
            "(7) THE ACTUALIZATION'S ACCOUNTING IS CORRECTED RATHER THAN CITED, AND G_057'S CONCLUSION SURVIVES ITS OWN REASON. G_057 recorded the actualization's phase velocity as 0.000E+000, but its implementation returns that value from two SIDE CONDITIONS - the update rule's spatial part is zero and the coupling census is zero - and never measures the phase content of the time-like component it names, so the number was true of a quantity it did not measure (project rule 5). Measured directly, the uniform reading is 0.000E+000, because every phase mode sums to zero: G_057's conclusion holds. But the local clock-rate reading of the same pressure measures 6.969E-003, which is not a floor, and AT defines no update rule for the organisation at all - so it is the IDENTIFICATION of the pressure that carries the weight. The number survives; the reason for it does not. " +
            "OUTPUT: DERIVED. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the push table with its phase parts, the exact multiplier identity on 42 visible modes, the creating/amplifying fixed-point counts, the degeneracy scan and the re-measured G_057 pair) and it has live branches: no candidate with a non-zero push would be REFUTED, and only a reading of the running rule pushing the phase would be BOUNDARY. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_058 keep their verdicts; G_058's rank criterion is replaced as a measure without being contradicted, and G_057's conclusion stands on a corrected reason. G-group registry gains this audit as a Derived claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/FlowSourceAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimensions 53; phase floor 1E-9; push vector per candidate (|push| / phase / amplitude / rank): occupancy imbalance 1.368E+000 / 7.155E-001 / 1.166E+000 / 1; phase imbalance 9.246E-015 / 9.246E-015 / 6.391E-029 / 0; amplitude-phase coupling 8.295E-016 / 7.000E-016 / 4.450E-016 / 0; actualization uniform 9.798E+000 / 0.000E+000 / 0.000E+000 / 0; actualization local rate 3.407E-001 / 6.969E-003 / 3.407E-001 / 1; spectral mismatch 2.572E-002 / 2.388E-016 / 2.572E-002 / 0; boundary assignment 1.575E-002 / 9.282E-003 / 1.272E-002 / 1; difference multiplier 1 - e^(-i delta_c) with delta_c = 2 pi c / 96 returns {|sin delta_c|, 2 sin^2(delta_c/2)} exactly on 42 of 42 visible modes; residue range 2.141E-003 .. 1.998E+000; most phase-heavy channel 1, most amplitude-heavy channel 47; canonical state phase content 9.246E-015; family 192 states, creating sources fixed only at the uniform state, amplifiers move exactly the 106 phase-bearing states; largest phase/amplitude ratio 7.296E-001; 0 degenerate pairs; G_057 recorded 0.000E+000 from side conditions, uniform reading 0.000E+000, local clock-rate reading 6.969E-003",
            CalculationId: "flow-source-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_059", "ResearchY-G_058", "ResearchY-G_057", "ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-G_052"],
            AuditIds: ["g059"]),
        new("phase-dynamics-closure-audit", "Phase Dynamics Closure Audit", "Can any AT update rule generate a non-trivial phase evolution? BOUNDARY: the requested measure cannot discriminate - the linearisation and operator ranks are 53 for EVERY rule tested, the do-nothing identity included, while the push rank is 1 for any rule that moves and 0 for the process AT actually runs. All five candidates (single scalar flow, multiple coupled scalar flows, vector-valued flow, connection-driven flow, T1/T2 coupling) have push rank 1, and coupling several scalar flows does not help because a sum of gradients is one vector. The linearisation is full for every generator - a scalar flow's linearisation is its potential's Hessian, positive definite and full rank on every subspace - and the operator is full even for the identity, which is invertible on the phase sector. The actualization has no spatial generator (spatial part 0.000E+000, census 0), so its push rank is 0. An expected hierarchy (vector generators at 53, scalar rules at 1) is REFUTED: no rank measure separates them.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["phase-flow-audit", "non-scalar-selection-audit", "phase-determination-audit", "amplitude-phase-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - THE REQUESTED CRITERION CANNOT DISCRIMINATE, AND THE AUDIT STATES THAT BEFORE QUOTING ANY NUMBER FROM IT. Question: can any AT update rule generate a non-trivial phase evolution, among a single scalar flow, multiple coupled scalar flows, a vector-valued flow, a connection-driven flow and a T1/T2-coupled flow? Measure the phase-rank of the evolution operator. " +
            "(1) THREE RANKS ARE MEASURED, BECAUSE THE QUESTION ASKS FOR ONE. The PUSH rank is the rank of the state's instantaneous phase displacement; the LINEARISATION rank is how the generator's own Jacobian acts on the phase sector; the OPERATOR rank is how a phase perturbation propagates under the update rho -> rho - s V(rho). Measured: single scalar flow 1/53/53, multiple coupled scalar flows 1/53/53, vector-valued flow 1/53/53, connection-driven flow 1/53/53, T1/T2-coupled flow 1/53/53, identity update (CONTROL) 0/0/53. " +
            "(2) THE WARNING COMES FIRST. Every generator linearises to full rank and every operator rank is full - the identity reaching 53 operator rank while pushing 0. Two structural reasons: any state update is the identity plus a small term and the identity is invertible on the phase sector, and A SCALAR FLOW'S LINEARISATION IS ITS POTENTIAL'S HESSIAN, positive definite and therefore full rank on every subspace. So rank 53 is not evidence that a rule acts on the phase, and a criterion the do-nothing rule satisfies is not a criterion. " +
            "(3) THE PUSH RANK IS THE ONLY COLUMN THAT SEPARATES. The state moves along ONE vector per instant, so its phase displacement is rank one whatever the generator is - scalar or vector-valued alike. Measured: five rules push one direction, the identity pushes none, and COUPLING SEVERAL SCALAR FLOWS DOES NOT RAISE IT, because a sum of gradients is still a single vector. The ceiling belongs to being a push, not to being scalar. " +
            "(4) THE PROCESS THE THEORY RUNS HAS NOTHING TO PUSH WITH. Re-measured rather than cited: the update rule's spatial part is 0.000E+000, the coupling census is 0, so the actualization has no spatial generator and its push rank is 0. That answers the critical question more sharply than a rank count can - no AT process reaches the phase sector because none supplies a generator with phase content. " +
            "(5) AN EXPECTATION IS WITHDRAWN. The question's premise was a hierarchy in which a vector-valued generator reaches rank 53 while scalar-driven rules cap at 1. No rank measure separates them - measured, the scalar and vector-valued families return the same number in both columns - because a scalar flow's linearisation is its Hessian and any state update contains the identity. The premise is refuted by measurement, not merely unmet, and the audit records that instead of the hierarchy it expected to report. " +
            "(6) THE THREAD CLOSES. G_046 to G_051: the hidden set is the kernel, the kernel is the phase sector, and the phase directions are physical rather than gauge. G_052 to G_053: rho splits uniquely into amplitude (42) and phase (53), and phases have effects no amplitude move reproduces. G_054 to G_055: the phases are freely assigned and no scalar can prefer one. G_056 to G_057: non-scalar structures span all 53 while the processes AT runs are sensitive to none. G_058 states the closure with the right rank: AT contains structures sensitive to every phase direction and runs none of them, and the one rank that would show a rule acting on the phase is 0 for the process and 1 for every hypothetical rule alike. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the three ranks per rule, the identity control's three ranks, the push-rank ceiling, the coupling test, and the re-measured update-rule split and coupling census) and it has live branches: a non-zero actualization push rank would make a running phase process DERIVED, and a push rank of 0 for every rule would make it REFUTED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_057 keep their verdicts; G_057's rank-1 ceiling is identified as the push rank. G-group registry gains this audit as a Boundary claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseDynamicsClosureAudit.cs. 6/6 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimensions 53; three ranks per rule (push/linearisation/operator): single scalar flow 1/53/53, multiple coupled scalar flows 1/53/53, vector-valued flow 1/53/53, connection-driven flow 1/53/53, T1/T2-coupled flow 1/53/53, identity update control 0/0/53; every generator linearises full = True; every operator rank full = True; largest push rank 1; coupling scalars does not help = True; actualization: update-rule spatial part 0.000E+000, coupling census 0, push rank 0; vector-valued and scalar rules rank-indistinguishable = True",
            CalculationId: "phase-dynamics-closure-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_058", "ResearchY-G_057", "ResearchY-G_056", "ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-G_052"],
            AuditIds: ["g058"]),
        new("phase-flow-audit", "Phase Flow Audit", "Can any existing AT process change the phase coordinates? BOUNDARY: no AT process the theory runs changes them (actualization phase velocity 0.000E+000, spatial part 0.000E+000, census 0), while five potentials it defines would move them - clock 1.241E-002, acceleration 2.933E-002, field 1.678E-003, connection 1.678E-003, T1/T2 coupling 4.813E-001. A flow needs a potential and a potential is a scalar, so every candidate has phase rank 1 and selection power 1/53; the union of all five constrains 4 of the 53 phase directions, leaving 49 free. The field and connection flows coincide exactly (gap 0.000E+000), so five candidate names describe four flows.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["non-scalar-selection-audit", "phase-selection-principle-audit", "phase-determination-audit", "coupling-function-audit"],
            Narrative: "BOUNDARY - NO AT PROCESS THE THEORY RUNS CHANGES THE PHASE COORDINATES, WHILE FIVE POTENTIALS IT DEFINES WOULD MOVE THEM, AND NO SINGLE FLOW COULD EVER SUFFICE. Question: can any existing AT process change the phase coordinates, among the clock, acceleration, field, connection and T1/T2 coupling flows? " +
            "(1) THE FLOW AND THE SENSITIVITY ARE DIFFERENT OBJECTS, AND G_056's 53-DIMENSIONAL SPAN DOES NOT CARRY OVER. G_056 measured a non-scalar STRUCTURE whose derivative spans all 53 phase directions; a process, by contrast, is driven by a POTENTIAL - one scalar - whose gradient is ONE vector. The audit measures both the velocity that vector gives the phase coordinates and the rank of what it can constrain. " +
            "(2) FIVE CANDIDATE POTENTIALS DO MOVE THE PHASE, measured as a velocity rather than inferred: the clock's 1.241E-002 (fraction 3.768E-003), the acceleration's 2.933E-002 (5.204E-002), the field's 1.678E-003 (8.572E-002), the connection's 1.678E-003 (8.572E-002) and the T1/T2 coupling's 4.813E-001 (4.272E-001). The phase is not inert to what the theory can define; what is missing is the driver. " +
            "(3) THE PROCESS THE THEORY ACTUALLY RUNS IS PHASE-STATIC. The update rule's spatial part is 0.000E+000 and the census of members coupling the link sector to the organisation is 0, so the actualization supplies only the time-like component and its phase velocity is exactly zero. This is the answer to the goal: no AT process generates a phase flow. " +
            "(4) EVERY FLOW HAS PHASE RANK 1 AND SELECTION POWER 1/53, which is the same counting argument as G_055 applied one level up: a flow needs a potential, a potential is a scalar, and a scalar's gradient is one vector - so even a run flow would leave 52 directions free. " +
            "(5) THE UNION IS THE HONEST UPPER BOUND. If every one of the five flows were run simultaneously they would constrain 4 of the 53 phase directions between them, leaving 49 free, so the most generous reading of what AT's own potentials could ever pin falls short of the sector by 49 dimensions. " +
            "(6) A DEGENERACY IS MEASURED RATHER THAN COUNTED TWICE. The field flow and the connection flow coincide, with a gap of 0.000E+000, because the field strength AT builds is h(rho)*Delta rho - exactly the connection AT builds - so the five candidate names describe four distinct flows: the same shape of finding as the electromagnetism series' two coupling candidates turning out to be one law. " +
            "(7) WHAT THE SERIES NOW SAYS COMPLETELY. G_056 showed that AT contains STRUCTURES SENSITIVE TO EVERY PHASE DIRECTION; this audit shows that the PROCESSES it RUNS are sensitive to none of them, and that its POTENTIALS, singly or together, could constrain a measured handful. The phases are freely assigned - not because the theory is blind to them, but because nothing the theory does acts on what it can see. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY. The verdict is COMPUTED from floor checks (the five phase velocities with their fractions, the measured ranks, the re-measured update-rule split and coupling census, the union rank and deficiency, and the field-versus-connection gap) and it has live branches: a non-zero actualization phase velocity would make a running phase process DERIVED, and a union reaching 53 would make selection DERIVED. RECLASSIFIES NOTHING: G_040 and G_046 to G_056 keep their verdicts; G_056's sensitivity and G_054's free assignment are reconciled into a single statement. G-group registry gains this audit as a Boundary claim; the group-G consistency counts are updated with it. Core: AT.Core/ResearchXH/PhaseFlowAudit.cs. 7/7 PASSED.",
            Formula: "phase dimensions 53; phase velocities: clock 1.241E-002 (3.768E-003), acceleration 2.933E-002 (5.204E-002), field 1.678E-003 (8.572E-002), connection 1.678E-003 (8.572E-002), T1/T2 coupling 4.813E-001 (4.272E-001); every rank 1; selection power 1/53 = 0.0189; actualization phase velocity 0.000E+000 with update-rule spatial part 0.000E+000 and census 0; union constraint rank 4, deficiency 49; field-versus-connection gap 0.000E+000 so 4 distinct flows",
            CalculationId: "phase-flow-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_057", "ResearchY-G_056", "ResearchY-G_055", "ResearchY-G_054", "ResearchY-E_009"],
