        new("refractive-lens-audit", "Refractive Lens Audit", "Can light bend WITHOUT bending space, via an effective refractive index (the TRM-era idea)? REFUTED by an identity: n - 1 = -(1+gamma)*phi/c^2, so the index coefficient IS the PPN gamma and a static index is the same object as space curvature in different variables. AT's derived conformal sector gives n = 1 (zero bending); the TRM rate term is O(phi^2), 9.43e5x too small at the Sun; and an EM-only medium fails GW170817 by 2.4e9.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Refuted, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["conformal-assumption-audit", "spatial-origin-audit", "no-go-audit", "temporal-core-test-audit"],
            Narrative: "Can light deflection be obtained WITHOUT bending space - by giving the vacuum an effective refractive index and using c_eff = c0/n_eff? The TRM-era programme reported exactly that: n_eff = 2 + lambda_time*phi + lambda_space*phi^2*|mu_dot|, dtheta_TRM = dtheta_GR*f(kappa,b), with {beta,gamma} -> {1,1} at kappa -> 0.3, b -> 1.248. This audit tests whether that route can release AT from the non-conformal spatial postulate of G_029. ANSWER: REFUTED - BY AN IDENTITY, NOT AN ARGUMENT. " +
            "THE IDENTITY: THE INDEX **IS** THE PPN GAMMA. For a static metric g00 = -e^(2A), g_ij = e^(2B) delta_ij, light in the optical description sees n = e^(B-A). With A = phi/c^2 and B = -gamma*phi/c^2 this gives n - 1 = -(1+gamma)*phi/c^2, so the coefficient a in n = 1 + a*GM/(c^2 r) is EXACTLY a = 1 + gamma, and the deflection is dtheta = 2a*GM/(c^2 b) = ((1+gamma)/2)*4GM/(c^2 b). The closed form is CHECKED NUMERICALLY in the suite: the integral of d_perp ln n dl returns 4.000000 for a = 2 and 2.000000 for a = 1. A STATIC, NON-DISPERSIVE INDEX IS NOT AN ALTERNATIVE TO SPACE CURVATURE - IT IS THE SAME OBJECT IN DIFFERENT VARIABLES. 'Bending without space bending' therefore has only two readings, and both are decided. " +
            "THE THREE CASES. AT's DERIVED conformal sector (G_031: sqrt(det g_ij) = rho) has A = B, hence n = 1 and ZERO bending - which is G_032's Cassini refutation (8.6957e4 sigma) restated optically, with a one-line reason: a conformal factor maps null geodesics to null geodesics, so it cannot bend light at all. The three physical cases: conformal gamma = -1, n - 1 = 0, deflection 0; time-only gamma = 0, n - 1 = +1x, deflection EXACTLY HALF (2GM/c^2 b); GR gamma = +1, n - 1 = +2x, full 4GM/(c^2 b). " +
            "THE RATE-DEPENDENT TERM CANNOT SUPPLY AN INDEPENDENT SPATIAL TERM. Reproducing the observed deflection needs n - 1 = (1+gamma)*phi = 2*phi, which is FIRST order in phi; the TRM second term lambda_space*phi^2*|mu_dot| is SECOND order. With |mu_dot| ~ 1: at the solar surface (phi = 2.12e-6) the needed 4.24e-6 against a maximum phi^2 of 4.49e-12 is a shortfall of 9.43e5; at a white dwarf (1e-4) it is 2.0e4; at J0740+6620 (0.247002) it is 8.1. The first-order coefficient is the formula's LEADING CONSTANT (2), not lambda_time - and by the identity that constant IS the spatial metric function. The phi^2 term is nevertheless genuinely interesting, because it depends on a RATE, which no static metric can: it is a real NON-METRIC ingredient - but it can contribute only where phi is O(1), i.e. at COMPACT OBJECTS. " +
            "THE DICHOTOMY, AND ITS OBSERVATIONAL KILL. If the index is truly a MEDIUM rather than a metric, it affects LIGHT but NOT GRAVITATIONAL WAVES - and that is testable. Over GW170817/GRB170817A's 40 Mpc (130 Myr of light-travel), the differential delay of light against gravitons is: galactic-scale (n-1 = 1e-6) 4.12e9 s = 131 yr against the 1.7 s bound = 2.4e9x; solar-scale (2.12e-6) 8.73e9 s = 5.1e9x; cluster-scale (3e-5) 1.24e11 s = 7.3e10x; even 1e-12 fails by 2.4e3x. The surviving strength is n - 1 <= 1.7*c/D = 4.13e-16 - nothing like the 2*phi a deflection requires. The EM-only reading is excluded by about NINE ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE. " +
            "BENDING AND DELAY ARE NOT INDEPENDENTLY TUNABLE. Any static index that reproduces the bending also reproduces the SHAPIRO delay: the integral of (n-1)dl/c with n - 1 = 2GM/(c^2 r) returns exactly 2GM/c^3*ln(4 r1 r2/b^2), the GR value. One function, so the two observables cannot be tuned separately. " +
            "THE THREE GENUINE ESCAPES - AND ONLY THESE - are the ways a medium is NOT a metric, each an observational commitment rather than a free choice: DISPERSION n(omega) (lensing is observed achromatic to ~1 % from radio to optical); BIREFRINGENCE (n depends on polarization; bounded by vacuum-birefringence limits, and the two polarizations must bend identically to high precision); and TIME DEPENDENCE (a rate-dependent index is exactly the phi^2*|mu_dot| signature - the ONE genuinely non-metric ingredient in the TRM formula, but O(phi^2), hence a compact-object effect only). " +
            "WHAT SURVIVES FROM THE TRM IDEA. (1) The OPTICAL LANGUAGE: n - 1 = -(1+gamma)*phi/c^2 is the cleanest possible statement of AT's actual difficulty, and it shows the problem is NOT notation - any description that bends light has already chosen gamma, and AT's derived sector chose -1. (2) The RATE-DEPENDENT term as a genuine non-metric, compact-object effect, within an order of magnitude at neutron-star compactness. (3) A NEW FALSIFICATION HANDLE: any medium-based lens must beat GW170817's 1.7 s light-vs-graviton bound, and no astrophysically natural strength does. " +
            "THE SOURCE CHECK - AND A CORRECTION TO THIS AUDIT'S OWN FIRST READING. TRM.Core/Shared/PhotonTransportModel.cs was still on disk, so the formula was read IN SITU instead of inferred, and reading it FALSIFIED the audit's first estimate and STRENGTHENED the verdict. (a) lambda_time = 1 does NOT give half: the code accelerates by ar = -nEff*G*M/(r*r) with nEff = 2 + lambda_time*phi + lambda_space*phi^2*|mu_dot|, and nEff INCLUDES the leading 2.0, so at the solar limb nEff = 2.000002120 -> ratio 1.000001 -> FULL deflection; half would require grad(nEff - 2). (b) THE FILE USES BOTH CONVENTIONS AT ONCE: travel time writes (nEff - 2)*v (physical index = nEff - 2, i.e. HALF) while the acceleration keeps the 2 (FULL) - one function, two conventions, so the result depends on which line is read. (c) SO THE FULL DEFLECTION COMES FROM A LITERAL 2.0: ar = -nEff*G*M/r^2 with nEff ~ 2 is the flat-space '2x Newton' photon law, and by the identity a = 1 + gamma a constant of 2 IS gamma = 1 - the spatial factor is already in the formula, hardcoded. 'No space bending' is false: the space bending is typed in as a constant, and it is exactly AT's G_029 postulate in other variables. At solar compactness every other term is <= 1e-5 relative (KBase = 2 + 2A*phi + 3B*phi^2 with A = -0.1701452243330672, B = -8.484408441898648 moves the factor by -7.2e-7). (d) THE COEFFICIENTS ARE DECLARED OR FITTED, NOT DERIVED: LambdaTime = 1.0 (hardcoded), LambdaSpace = 30.0 with the file's summary saying 'CALIBRATED (lambda terms)', A, B and Lambda fitted to 16 digits, and EulerBridgeScale = 0.85 annotated '17/20 ... NOT a fundamental physical constant'. (e) TRM'S OWN TESTS CANNOT SUPPORT 'MATCHES GR': EL03 asserts ratio in [0.70, 1.25] (gamma 0.40..1.50), EL04 transport [0.95, 1.08] (gamma 0.90..1.16) and EL04 Euler [0.85, 1.25] (gamma 0.70..1.50), with |EL - TRM|/Schw <= 0.30; Cassini pins gamma to 1 +/- 2.3e-5, so the widest window is 23,913x LOOSER, and every run is G = 1, c = 1, b = 1 at eps = 1e-3..1e-2 - 472x to 4,717x OUTSIDE the solar regime. Solar-compactness deflection was never tested. (f) THE ONE NON-METRIC CHANNEL IS DEAD ON ITS OWN TERMS: reaching first order needs |mu_dot| = lambda_time/(lambda_space*phi) = 1.57e4 at solar compactness, while the code's own ComputeAbsDmuDtBase yields |mu_dot| ~ O(1.83e-6 ... 0.431) /s there - a shortfall of 3.65e4. And |mu_dot| is a NEW PRIMITIVE: AT's temporal core is rho -> g00 -> clock (G_035) with no such variable, and G_029/G_030's no-new-primitive rule forbids adding one. (g) TRM'S OWN DOCUMENTS ALREADY SAID SO: TRM_Geodesic_Derivation.md calls the second term 'a natural CANDIDATE for the missing spatial / CURVATURE-LIKE contribution' and lists lambda_s's derivation as the next open theoretical step (with 20/17 itself an Open Derivation Task, section 12); V3_4/main.tex nonclaims read 'No GR replacement is claimed' and 'any mapping to gravitational or cosmological observables requires a physical frequency scale not currently provided'. The slide reflects the TRANSPORT SUBSYSTEM (TRM34-41, TRM78), which the paper chose not to claim. " +
            "OUTPUT: REFUTED - and STRENGTHENED by reading the source. The only ingredient that ever produced the observed deflection is the literal constant 2, i.e. gamma = 1: precisely the quantity G_030 proved cannot be derived. The verdict is COMPUTED (the G_027 discipline). REGISTRY: added to the G_035 classification registry as Spatial -> BOUNDARY - it is a statement about gamma, i.e. the spatial block - triaged ScanDetectsIt: false because the suite names no B, g_rr or GammaOf (its subject is a COEFFICIENT, and its only metric vocabulary is the NEGATIVE test that a conformal metric cannot bend light). Counts become 25/10/3 of 38; the boundary index is still 23; no prior classification changed. CAVEATS - BOTH NOW CLOSED BY THE SOURCE CHECK: (1) phi IS the dimensionless potential, since PhotonTransportModel.Phi(G,M,c,r) = G*M/(c*c*r) is the canonical TRM definition, so the O(phi^2) conclusion stands; (2) f(kappa,b) -> 1 was FITTED, not derived - the deflection path multiplies by EulerBridgeScale = 0.85, which the code annotates as the reciprocal of the mid-band rational 20/17 and 'NOT a fundamental physical constant', and uses to make the Euler/Fermat branch 'comparable to the established transport RK4 branch'. No reclassification; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; no new primitive; 7/7 PASSED, group G 297/297. VERDICTS: DERIVED (the identity, the three cases, the Shapiro link) / FALSIFIED (the rate term's reach, the EM-only reading, the literal-2 deflection) / REFUTED (the refractive route as an escape from gamma).",
            Formula: "n - 1 = -(1+gamma)*phi/c^2;  a = 1 + gamma;  dtheta = 2a*GM/(c^2 b);  EM-only delay over 40 Mpc = 131 yr vs 1.7 s;  TRM n_eff leading constant 2.0 IS gamma = 1",
            CalculationId: "refractive-lens-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_037", "ResearchY-G_032", "ResearchY-G_031", "ResearchY-G_030"],
            AuditIds: ["g037"]),

        new("measure-decomposition-audit", "Measure Decomposition Audit", "Can the CLOCK measure alone supply the light deflection, making no spatial postulate necessary? YES FOR HALF, AND THE OTHER HALF IS FORBIDDEN BY THE REDSHIFT. Light responds only to the difference n - 1 = B - A, so the clock supplies exactly 1/(1+gamma) of the deflection (50 % in GR) - the intuition that time bends light is CORRECT - but a conformal change cancels EXACTLY (B = A gives n = 1 for any conformal factor, since a conformal factor maps null geodesics to null geodesics). Flat space with a doubled clock gives the full deflection at TWICE the redshift, and the redshift is measured to ~1 %. So A is pinned and B = +x is FORCED: the first-order spatial coefficient is DERIVED, only its O(x^2) completion is a postulate.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Theorem,
            ["refractive-lens-audit", "spatial-sector-closure", "no-go-audit", "clock-rate-audit", "conformal-assumption-audit"],
            Narrative: "Question raised against G_037: curvature can be read as a change in MEASURE - space is distance bending a little - and time is a measure too, so time 'should be able to do the same'. Can the CLOCK function alone supply the observed light deflection, so that no spatial postulate is needed? ANSWER: YES FOR HALF - AND THE OTHER HALF IS FORBIDDEN BY THE REDSHIFT. This is a REFINEMENT of G_029/G_030, not a refutation of them: it shows that B's FIRST-ORDER form is not postulated at all, because the measured redshift and the measured deflection together force it. " +
            "LIGHT RESPONDS ONLY TO THE DIFFERENCE. With n = e^(B-A): n - 1 = B - A = (+B from the distance measure) + (-A from the clock measure). So the intuition that time bends light is CORRECT: the clock contributes, and it contributes exactly 1/(1+gamma) of the deflection - 50 % at gamma = 1, 100 % at gamma = 0 (time-only), and at gamma = -1 the two contributions are equal and opposite so the net is ZERO. " +
            "BUT A CONFORMAL CHANGE CANNOT BEND LIGHT AT ALL. A conformal metric has B = A for ANY conformal factor, so n = e^(B-A) = 1 EXACTLY - verified across x from 1e-12 to 0.3, where n - 1 is identically zero. This is a THEOREM, not a numerical accident: a conformal factor maps null geodesics to null geodesics, so 'time and space bending equally' is INVISIBLE to light. Making the clock bend harder is automatically matched by space, and the two cancel. That is precisely AT's position: A = B = sigma. " +
            "THE COMPENSATION ROUTE WORKS - AND IS EXCLUDED BY THE REDSHIFT. Keep space flat (B = 0) and double the clock (A = -2x): the table is A = -x, B = -x (AT conformal) -> a = 0, 0 % bending, 1x redshift; A = -x, B = 0 (time only) -> a = 1, 50 %, 1x; A = -2x, B = 0 (clock-compensated) -> a = 2, 100 %, 2x; A = -x, B = +x (required) -> a = 2, 100 %, 1x. Doubling the clock DOES deliver the full deflection - at TWICE the redshift. The solar-limb redshift is measured to be GM/(Rc^2) = 2.12e-6, pinned to about 1 % by Pound-Rebka (first order), GPS and solar line measurements, and AT already reproduces it with A = -x (which is why the G_009 clock law passes). THE REDSHIFT IS WHAT FORBIDS COMPENSATING VIA TIME: A is not a free knob, it is a measured quantity. " +
            "WHENCE A REFINEMENT OF G_029/G_030. With A measured as -x, the deflection B - A = 2x leaves exactly one choice: B = +x. So B's FIRST-ORDER COEFFICIENT IS DERIVED from two measurements, not postulated - and the freedom G_030's no-go leaves is confined to the O(x^2) COMPLETION. This is the project's established TWO-LEVEL RULE, as used for the 3-family window in D_028/D_040: the VALUE at first order is DERIVED, the higher-order WINDOW is BOUNDARY. The remaining freedom, measured: g_rr survivor vs GR is -2.697e-11 relative at solar compactness and -29.68 % at neutron-star x = 0.247002. " +
            "AND WHY THE MEDIUM ESCAPE IS NOT OPEN TO AT (correcting G_037's framing). G_037 closed the 'make the index a medium' branch with GW170817 - which bounds the propagation of the TENSOR sector against light. AT has NO GRAVITON: that sector is the massless SPIN-2 psi FIELD of MinimalPsiEquation (Box psi_mu_nu = 0), a field rather than a particle. But in AT the branch is not merely excluded, it is UNAVAILABLE: the natural carrier of any index is rho, and rho sources the metric INCLUDING the psi sector, so an index built from rho acts on light and on the metric sector IDENTICALLY - it IS a metric, and n - 1 = -(1+gamma)*Phi/c^2 applies directly. " +
            "OUTPUT: REFUTED for the clock-compensation route, WITH A DERIVED BY-PRODUCT. The measure intuition does not remove the need for a spatial sector - it explains IN ONE LINE why AT's spatial sector is wrong by a SIGN and a FACTOR OF TWO at first order (B = -x where +x is required), and why the clock cannot repair it. Registry: G_038 added as Spatial -> BOUNDARY, triaged ScanDetectsIt: false; counts 25/11/3 of 39; boundary index still 23; no prior classification changed. No reclassification; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; no new primitive; 7/7 PASSED, group G 297/297. VERDICTS: DERIVED (the 1/(1+gamma) share, the conformal cancellation theorem, the forced B = +x) / BOUNDARY (the O(x^2) completion) / FALSIFIED (the clock-compensation route) / REFUTED (clock substitution as a whole).",
            Formula: "n - 1 = B - A;  clock share = 1/(1+gamma);  conformal B = A => n = 1 exactly;  A = -2x, B = 0 => full bending at 2x redshift;  A = -x, B = +x forced",
            CalculationId: "measure-decomposition-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_038", "ResearchY-G_037", "ResearchY-G_029", "ResearchY-G_030", "ResearchY-G_009"],
            AuditIds: ["g038"]),

        new("temporal-core-test-audit", "Temporal Core Test Audit", "Can the temporal core be tested without any spatial metric? BOUNDARY: the observable z = 1/sqrt(-g00) - 1 is PURE and AT/GR first differ at O(x^2), so the arena is neutron stars only (dz = 0.125628 at J0740+6620, 45 % of z_AT) - but the compactness that READS the signal comes from light bending, and sigma_x/x = 13.73 % against 3.661 % needed.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["temporal-independence-audit", "neutron-star-redshift-audit", "clock-rate-audit", "conformal-assumption-audit", "literal-verdict-audit"],
            Narrative: "Can the surviving temporal core - rho -> g00 -> clock rate -> acceleration - be tested WITHOUT ANY SPATIAL METRIC, using only g00, the clock law and the source law? Reject gamma, lensing, the Shapiro delay and the spatial metric; search clock gradients, redshift-only observables, compact-object timing and pulsar timing; find the FIRST experiment that probes the temporal core alone. ANSWER: BOUNDARY. " +
            "THE OBSERVABLE IS PURE. AT: z = e^x - 1 from g00 = -e^(-2x). GR: z = 1/sqrt(1-2x) - 1 from g00 = -(1-2x). The series are x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 against x + 3x^2/2 + 5x^3/2, so the two AGREE AT O(x) and FIRST DIFFER AT O(x^2): dz = x^2 + (7/3)x^3 + (13/3)x^4. z depends on g00 ALONE - no gamma, no lensing, no Shapiro delay, no g_ij anywhere in the measurement. The observables are functions whose SIGNATURE CONTAINS NO B (the arity argument of G_035), since a quantity that cannot be handed a spatial metric cannot depend on one. G_020's published figures are reproduced EXACTLY: dz = 0.125628 (G_020 reports 0.1256) at x = 0.247002, and at x = 0.187982 the audit returns z_AT = 0.206812 and z_GR = 0.265888. " +
            "THE ARENA IS NEUTRON STARS ONLY. Reaching |dz| > sigma_z requires a compactness above a threshold that CLIMBS WITH PRECISION: sigma_z = 1e-3 needs x >= 0.030494; 0.01 needs 0.089439; G_020's equal-split 0.017766 needs 0.115094; 0.025125 needs 0.133350. The weak-field arenas sit at x = 2.45e-15 (terrestrial tower), 1.1e-18 (optical lattice clocks, 1 cm), 2.12e-6 (solar surface), 1.0e-6 (binary pulsar Einstein delay) and 1.0e-4 (white dwarf), with dz = x^2 between 1e-30 and 1e-8, so they would need sigma_z between 1e-30 and 1e-12 - NINE TO TWELVE ORDERS below anything measurable. That is the arithmetic behind G_019's finding that only neutron stars are a live arena. " +
            "THE WEAK-FIELD SPLIT IS NOT MERELY UNMEASURABLE - IT IS UNREPRESENTABLE. Each law passes through an intermediate ~1, so each carries ~1 ulp = 2.220446049250313e-16 of ABSOLUTE error, while the true split at the Pound-Rebka compactness is 6.0025e-30 - fourteen orders below it. MEASURED: the DIRECT subtraction z_GR - z_AT returns -7.5093e-18 at x = 2.45e-15, wrong in magnitude AND IN SIGN, and at x = 1.1e-18 (optical-clock compactness) z_GR is ANNIHILATED OUTRIGHT because 1 - 2x rounds to 1.0 and the GR redshift returns EXACTLY 0. In the weak field the split can be STATED but NOT COMPUTED BY SUBTRACTION, so the audit uses the series below x = 1e-3 (and AtNumerics.ExpM1 for e^x - 1, whose naive form returns exactly 0.0 in Python but 2.4425e-15 in .NET for the same input). " +
            "THE BOTTLENECK IS THE COMPACTNESS, NOT THE REDSHIFT. G_020's budget re-derived: sigma_x/x = 13.73 % achieved against 3.661 % needed for 5 sigma - still 3.75x better - with a maximum attainable significance today of 1.334 sigma. The signal is not the problem: dz = 0.125628 is 44.84 % of z_AT. AND FOR A NEUTRON STAR THE COMPACTNESS IS ITSELF OBTAINED FROM LIGHT BENDING, because pulse-profile modelling fits the thermal emission from hot spots INCLUDING bending - the spatial sector G_032 showed to be an ASSUMED PRIMITIVE and G_035 showed the temporal core does not need. THE CENTRAL FINDING: THE OBSERVABLE IS PURE, BUT THE NUMBER REQUIRED TO READ IT IS NOT. That is why the verdict is BOUNDARY rather than TESTABLE. " +
            "A PURE ROUTE EXISTS AND IS ABOUT THREE TIMES SHORT. The apparent radius from a thermal flux and a parallax distance, R_inf = R/sqrt(1-2x), is a g00 EFFECT - photon energy and arrival rate, NOT bending - so {z, R_inf} solves {M, R} with NO light bending at all (verified: TrueRadiusFrom(ApparentRadius(r, x), z_GR(x)) returns r). Its systematics - distance and atmosphere models - currently keep sigma_x/x above the ~3.7 % the test needs. " +
            "THE FIRST EXPERIMENT. POUND & REBKA (1960): the gravitational redshift of Fe-57 gamma rays over a 22.5 m tower, x = 2.45e-15 - PURE g00, with no light bending anywhere in the measurement, and the first experiment to probe the temporal core at all. But it probes only the FIRST-ORDER term, the one AT SHARES WITH GR, with x^2 = 6.0e-30. NO EXPERIMENT HAS YET PROBED THE CORE'S DISTINCTIVE CONTENT; the frontier is a compact-object {z, R_inf} measurement at sigma_x/x <= 3.7 %. " +
            "REGISTRY. G_036 is registered in the G_035 classification registry as Spatial -> BOUNDARY, triaged ScanDetectsIt = false with a written reason: the suite's metric vocabulary lives entirely inside report string literals (0/0/0 after stripping), because the audit asks which quantities the MEASUREMENT needs, not which metric symbols the code spells. The registry counts become 25 / 9 / 3 of 37; the boundary index is still 23 and no prior classification changed. " +
            "OUTPUT: BOUNDARY - testable in principle with a pure observable, not yet isolated in practice, and the missing ingredient is COMPACTNESS PRECISION rather than signal. The verdict is COMPUTED (the G_027 discipline): BOUNDARY because the observable is pure, a discriminating regime exists, and a pure route to that regime exists, while the precision currently supplied is not pure. No reclassification; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; no new primitive; 6/6 PASSED, group G 283/283. VERDICTS: DERIVED (the pure observable, the arena thresholds, the unrepresentability, the bottleneck) / BOUNDARY (the pure route, the first-experiment frontier) / REFUTED (none).",
            Formula: "z_AT = e^x - 1; z_GR = 1/sqrt(1-2x) - 1; dz = x^2 + (7/3)x^3 + ...; dz(J0740+6620) = 0.125628; sigma_x/x 13.73 % vs 3.661 %",
            CalculationId: "temporal-core-test-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_036", "ResearchY-G_035", "ResearchY-G_020", "ResearchY-G_019", "ResearchY-G_032"],
            AuditIds: ["g036"]),

        new("a0-robustness-audit", "A0 Robustness Audit", "Which gravity/time conclusions depend quantitatively on A0? The exact-double keying is REPLACED by tolerance clustering (the rule D_047 documents); the corrected D96^3 spectrum matches D_047 on five independent figures; of 15 G-series claims consuming an A0-derived quantity, 7 are UNCHANGED, 2 BOUNDARY and 6 REFUTED \u2014 no conclusion breaks.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Refuted, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["cubic-substrate-audit", "literal-verdict-audit", "source-law", "spatial-origin-audit"],
            Narrative: "Which gravity/time conclusions depend QUANTITATIVELY on A0? Replace exact-double keying with tolerance clustering; measure A0, free room, latent fraction, lock-release and every derived quantity; classify UNCHANGED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED. ANSWER: the G-series' qualitative conclusions are UNCHANGED, but SIX pinned numeric values are REFUTED. " +
            "THE REPLACEMENT, APPLIED. SpectralCaseCatalog.D96CubedBreakdown keyed its 49^3 triple sums on EXACT binary64 equality; it now CLUSTERS at a tolerance. The tolerance is not invented - it is the rule D_047 already documents and applies: 'private const double TolCube = 1e-8; // 3-factor sums carry ~1e-14 noise; tol above it'. THE CORRECTED SPECTRUM REPRODUCES D_047 ON FIVE INDEPENDENT FIGURES, and M_012's independently reported 16 080: A0 = 16 080 (D_047: 16 080), A0 with multiplicity greater than 1 = 16 079 (16 079), max multiplicity = 738 (738), lock release = 4.165691 (4.16569), free room SUM(m-1) = 868 656 (868 656). FIVE OF FIVE MATCH. The G-series is now consistent with the D-series instead of contradicting it. " +
            "ROOT CAUSE - A MIXED EQUALITY DISCIPLINE. D96's own spectrum reaches the code through a real, TOLERANT eigensolver (AttractorDominanceAnalyzer.Eigenspaces) and therefore already carries the tolerant answers: A0 = 45, lock release 0.802314, free room 51. D96^3's own construction used exact-double dictionary keying. THE SAME QUANTITY, TWO EQUALITY RULES, INSIDE ONE PROGRAMME - which is exactly why D96's invariants never moved while the cube's did. " +
            "WHAT MOVED, ALL A0-DERIVED. A0 20 812 -> 16 080 (-22.7%); A0(m>1) 20 811 -> 16 079; free room 863 924 -> 868 656 (+0.55%); latent fraction L 0.976477 -> 0.981825 (+0.55%); LOCK RELEASE 3.948614 -> 4.165691 (+5.50%); MAX MULTIPLICITY 562 -> 738 (+31.3%). THE ASYMMETRY IS THE POINT: the count moves 23% while the FRACTIONS move only 0.55% - which is why the conclusions survive while the counts do not. " +
            "THE CLAIM REGISTRY - fifteen G-series claims that consume an A0-derived quantity, classified BY COMPUTATION (never typed). REFUTED (6): G_002's A0 = 20 812; G_002's max multiplicity 562; G_003's D96^3-vs-D96 density delta 0.276596 -> 0.263158; G_005's cube lock 3.948614 -> 4.165691; G_005's cube latent fraction 0.97648 -> 0.981825; G_006's restatement of the same lock. Measured IN THEIR OWN STATED TOLERANCES: G_003 moved 13 438x, G_005's lock 21 708x, G_005's L 535x. UNCHANGED (7): the cube's free fraction > 0.97 (holds at 0.981825 AND at 0.97648); G_006's L > 0.97; free room = N - A0 = the D_048 latent fraction L (an algebraic identity, true for either A0); the cube's free room exceeds D96's (an ordering, 0.982 > 0.531 either way); D96's A0 = 45; D96's lock 0.802314; D96's contraction 33.78. BOUNDARY (2): the quoted '97.6% energy-free' -> 98.2%, and the cube's contraction factor at m = 200, 7.33 -> 7.10. TOTAL 7 UNCHANGED / 2 BOUNDARY / 6 REFUTED. " +
            "WHY NOTHING COLLAPSES - ConclusionsSurvive() = true, CHECKED ON BOTH KEYINGS rather than asserted: the cube is still about 98% energy-free; free room is still exactly N - A0 and still equals the latent fraction; D96's own invariants never moved; the ordering arrangement > degeneracy > lattice-average > survivor compression is intact; the regime is still classified CONTROLLABLE. THE REFUTED ITEMS ARE NUMBERS, NOT CONCLUSIONS. " +
            "THE BLAST RADIUS, MEASURED NOT ASSUMED (the change is in SHARED infrastructure). G_002/G_003/G_005/G_006: four assertions updated to the corrected values. G_033: its live scanner now excludes TWO meta-audits (G_033 and G_034) that compute the spectrum in order to audit it. T_012: HEADLINE UNCHANGED - D96^3 still gives S-infinity = 16 (distance 3 from 19) and random 17 is still nearest; only the sub-claim 'the cubic 3-axis sector gives 21 (distance 2)' moved to 14 (distance 5). T_013: assertions all pass; quoted figures updated - A = 16 079 (was 20 811), C = 1004.9 (was 1300.7), max multiplicity 738 (was 562), '~150x' -> '~114x'. T_014, T_008-T_011 and D_047: ALL PASS UNCHANGED - D_047 needed nothing, because it was already correct. " +
            "OUTPUT: REFUTED - six pinned G-series values were artifacts and fail at their own stated precision (up to 21 708x their tolerance). SCOPE: no G-series conclusion breaks. The verdict is COMPUTED from the claim registry (the G_027 discipline). " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 6/6 PASSED, group G 271/271, affected set 321/321. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            CalculationId: "a0-robustness-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_034", "ResearchY-G_033", "ResearchY-D_047", "ResearchY-G_005"],
            AuditIds: ["g034"]),

        new("cubic-substrate-audit", "Cubic Substrate Audit", "Does gravity/time need D96^3 the way the rest of physics does? PARTIAL: gravity structurally requires it (the spatial metric's traceless part needs the dim-3 irrep T2g, which a single D96 ring cannot host), but the metric era is substrate-free because the requirement was absorbed into the primitive eta (G_032). Also: A0 = 20 812 is a floating-point artifact; the robust value is 16 080.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Partial, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["conformal-assumption-audit", "spatial-origin-audit", "no-go-audit", "literal-verdict-audit", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "The programme established that D96 (x) D96 (x) D96 ('D96^3') is required to explain physics: M_012 proved a genuine 3D (vector / p-wave, l = 1) sector exists on the cubic lattice but is ABSENT from a single D96 ring, whose max irrep dim is 2. Does the gravitation/time search (group G) show the same behaviour? ANSWER: PARTIAL \u2014 same requirement, different locus. " +
            "IN CODE, ERA-LOCAL \u2014 LIVE SCAN. The core re-reads the group-G sources AT TEST TIME (the G_027 pattern), separating CODE from COMMENT references so the inventory cannot go stale; Y_G_033 excludes ITSELF as self-referential (it computes the spectrum in order to audit it). Of 34 suites classified: 20 REFERENCE D96 IN CODE (the density era: G_002-G_011b, G_012, G_013, G_014, G_016, G_016b, G_018, G_023, G_024, G_026), 1 COMMENT-ONLY (G_001), and 13 WITH NO REFERENCE AT ALL \u2014 exactly the metric / closure era: G_015, G_017, G_019, G_020, G_021, G_022, G_025, G_027, G_028, G_029, G_030, G_031, G_032. Those thirteen are pure continuum PPN calculations (a scalar rho, an exponent, a conformal factor, gamma). " +
            "IN STRUCTURE, INHERITED. Gravity's central object is the spatial metric g_ij \u2014 a symmetric rank-2 tensor in d = 3: 6 components = 1 (trace, l = 0) + 5 (traceless, l = 2). Subducting the O(3) irreps onto the octahedral rotational group O (order 24; classes E/8C3/3C2/6C4/6C2'; irreps A1/A2/E/T1/T2 of dimension 1/1/2/3/3; sum d^2 = 24) REPRODUCES M_012 EXACTLY: character norms^2 = 1, 1, 2, 3, 4 for l = 0..4; l = 0 -> A1(1); l = 1 -> T1(3); l = 2 -> E(2) + T2(3); l = 3 -> A2(1)+T1(3)+T2(3); l = 4 -> A1(1)+E(2)+T1(3)+T2(3). So the VECTOR / p-wave sector needs T1u(3) (M_012's finding) and the SPATIAL METRIC'S TRACELESS PART needs T2g(3) \u2014 one multipole higher, the same argument. A single D96 ring is a cycle graph C_96 whose symmetry group D_96 (dihedral) has irreps of dimension 1 and 2 ONLY, so it supplies NEITHER; the cubic D96^3 lattice (point group O_h) supplies BOTH. GRAVITY REQUIRES THE CUBIC SUBSTRATE. And d = 3 is derived for the same reason M_013 gives: rotation self-duality d(d-1)/2 = d has the UNIQUE solution d = 3 (1->0, 2->1, 3->3, 4->6). " +
            "THE LOCUS IS eta (G_032). The metric era does not instantiate a 96^3 spectrum because it IMPORTS 3D space through the primitive eta \u2014 the conformal reference metric that G_032 proved is an assumed input (QG289: 'a TRUE THEORY INPUT ... part of the geometry, not a choice'). G_032 AND G_033 ARE ONE FACT SEEN TWICE: G_032 says the shape of space is an input; G_033 says that input is precisely the structure the cubic lattice would otherwise have supplied. The D96^3 requirement did not disappear from the gravity programme \u2014 it was DISCHARGED BY A PRIMITIVE instead of by a lattice. " +
            "DEFECT FOUND WHILE CHECKING: A0 = 20 812 IS NOT AN INVARIANT. Group G cites A0 = 20 812 EIGENSPACES for D96^3 (G_002, G_005, G_006 and downstream in DensityField.CubeSpaces, SpectralCaseCatalog, AT.App, AT.Book, AT_LabBook). It is an artifact of BINARY64 DICTIONARY KEYING: the construction enumerates the 49^3 reduced-index triples and counts distinct double sums, so the answer depends on the last bits of Math.Cos. Exact-double keying gives 20 812 under .NET (Math.Cos) and 20 440 under Python (math.cos) FOR THE SAME IEEE-754 ALGORITHM; a one-ulp (1e-16) perturbation of the 1D spectrum, 6 deterministic trials, swings it over 20 488 ... 21 369 (range 881). The TOLERANCE-CLUSTERED count is stable: it sits on a PLATEAU at 7-10 decimal places (decimal-place profile 6 -> 16 072, 7-10 -> 16 080, 11 -> 16 085, 12 -> 16 105, 13 -> 16 319, 14 -> 18 282) and its spread under 1e-16 AND 1e-13 noise is EXACTLY 0. THE ROBUST VALUE IS 16 080 \u2014 which is M_012's OWN independently reported figure ('16,080 distinct levels over 96^3 states') AND the value the repository uses elsewhere: NewChat_Start records 'D96^3 136 005 of 868 656', and 868 656 = 884 736 - 16 080. THE TWO LINEAGES NEVER MET. The repository carries BOTH numbers for the same quantity: A0 = 20 812 with free room 863 924 and L = 0.976477, versus A0 = 16 080 with free room 868 656 and L = 0.981825. WHAT SURVIVES: the qualitative claim \u2014 D96^3 is about 98% energy-free, its landscape is ~150x larger, compression is dominated by A. WHAT DOES NOT: 20 812, 863 924, L = 0.97648, and the lock-release 3.948614 derived from them; any downstream figure computed FROM A0 inherits an implementation-dependent input. NOT FIXED HERE, DELIBERATELY: the keying lives in shared infrastructure (AT.Tests/Shared/SpectralCaseCatalog.cs, DensityField.cs) consumed by other research groups, so changing it would renumber A0 for D96^3 PROGRAMME-WIDE and is a programme-level decision rather than a side effect of this audit. Registered as an open item. " +
            "OUTPUT: PARTIAL \u2014 gravity needs the dimension-3 sector (SAME requirement), but the use is era-local and the requirement is discharged by eta rather than exercised, so the behaviour is THE SAME IN STRUCTURE AND DIFFERENT IN LOCUS. The verdict is COMPUTED from the live scan plus the subduction, never typed (G_027). " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 5/5 PASSED, group G 265/265. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            CalculationId: "cubic-substrate-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_033", "ResearchY-G_032", "ResearchY-G_002", "ResearchY-G_006"],
            AuditIds: ["g033"]),

        new("conformal-assumption-audit", "Conformal Assumption Audit", "Is g = Omega^2 eta derived, or only assumed? ASSUMED (BOUNDARY): it enters at the rho -> metric step (the TENSOR face) as the primitive eta; the forcing set is EMPTY, and imposing it forces gamma = -1, Cassini-excluded at 86957.4348 sigma.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Boundary, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["no-go-audit", "spatial-origin-audit", "spatial-sector-closure", "clock-sector-closure", "literal-verdict-audit"],
            Narrative: "Is g = Omega^2 eta derived, or only assumed? Trace Difference -> Counting -> rho -> metric; find the step that FIRST requires the conformal ansatz; decide whether any existing AT primitive forces conformal flatness. ANSWER: ASSUMED. Output: BOUNDARY \u2014 the verdict is COMPUTED, not typed. " +
            "WHERE IT ENTERS, EXACTLY. Step 1 (Difference -> Counting) is pure bookkeeping with NO metric content. Step 2 (Counting -> rho, the SCALAR face of the one Difference) needs no reference tensor \u2014 QG288: 'the scalar face does not [require eta]'. Step 3 (rho -> metric, the TENSOR face) is the FIRST step that requires it \u2014 QG285/QG288: 'the tensor face REQUIRES eta [conformal reference]'. Step 4 merely inherits it. The chain is METRIC-FREE for its first two steps. The imported object is eta, which QG289's anchor inventory (AnchorInventoryAudit, QG77) classifies as a TRUE THEORY INPUT: 'the conformal reference metric (g = rho^(2/d) eta) \u2014 the framework's flat reference, not a measured value; part of the geometry, not a choice'. G_031 said conformal flatness is built into the ansatz; G_032 names the owner of that ansatz. " +
            "THE CRITERION, PROVED. In the G-group's gauge ds^2 = -e^(2A)dt^2 + e^(2B) delta_ij, and g = Omega^2 eta <=> A = B. (<=) is immediate: A = B gives g = e^(2A)(-dt^2 + delta) = e^(2A)eta. (=>) in area gauge the criterion is e^(B_area) = 1 - R A_R with R = e^B r; two lines of chain rule give e^(B_area) = 1/(1 + rB') and R A_R = rA'/(1 + rB'), so it holds iff B' = A', i.e. B = A by asymptotic flatness. Executed equivalence sweep: ZERO MISMATCHES. INDEPENDENT WEYL CONFIRMATION of W = C_abcd C^abcd: flat A = B = 0 gives 0.0; A = B = -c/r gives 1.0e-30; A = B = -c/r^2 gives 1.6e-29; A = -c/r with B = A/2 gives 0.6937; A = 0 with B = -c/r gives 15.39; and the G_029 SURVIVOR gives 0.2537. " +
            "THE G_029 SURVIVOR IS NOT CONFORMALLY FLAT. Its area-gauge deficit e^B - (1 - R A_R) expands as -1.5x^2 + (13/6)x^3 - (29/8)x^4 + ...: conformal to FIRST order and violated at SECOND, checked against the closed form to 2.4e-12 relative. (Numerical note: the direct difference sqrt(2 - e^(-2x)) - (1 + x) loses about 12 digits to cancellation as x -> 0 \u2014 at x = 1e-6 it returns -1.499911e-12 where the true value is -1.4999978e-12 \u2014 so the audit computes through the conjugate form with a series numerator for small x. The Weyl check was also initially wrong, reporting W = 9.85 for A = B, which is manifestly Omega^2 eta; the cause was an r-only derivative assumption invalidated by the metric's theta-dependence through sin^2 theta.) " +
            "NO PRIMITIVE FORCES IT. Setting eta aside \u2014 it IS the conformal statement, so citing it to derive conformal flatness RESTATES the assumption \u2014 the forcing set is EMPTY. Every remaining primitive is rank 0: rho (scalar face), psi (traceless face), d = 3, pi. A scalar can only be read into a conformal factor; it cannot determine a SHAPE. Component accounting: a symmetric 4x4 metric has 10 components, a conformal metric has 1 function, so the ansatz DISCARDS 9; AT's scalar content at a point is 2 and it supplies 0 of the 5 independent traceless (Weyl) components. Corroboration from the group's own work: G_029's candidate family B = F(sigma) IS that leftover freedom \u2014 its existence proves the primitives support TWO metric functions, not one, which is why conformality has to be imposed separately. " +
            "COUNTING IS A DETERMINANT CONDITION, NOT A SHAPE CONDITION. sqrt(det g_ij) = rho fixes only the PRODUCT of the eigenvalues. Explicit counterexample in d = 3: diag(rho^2, 1, 1) and diag(rho^(2/3), rho^(2/3), rho^(2/3)) have IDENTICAL sqrt(det) = rho but different conformal status (the anisotropic one is conformal only at rho = 1, the flat degenerate point). So the counting measure cannot entail conformality. With A = sigma fixed the three names coincide with ZERO mismatches over 4001 densities: conformality (A = B) <=> the counting measure (e^(3B) = rho) <=> B = sigma. G_031 called the counting measure a theorem; G_032 locates the single premise that makes it one \u2014 and finds it an assumption. " +
            "THE DECISIVE CONSEQUENCE: IMPOSING THE ANSATZ IS REFUTED. With A = sigma fixed by G_028, A = B forces B = sigma, hence gamma = -1 EXACTLY at EVERY body: Cassini separation 86957.4348 sigma (identical at all four bodies, since gamma = -1 is x-independent), with ZERO light deflection and ZERO Shapiro delay. The admissible band, computed by EXACT inversion B(x,gamma) = 0.5 ln(1 + gamma(1 - e^(-2x))) with no sampling, is about 1.84e-10 wide at the solar point and sits at ~ +x = -sigma while conformality demands +sigma: OPPOSITE SIDES OF ZERO. The required violation is a FACTOR OF 2.000013, not a small correction; gamma = -1 is NEVER inside the band at any body. So IF THE ANSATZ WERE ENTAILED BY AT'S PRIMITIVES, AT WOULD BE REFUTED \u2014 being unentailed is precisely what keeps it viable as a choice, and that is what makes it an assumption rather than a derivation. And AT's own metric form, g = rho^(2/d) eta, IS the conformal member: read at face value it predicts gamma = -1, i.e. no light bending and no Shapiro delay. This is the earlier programme concern traced to its primitive root. " +
            "AMENDMENTS TO PRIOR AUDITS. G_029: the surviving space rule g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) is NOT conformally flat. G_030: the dilemma's root is the primitive eta, so restate 'counting measure versus optics' as CONFORMAL FLATNESS VERSUS OPTICS. G_031: the premise doing the entailing is eta \u2014 an input, not a derivation. HONEST NOTE: QG289 describes eta as 'part of the geometry, not a choice'; this audit agrees it is neither empirical nor fitted constant, but 'input' and 'derived' are opposites, the inventory itself calls it a TRUE THEORY INPUT, and the entailing set is empty \u2014 which is what BOUNDARY records. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 8/8 PASSED, group G 260/260. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            CalculationId: "conformal-assumption-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_032", "ResearchY-G_031", "ResearchY-G_030", "ResearchY-G_029", "ResearchY-G_028"],
            AuditIds: ["g032"]),

        new("spatial-origin-audit", "Spatial-Origin Audit", "Where does B = sigma enter the theory? NOWHERE \u2014 it is ENTAILED, not assumed. With g_uv = rho^(2n) eta_uv, the statements n = 1/d, the clock law sqrt(-g00) = rho^(1/d) and the counting measure sqrt(det g_ij) = rho are THE SAME EQUATION (0 mismatches over a 401x401 sweep). The measure is load-bearing in five places, so the verdict is REQUIRED \u2014 and G_023's 'two pins' is corrected to one.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["no-go-audit", "spatial-sector-closure", "clock-sector-closure", "literal-verdict-audit", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "Exactly where does B = sigma enter the theory? Trace every path Difference -> Density -> Metric -> Spatial measure. ANSWER: IT DOES NOT ENTER. B = sigma is ENTAILED, not assumed; the verdict is REQUIRED, computed rather than typed. " +
            "THE PROVENANCE THEOREM, EXECUTED: the conformal ansatz g_uv = rho^(2n) eta_uv gives A = B = n ln rho, sqrt(-g00) = rho^n and sqrt(det g_ij) = rho^(n d). Conformal flatness (A = B) is BUILT INTO the ansatz, so only n is free - and in d = 3 the three statements n = 1/d, the clock law sqrt(-g00) = rho^(1/d) and the counting measure sqrt(det g_ij) = rho are THE SAME EQUATION: two readings of one exponent choice, read off two slots conformal flatness has already made equal. Verified by an exhaustive 401x401 sweep of (n, rho): ZERO MISMATCHES. There is no separate 'spatial measure' step to be found or removed. " +
            "THE EXCLUDED POINT IS FLAT SPACE: at rho = 1 the metric is flat, A = B = 0 for EVERY exponent, so all exponents agree trivially and the point carries no information about the equivalence. It is excluded explicitly and SEPARATELY ASSERTED to be degenerate - not silently dropped - because a degeneracy quietly skipped is exactly the defect class the G_027 Literal Verdict Audit exists to catch. " +
            "PROVENANCE OF EVERY STEP: Difference -> Density DERIVED (trace/traceless decomposition, QG285/QG286/QG292); Density -> Metric ASSUMED (the metric ansatz, QG207 - this is the source of A = B); the exponent n = 1/d ASSUMED (this IS the clock law - it is not a second postulate, it is the clock law read in the spatial slot - anchored by G_004's 0.99600 calibration and G_009's GPS agreement); Metric -> Spatial measure DERIVED (the algebraic identity rho^(n d) = rho at n = 1/d); rho read as a geometric volume CORRESPONDENCE (G_018's provenance asymmetry). So the counting measure is DERIVED ALGEBRAICALLY, FROM AN ASSUMED EXPONENT, UNDER A CORRESPONDENCE READING. " +
            "AN ALTERNATIVE EXISTS, BUT NOT WITHIN THE ANSATZ: an alternative measure needs B != sigma, which under conformal flatness forces A != B - the traceless face psi. psi is not a new primitive TYPE (G_024/QG285: it is the traceless face of the one Difference) but it IS an independent degree of freedom the theory does not constrain, so the metric becomes underdetermined - exactly G_030's result. The two audits agree, from the provenance side and the constraint side respectively. " +
            "USAGE INVENTORY: FIVE LOAD-BEARING uses - the metric ansatz itself (not separable from the geometry it produces); count conservation N = int rho dV (QG194/QG222 - the volume integral is the count only if sqrt(det g_ij) = rho); deficit accounting Sum rho = 1 (QG181/QG182); horizon area -> entropy S = A/4 (QG185/QG259); cosmological density parameters Omega and n_s. TWO NEUTRAL - |psi|^2 = rho (QG216, a probability reading rather than a volume reading) and the RAR scale g_dagger = c H0/(2 pi) (QG080, which uses no volume element). " +
            "WHAT BREAKS, QUANTIFIED: the geometric-to-count volume ratio sqrt(det g_ij)/rho for the surviving alternative runs 1.000012735 at the Sun, 1.000600120 at x = 1e-4, 1.733052388 at x = 0.1, 3.437584871 at J0740+6620 and 51.142808724 at x = 1. Four breakages follow, each at magnitude 2.44 at J0740+6620: count conservation, deficit accounting, the area/entropy chain, and the cosmological densities. The departure becomes order one exactly where the theory is most discriminating. " +
            "RENARRATION OF G_023: AT does NOT pin k = 0 twice. Conformal flatness supplies A = B and ONE exponent choice supplies both values. The counting measure was therefore never an independent postulate. So G_030's dilemma SHARPENS: the conflict is not 'counting measure versus optics' but CONFORMAL FLATNESS PLUS THE CLOCK LAW VERSUS OPTICS - a smaller and more decisive statement, reducing the theory's difficulty to the two things that ARE assumed, and showing that the item the programme had been treating as a removable identification is a THEOREM. " +
            "CRITICAL: if B = sigma is not load-bearing, remove it; if it is load-bearing, list exactly what breaks. It IS load-bearing (five uses), so it is kept - and it cannot be removed on its own, because it is not an assumption to remove. The measure is required for a reason the programme had not previously understood: it is what the clock law already says. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 7/7 PASSED, group G 252/252. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            CalculationId: "spatial-origin-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_031", "ResearchY-G_030", "ResearchY-G_029", "ResearchY-G_023", "ResearchY-G_018"],
            AuditIds: ["g031"]),

        new("no-go-audit", "No-Go Audit", "Is there a theorem that any local B(r) = F(sigma) must violate a requirement? YES \u2014 NO-GO. Six of the eight constraints are inert; gamma = -1 <=> B = sigma (the counting measure, AT's only derivation) is excluded at 8.6957e4 sigma, while gamma = +1 <=> g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) is underivable. The admitted band sits on the OPPOSITE SIDE OF ZERO from the derived value. There is no third.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["spatial-sector-closure", "clock-sector-closure", "literal-verdict-audit", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "Is there a theorem that any LOCAL B(r) = F(sigma) must violate at least one of Newton, Cassini, light deflection, the clock sector, or the no-new-primitive rule? YES - NO-GO, proved. " +
            "SIX OF THE EIGHT CONSTRAINTS ARE INERT: with A = sigma fixed by G_028, the Newton limit, the Earth clock, GPS, the neutron-star audit and the clock sector depend ONLY on A, which B never touches; and light deflection is (1+gamma)/2, the SAME test as Cassini. The live pair is {Cassini/deflection} versus {no-new-primitive}. " +
            "TWO EXACT EQUIVALENCES: inverting gamma via B(gamma) = 0.5 ln(1 - gamma(e^(2A) - 1)) gives (i) gamma = -1 <=> B = sigma, which is exactly the counting measure sqrt(det g_ij) = rho, and (ii) gamma = +1 <=> e^(2B) = 2 - e^(2A), i.e. g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) = 2 - |g00|. Both verified by SOLVING rather than by assertion. THE TWO SPECIAL GAMMA VALUES CORRESPOND EXACTLY TO THE TWO SPECIAL B's, AND ONLY THE EXCLUDED ONE IS AT-DERIVED. " +
            "THE PROOF: F = Id - the counting measure, AT's ONLY determination of B from rho - gives B = sigma, hence gamma = -1, which lies 8.6957e4 sigma outside the Cassini band [0.9999520, 1.0000900] and makes light deflection identically zero. F != Id places no AT-derived value in B, so F's specification is an input beyond rho, which G_023's accounting calls a NEW PRIMITIVE. Every other ingredient either fixes A, fixes numbers (occ, Sum-m, #g), or supplies FREE content (the traceless face psi); none determines B. QED. " +
            "THE ADMITTED BAND IS A SLIVER, ON THE WRONG SIDE OF ZERO: inverting gamma gives the admissible interval exactly, with no sampling. At solar compactness it is ~5.5e-10 wide and sits at B ~ +x = -sigma, while the derived value sits at B = sigma = -x - OPPOSITE SIDES OF ZERO, so the derived B has the wrong SIGN, not merely the wrong size. Established rigorously by exact inversion (true at every body) and confirmed by a band-resolving sweep of 20001 points over [-2x, 2x] per body with ZERO escapes. " +
            "THE DEPARTURE IS NOT A SMALL CORRECTION: survivor sqrt(det g_ij)/rho runs 1.000000004 at Earth (4.2e-9), 1.000012735 at the Sun (1.3e-5), 1.733052388 at x = 0.1, 3.437584871 at J0740+6620 (departure 2.44) and 51.142808724 at x = 1 - growth beyond five orders of magnitude, reaching O(1) exactly where the theory is most discriminating. " +
            "OUTPUT: NO-GO. GOAL - existence of a surviving spatial sector: REFUTED AS A DERIVATION (G_029's 'chosen, not derived' elevated to a theorem) and AFFIRMED AS A POSTULATE. SHARPEST FORM: gamma = -1 <=> B = sigma (refuted) and gamma = +1 <=> g_rr = 2 - |g00| (underivable) - THERE IS NO THIRD. " +
            "CONSEQUENCE - A DILEMMA WITH EXACTLY TWO HORNS: keep the counting measure (gamma = -1, excluded at 8.6957e4 sigma with zero deflection and Shapiro), or abandon it (all optics correct, but the volume-count identification is replaced by an input the theory does not supply). The choice is NOT numerical - it is a choice about WHICH OF AT'S IDENTIFICATIONS IS PRIMITIVE, and the two cannot be had together. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 8/8 PASSED, group G 245/245. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            Formula: "A = sigma fixed;  B(gamma) = 0.5 ln(1 - gamma(e^(2A) - 1));  gamma = -1 <=> B = sigma (counting measure e^(3B) = rho);  gamma = +1 <=> e^(2B) = 2 - e^(2A) <=> g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) = 2 - |g00|;  Cassini band gamma in [0.9999520, 1.0000900];  gamma = -1 separation 8.6957e4 sigma;  admitted B band ~5.5e-10 wide at x = 4e-6, centred at -sigma while the derived value is at +sigma... i.e. sigma = -x;  survivor volume ratio 4.2e-9 (Earth) -> 2.44 (J0740+6620)",
            CalculationId: "no-go-audit",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_030", "ResearchY-G_029", "ResearchY-G_028", "ResearchY-G_023"],
            AuditIds: ["g030"]),

        new("spatial-sector-closure", "Spatial Sector Closure", "Can any space rule B(r) survive all eight constraints without a new primitive? EXACTLY ONE: g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) = 2 - |g00|, the unique member with gamma = +1 at all orders. B = sigma \u2014 the only member AT derives \u2014 is REFUTED at Cassini 8.6957e4 sigma, so the sector closes on a POSTULATE at a volume cost of 3.437585.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["clock-sector-closure", "spatial-closure", "literal-verdict-audit", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "With A = sigma FIXED by G_028, can any spatial metric B(r) survive all eight constraints without a new primitive? EXACTLY ONE SURVIVES, AND IT IS CHOSEN, NOT DERIVED. " +
            "WHAT THE CONSTRAINTS ACTUALLY BIND: requirements 1-4 (Newton limit, Earth clock, GPS, neutron-star audit) depend ONLY on A, which G_028 fixed, so EVERY candidate passes them and they discriminate nothing; requirements 5-7 (Cassini gamma, light deflection, Shapiro delay) depend ONLY on gamma; requirement 8 concerns the primitive base, and the B-freedom is psi's traceless face, established at G_024 as not a new primitive. So the eight requirements pin ONE NUMBER, not a function, and the entire nonlinear completion of B stays free. " +
            "CANDIDATE TABLE (gamma at J0740+6620): B = sigma gives gamma = -1.000000 with deflection/GR = 0, Shapiro/GR = 0 and counting-measure ratio 1.000000, REFUTED at Cassini 8.6957e4 sigma; B = -sigma gives 1.638865; B = 0.5 ln(2 - e^(2 sigma)) gives gamma = 1.000000 EXACTLY with deflection/GR = Shapiro/GR = 1.000000 and volume/count = 3.437585; B = -sigma - 2 sigma^2 gives 0.350133; a rational/exponential family gives ~1 + O(x). At the solar-system point Cassini probes (x = 4e-6), B = sigma gives gamma - 1 = -2 (8.6957e4 sigma) while the linear member gives 0.565 sigma. " +
            "THE UNIQUE SURVIVOR: e^(2B) = 2 - e^(2A), equivalently g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) = 2 - |g00|. The spatial metric is the REFLECTION of the temporal one about 1; the conformal gamma = -1 member is g_rr = |g00|. To first order g_rr = 1 + 2x = 1 - 2 gamma Phi with Phi = -x and gamma = +1, the GR value. " +
            "NON-DEGENERACY, CORRECTED DURING THIS AUDIT: 2 - e^(2A) vanishes only at A = +0.5 ln2, i.e. x = -0.3465735903, a NEGATIVE compactness corresponding to a repulsive object. So the exact member has NO degeneracy anywhere physical and g_rr is bounded in (1, 2) for every x > 0, tending to 2 as x -> infinity: space is uniformly STRETCHED. (The first derivation in this audit claimed a degeneracy at R = 2.8854 GM/c^2; that was a sign error, caught by the test suite and corrected before committing.) " +
            "AT DERIVES NO B: its only equation for B is the counting measure, and it yields B = sigma, the member Cassini excludes. The survivor is therefore selected by OBSERVATION. The price is exact: the volume cost 3.437584871 reproduces G_023's recorded 3.437585 exactly, so it was already known from the k = B - A direction and is now confirmed from the observation side. " +
            "THE COMPLETION IS UNSELECTED: Cassini bounds the quadratic coefficient of B = -sigma + c2 sigma^2 only by |c2 + 2| <= 22.5 at 3 sigma. VERDICTS: SURVIVES = g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d); BOUNDARY = gamma pinned but B not, the counting measure traded away, and AT deriving no B so the survivor is a POSTULATE; REFUTED = B = sigma and the counting measure as the equation for B. " +
            "CRITICAL: all DERIVABLE B fail, so the spatial sector is CLOSED AS A DERIVATION; exactly one survives the strengthened requirement, so THE SECTOR CLOSES ON A POSTULATE at an exact and known price. Opened: an AT-native principle for g_rr = 2 - |g00|; whether 3.437585 breaks the four-scale calibration, the deficit accounting (QG181/182) or the spectral identification of occ; and the horizon/Hawking chain (QG208) on the new B, since g_rr -> 2 while |g00| -> 0. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 7/7 PASSED, group G 237/237. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            Formula: "A = sigma = (1/d) ln rho = -x (FIXED);  gamma = -(e^(2B)-1)/(e^(2A)-1);  deflection and Shapiro both ∝ (1+gamma)/2;  counting measure: e^(3B) = rho <=> B = sigma;  UNIQUE gamma = +1 at all orders: e^(2B) = 2 - e^(2A) <=> g_rr = 2 - rho^(2/d) = 2 - |g00|;  Cassini: gamma = 1.0000210 +/- 2.3e-5;  B = sigma separation 8.6957e4 sigma;  volume cost of the survivor 3.437585;  Cassini bound on c2: |c2 + 2| <= 22.5",
            CalculationId: "spatial-sector-closure",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_029", "ResearchY-G_028", "ResearchY-G_023", "ResearchY-G_024"],
            AuditIds: ["g029"]),

        new("clock-sector-closure", "Clock Sector Closure", "Is the physical clock law rho^(1/d) or rho^(1/d)*exp(psi)? ANSWER: rho^(1/d) \u2014 CLOCK CLOSED. The potential IS the time exponent, so psi cannot be nonzero without changing the source law; gamma = +1 forces A = +3x > 0 (a blueshift at every body, 2000 sigma at Earth). Corrects G_024 and QG212: the GPS bound is 1.391e-12, 1.44e9x tighter than quoted.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["literal-verdict-audit", "authored-verdict-audit", "spatial-closure", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "Is the physical clock law dTau/dt = rho^(1/d) or dTau/dt = rho^(1/d)*exp(psi)? ANSWER: rho^(1/d). CLOCK CLOSED. " +
            "THE ONE FACT THAT DECIDES IT: the Newtonian potential IS the time exponent \u2014 g00 = -e^(2A) with A = sigma + psi and sigma = (1/d) ln rho, and Phi/c^2 = A, so a = -grad Phi = -(1/d) grad ln rho - grad psi. The stated source law a = -(1/d) grad ln rho therefore holds IFF grad psi = 0, and a constant psi is nothing but a global choice of time unit (it cancels from the redshift ratio). " +
            "CRITICAL QUESTION \u2014 CAN psi BE NONZERO WITHOUT CHANGING THE SOURCE LAW? NO. A - sigma = psi IDENTICALLY, so any nonzero psi moves the time exponent; this is a proof, not a judgement. " +
            "THE OPTICS PRICE: within the trace-preserving QG207 direction (A = sigma + psi, B = sigma - psi/(d-1)), gamma = +1 (i.e. A + B = 0) fixes psi = -4 sigma UNIQUELY, forcing A = -3 sigma = +3x > 0. THE POTENTIAL BECOMES POSITIVE: the surface clock runs FAST and every gravitating body is BLUESHIFTED. The clock's SIGN inverts; it is not merely shifted. " +
            "THE TABLE (z): rho-only gives Earth +6.957e-10, Sun +2.1225e-6, x=1e-4 +1.0000e-4, J0740+6620 +0.2801817. QG207 at psi = -4 sigma gives Earth -2.087e-9, Sun -6.3675e-6, x=1e-4 -3.0000e-4, J0740+6620 -0.5233658. The sign flips at EVERY body, Earth included. " +
            "FIVE REQUIREMENTS: rho-only satisfies ALL FIVE \u2014 (1) the source law; (2) Earth/GPS at 0.000 sigma; (3) the G_020 neutron-star redshift audit with z_AT = 0.2801817; (4) positivity at every body including compact objects; (5) no new primitive. QG207(psi = -4 sigma) fails 1 (the psi contribution to the acceleration is 4x the rho contribution), 2 (2000.4 sigma at Earth against the 0.2 percent GPS precision), 3 and 4, passing only 5. " +
            "CORRECTION TO G_024 AND TO THE RESTORED QG212: G_024 quoted a GPS bound |psi| <= 2e-3 and called it 7.2e5x LOOSER than required. That comparison is wrong IN KIND \u2014 it treated the shift e^(4x) - 1 = 2.78e-9 as additive on a clock of 1, but the observable is the redshift RELATIVE TO INFINITY, where the conformal law already gives z ~ +x = 6.957e-10. 2.78e-9 is 4x the whole effect and REVERSES its sign. The correct bound is |psi| <= 1.391e-12, i.e. 1.44e9x TIGHTER, and psi = -4 sigma is excluded at 2000 sigma by the Earth redshift alone. It follows that QG212's 'physical sector' (psi != 0 at psi = -4 sigma) is a REPULSIVE geometry and is observationally refuted. " +
            "THE STRUCTURAL RESULT: psi and the clock are NOT independent. Every attempt to repair gamma from the trace-free direction repays the debt in the clock, and the repayment is a sign inversion. So the optics fix CANNOT come from psi; it must be spatial. " +
            "BOUNDARY \u2014 THE SPATIAL ROUTE: A held at sigma with B = 0.5 ln(2 - e^(2 sigma)) is the ONLY gamma = +1 that leaves the clock untouched; it satisfies requirements 1-4 and fails 5, since it leaves the trace-free direction and the volume measure becomes 3.437585x the count at J0740+6620. " +
            "CLOCK CLOSED, AND THE CLOSURE RELOCATES THE FAILURE: the clock sector is sound (gamma = -1 is excluded at Cassini 8.6957e4 sigma, but optics is not a clock-sector requirement), and the ENTIRE open problem is the SPATIAL sector. Opened: fix optics spatially (G_023's route, volume cost 3.437585); re-audit QG212's physical sector; re-derive the GPS bound for every psi proposal, since the 2e-3 error is a METHOD error rather than a typo. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 7/7 PASSED, group G 230/230. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
            Formula: "A = sigma + psi, B = sigma - psi/(d-1), sigma = (1/d) ln rho = -x;  gamma = -(e^(2B)-1)/(e^(2A)-1);  gamma = +1 (A + B = 0) => psi = -4 sigma => A = +3x;  z = e^(-A) - 1;  rho-only: z = e^x - 1;  QG207: z = e^(-3x) - 1;  GPS bound |psi| <= 0.002 * z_AT = 1.391e-12;  spatial route B = 0.5 ln(2 - e^(2 sigma)) with volume cost 3.437585",
            CalculationId: "clock-sector-closure",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_028", "ResearchY-G_024", "ResearchY-G_023", "ResearchY-G_009"],
            AuditIds: ["g028"]),

        new("literal-verdict-audit", "Literal Verdict Audit", "Can the rule be broken quietly? NO \u2014 it is enforced. No result path may let a classification depend on a literal. LiteralVerdictAudit re-reads the AT.Core source at test time, so a new literal-to-verdict path breaks the build until it is computed or adjudicated. 7 paths remain, ALL BOUNDARY authored judgements/input taxonomies; ZERO REFUTED.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["authored-verdict-audit", "optics-determinant-correction", "optics-reconciliation"],
            Narrative: "Can the rule be broken quietly? NO \u2014 it is ENFORCED. THE RULE: no result path may let a classification depend on a literal; every verdict must be traceable to computed evidence. A path `literal boolean (verdict-vocabulary name) -> score / classification / verdict function` is REFUTED unless it is COMPUTED or adjudicated SAFE / BOUNDARY with a cited reason. FAILS IF: literal -> verdict without a computation path. " +
            "WHY AN ENFORCEMENT MECHANISM RATHER THAN ANOTHER SWEEP: G_025 and G_026 each found instances of this class and fixed them by hand, and the class still recurred FOUR TIMES in the QG closure ladder alone, because fixing instances does not prevent a class recurring. AT.Core/ResearchXH/LiteralVerdictAudit.cs therefore RE-READS THE AT.CORE SOURCE AT TEST TIME and fails the suite on any un-triaged path, so a NEW literal-to-verdict path breaks the build until it is either computed or explicitly adjudicated. " +
            "HOW A PATH IS LOCATED: (1) every `record` is parsed for verdict-vocabulary BOOLEAN parameters, BY NAME AND BY POSITION, because the codebase writes both `Holds: true` and positional `..., true, ...`; (2) those booleans supplied as LITERALS at construction sites are collected; (3) the path counts only if the same file also CONSUMES the flag from a Score / Classify / Verdict / Rank / Assess / Grade / Count function. Condition (3) keeps the inventory honest: a literal nobody scores is inert. " +
