            "ZERO REFUTED REMAIN, and the registry STRUCTURALLY FORBIDS a REFUTED entry, because a refuted path is FIXED rather than tolerated. THE ONE REFUTED PATH FOUND AND FIXED: ResearchQG/GdaggerOriginAnalyzer.cs, where every evidence flag, the ratio AND the score were literals at all six construction sites, and Score feeds OrderByDescending (the RANKING). The Coincidence row was even INTERNALLY INCONSISTENT: RatioToA0 typed 1.0 while its own numerator PredictedGdagger was NaN, so the typed ratio did not follow from its own input. All four are now DERIVED from the predicted g-dagger: HasExactTwoPi = |predicted - cH0/(2pi)| / (cH0/(2pi)) < 1e-6; RatioToA0 = predicted / a0 with NaN propagating honestly; Matches = |RatioToA0 - 1| <= 0.15, which is the criterion the Verdict text itself states; Score = 3.0 if exact 2pi and matching, else 1.5 if not falsifiable, else 0.5. VERIFIED to reproduce the previously TYPED values for all six mechanisms (3.0 / 3.0 / 0.5 / 0.5 / 0.5 / 1.5), so the fix changes PROVENANCE, not the physics, and the NaN-ratio contradiction is gone. " +
            "REGRESSION RECORD: FixedByComputation lists the eleven sites fixed by G_025/G_026/G_027 (the optics determinant and gamma; the four QG criteria tables; the Born-rule Survives and pass arrays; the RAR Derived rows; the g-dagger flags, ratio and score). They no longer SCAN, so a regression, meaning a literal reappearing, is caught by the scan and CANNOT BE EXCUSED BY THE REGISTRY. The scanner is also tested against a synthetic snippet in both directions: it must FIRE on the G_025/G_026 fingerprint and be SILENT when the flag is computed. " +
            "SCOPE: the scan covers AT.Core; AT.Tests, AT.App and AT.Book are downstream of the adjudicated objects. WHAT THE AUDIT DOES NOT CLAIM: it does not decide whether a verdict is CORRECT, only whether it is COMPUTED, and it forces the difference into the open rather than leaving it implied by a method name. " +
            "No reclassification; D_040 untouched; 5/5 PASSED, group G 223/223. VERDICTS: DERIVED / BOUNDARY / REFUTED.",
