        new("optics-determinant-correction", "Optics Determinant Correction", "Was the optics result actually derived? NO \u2014 independent verification of QG212 found a d-vs-(d\u22121) OFF-BY-ONE in the psi-perturbed determinant (error unbounded in psi) and a HARD-CODED gamma never computed from the metric. Corrected at 12 sites; gamma is now DERIVED; the optics conclusion is restored on derived grounds, the measure-preservation premise is refuted, and TRM metric-origin moves to MODIFIED.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["optics-reconciliation", "spatial-closure", "light-propagation", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "Was the AT-QG optics result actually DERIVED, or only documented? ResearchY-G_025 verifies the arithmetic independently \u2014 and finds two real defects. " +
            "DEFECT 1 \u2014 OFF-BY-ONE IN THE psi-PERTURBED DETERMINANT. MetricAnsatzAudit asserted that for g00 = -rho^(2/d) e^(2 psi) and g_ii = rho^(2/d) e^(-2 psi/(d-1)), det g = -rho^2 for ANY psi, so sqrt(-g) = rho is unchanged; and PerturbedVolumeElement(x, d, b) returned Profile(x, a) = rho BY CONSTRUCTION \u2014 it never computed a determinant, so PsiPerturbationPreservesMeasure() could only ever return true. THE SPATIAL BLOCK HAS d FACTORS, NOT (d-1). Correct: det g = -rho^(2(d+1)/d) e^(-2 psi/(d-1)); sqrt(-det g) = rho^((d+1)/d) e^(-psi/(d-1)); sqrt(det g_ij) = rho e^(-d psi/(d-1)). At x = 1 and b = 0.0 / 0.3 / 0.5 / -3.0 the spatial element is 2.0000000000 / 1.2752563032 / 0.9447331055 / 180.0342626010 (errors 0.00 / 36.24 / 52.76 / 8901.71 %) and the 4-volume is 2.5198420998 / 2.1688481946 / 1.9624550005 / 11.2931487976 (errors 25.99 / 8.44 / 1.88 / 464.66 %). THE ERROR IS UNBOUNDED IN psi, which is why the shipped test asserting sameVolume == true could never catch it. CONSEQUENCE: 'sqrt(-g) = rho is preserved for ANY psi' is FALSE, and det g = -rho^2 is NOT psi-independent \u2014 psi = 0 is the ONLY member that preserves the counting measure, which STRENGTHENS the selection QG207 was making. " +
            "DEFECT 2 \u2014 gamma WAS A HARD-CODED CONSTANT. GammaPsiZero() => NonTensorLensing.ConformalGamma() (= -1.0) and GammaPsiNonZero() => NonTensorLensing.GrGamma() (= +1.0): not one code path computed gamma from the metric, so origin-score items 2 and 3 were ((1+1)/2 = 1) and (Shapiro(1) = (1+1)/2 * 2 = 2) \u2014 arithmetic on a literal, unable to fail. Nothing therefore detected that the CODED metric psi = b x has gamma != +1 anywhere: b = 0.3 gives +0.3352 / +0.0022 / -0.0930 / -0.0694 at x = 0.1 / 0.5 / 1.0 / 2.0, and b = 0.5 gives +0.3772 / +0.1054 / +0.0112 / -0.0037. gamma = +1 requires psi = -2 sigma (d-1)/(d-2) = -4 sigma at d = 3, i.e. -(4/3) ln(1 + a x^2) \u2014 QUADRATIC at small x \u2014 whereas the code uses psi = b x, LINEAR. " +
            "CORRECTIONS APPLIED, 12 SITES ACROSS 5 AT.Core FILES. PerturbedVolumeElement now COMPUTES rho e^(-d psi/(d-1)); PerturbedDet and PerturbedVolumeElement4D ADDED; PsiPerturbationPreservesMeasure now FALSE; PsiPerturbationBreaksMeasure and ConformalIsTheMeasurePreservingMember ADDED (both TRUE); GammaPsiZero and GammaPsiNonZero now COMPUTED via GammaFromPsiMetric = (g_ii - 1)/(g_00 + 1) (exact); GammaFromPsiMetricFirstOrder, PsiForGrOptics and GammaPsiNonZeroExact ADDED; ConformalIsRestrictedSector REBASED on the corrected member test; the Redshift doc corrected and PsiClockShiftFactor / PsiSectorShiftsClock ADDED; TRMCompatibilityAudit's 'metric-origin' moved UNCHANGED -> MODIFIED; TRMasUVCompletion and the HawkingTemperatureWithPsi citation corrected (its own psi exponent d/(d-1) = 3/2 was re-derived and IS correct). " +
            "DERIVED: at rho = 1.000001 / 1.5 / 2.0, gamma(psi = 0, exact) = -1.0000000000 in every row; gamma(psi = -4 sigma, first order) = +1.0000000000 in every row; gamma(psi = -4 sigma, exact) = +1.0000020001 / +2.2500000000 / +4.0000000000 = e^(6 sigma) = rho^2 at d = 3 \u2014 so gamma = +1 holds ONLY IN THE WEAK FIELD. " +
            "WHAT SURVIVES: gamma = -1 for g = rho^(2/d) eta; gamma = +1 for psi != 0 (derived); lensing = Shapiro = frame dragging = 0 at psi = 0 and full GR at psi != 0; and the restricted-sector classification. WHAT DOES NOT: 'the psi sector preserves the counting measure' (REFUTED), 'metric-origin => UNCHANGED' (REFUTED -> MODIFIED; corrected matrix 4 UNCHANGED / 2 MODIFIED / 0 BROKEN), and 'gamma = +1 as a property of the coded psi = b x metric' (it was a constant). OPTICS RESOLVED (4/4) is RESTORED, on the corrected basis. SCORECARD: 1 of QG212's 4 origin-score points was substantive before the fix. " +
            "BOUNDARY: at psi = -4 sigma the EXACT gamma drifts as rho^2 and the same psi shifts the CLOCK law sqrt(-g_00) = rho^(1/d) e^(psi) by e^(-4 sigma) = rho^(-4/3) \u2014 2.784532e-9 at the Earth's surface (invisible; GPS tests 0.2 %) but O(1) at compactness, so the O(x^2) completion is LOAD-BEARING AND STILL UNSPECIFIED. Record: Docs/Research/ATQG_ConformalOpticsDeterminantCorrection.md (AT-QG phase 320). " +
