        new("optics-reconciliation", "Optics Reconciliation", "Was light bending already solved? YES — the AT-QG programme resolved conformal optics in QG212 (Status COMPLETE / OPTICS RESOLVED, tests ATQG2120/2121/2122): psi = 0 gives gamma = -1, psi != 0 gives gamma = +1 with full GR optics, and psi is NOT a new primitive. This object RESTORES that result and retracts three G-chain errors.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["spatial-closure", "spatial-metric", "light-propagation", "source-law"],
            Narrative: "Was light bending already solved? YES. The AT-QG programme resolved conformal optics BEFORE the G-chain began: Docs/Research/ATQG_ConformalOpticsResolution.md (QG212) has Status COMPLETE - OPTICS RESOLVED, tests ATQG2120/2121/2122 all passed, core class AT.Core/ResearchXH/ConformalOpticsResolution.cs, and the two-sector table: psi = 0 (conformal g = rho^(2/d) eta) gives gamma = -1 with lensing = Shapiro = frame dragging = 0 and the redshift surviving; psi != 0 (the QG207 completion) gives gamma = +1 with lensing and Shapiro at full GR and frame dragging restored. The verdict: conformal no-lensing is a RESTRICTED SECTOR - 'not a numerical artifact' (gamma = -1 is exact within the slice), 'not physical GR' (the slice is an isotropic assumption), and 'the physical sector is psi != 0'. QG212's method line reads 'no new primitives'. " +
            "THE G-CHAIN MIS-STATED THIS STATUS, and ResearchY-G_024 retracts three claims. (1) G_021/G_022/G_023 call psi 'a MINIMAL NEW PRIMITIVE (QG24)' - SUPERSEDED by QG285/QG286/QG292: the trace/traceless decomposition of the one Difference at d = 3 gives 6 components = 1 TRACE (rho) + 5 TRACELESS, of which 2 are transverse-traceless (psi, spin-2), so the minimal primitive set is {Difference, eta} and psi adds nothing. WITHDRAWN. (2) G_022 section 6 concluded 'the psi route is EMPTY' by deriving psi = 0 from the clock law and the acceleration law; that derivation was arithmetically correct and PREMISE-FALSE, because it assumed sqrt(-g00) = rho^(1/d) is non-negotiable - but that IS the psi = 0 slice, and the physical sector has sqrt(-g00) = rho^(1/d) e^(psi). WITHDRAWN. (3) G_023's REFUTED verdict rested on (1), so its REASON is void. " +
            "WHAT SURVIVES AND IS SHARPENED. (a) The psi = 0 slice is excluded BY MEASUREMENT at a computable significance: Cassini 8.6957e4 sigma, VLBA 6.6660e3 sigma, Gaia 1.2481e2 sigma (QG26 gives the bare gamma = -1; G_021 gives the number). (b) THE INVARIANT SPLIT: to first order gamma = -B/A, so psi = 0 <=> A = B = sigma <=> gamma = -1 (the restricted isotropic slice) and gamma = +1 <=> A + B = 0 (h00 = h_ii). Two realisations: keep the clock law (A = sigma, B = -sigma = +x) giving G_023's k = B - A = 2x - the clock-law-preserving special case; or the QG207 completion at psi = -4 sigma giving A = -3 sigma, B = +3 sigma, k = -6x. So G_023's identity is the clock-preserving form, and 'psi = 0 <=> A = B' IS the quantitative content of QG212's word 'isotropic'. " +
            "THE ONE GENUINE OPEN ITEM THIS AUDIT ADDS: in the QG207 parametrisation gamma = +1 requires psi = -4 sigma, so the completion is NOT redshift-neutral - the clock shift is e^(4x) - 1 = 2.784532e-9 at the Earth's surface and 8.490012e-6 at the Sun, both far below the verified tests (GPS +38.5 vs +38.6 us/day = 0.2 %; Cassini 2.3e-5 on gamma), so there is NO solar-system conflict and the implied bound |psi| <= 2e-3 from GPS is 7.2e5x LOOSER than required. BUT at compactness the leading-order redshift z = e^(-3x) - 1 turns NEGATIVE: -0.259182 at x = 0.10, -0.403664 at 0.172317, -0.523366 at 0.247002. PPN fixes only the FIRST-ORDER psi = -4 sigma, so the O(x^2) form of the completion is LOAD-BEARING AND UNCOMPUTED - a BOUNDARY flag, NOT a refutation. " +
            "VERDICTS: DERIVED = the two-sector structure as QG212 states it; the psi = 0 slice's measured exclusion; the invariant split; and that psi introduces no new primitive. BOUNDARY = the exact (nonlinear) completion is unspecified (the O(x^2) form is load-bearing for the strong-field redshift), and psi's ontological status is a documented boundary (QG299). REFUTED = G_022 section 6 and G_023's verdict reason. " +
            "No reclassification of the QG212 result - this audit RESTORES it; D_040 untouched; no canonical claim, value or equation changes; no new primitive.",
            Formula: "QG212 two sectors: psi = 0 -> gamma = -1, (1+gamma)/2 = 0;  psi != 0 (QG207) -> gamma = +1, (1+gamma)/2 = 1;  gamma = -B/A so psi = 0 <=> A = B and gamma = +1 <=> A + B = 0;  psi = -4 sigma <=> A = -3 sigma, B = +3 sigma, k = -6x",
            CalculationId: "optics-reconciliation",
            References: ["ResearchY-G_024", "ResearchY-G_023", "ResearchY-G_022", "ResearchY-G_021"],
            AuditIds: ["g024"]),

        new("spatial-closure", "Spatial Sector Closure", "Can ANY spatial metric be derived WITHOUT NEW PRIMITIVES giving gamma ~ +1 while preserving the clock law, the source law and the acceleration law? NO: gamma is controlled by ONE conformal invariant k = B - A, and AT pins k = 0 from two independent directions. Closes ResearchY-G_022.", TheoryLayer.Physics, TheoryClassification.Derived, TheoryObjectKind.Derivation,
            ["spatial-metric", "light-propagation", "source-law", "clock-rate"],
            Narrative: "Can ANY spatial metric be derived WITHOUT NEW PRIMITIVES yielding gamma ~ +1 while preserving the clock law, the source law and the acceleration law? Success criterion: gamma ~ +1 WITHOUT changing g00 physics. ANSWER: NO - one conformal invariant obstructs it and AT's construction pins it to zero. " +
            "THE FRAMEWORK (isotropic form - where PPN gamma is DEFINED): ds^2 = -e^(2A) dt^2 + e^(2B)(dR^2 + R^2 dOmega^2); Phi = (e^(2A)-1)/2; gamma = -(e^(2B)-1)/(e^(2A)-1) ~ -1 + k/x with k := B - A. A static spherical metric therefore has exactly TWO functions, A (time) and B (space), and gamma is controlled by ONE number. " +
            "k IS THE CONFORMAL INVARIANT: under g -> Omega^2 g both exponents shift by the same omega, so k = B - A is UNCHANGED - k is exactly the class data the causal-order -> conformal-class step (Malament 1977) supplies. Conformal flatness means g = Omega^2 eta, i.e. A = B, i.e. g_rr = -g00 - which IS k = 0. So conformal flatness <=> k = 0 <=> gamma = -1 for EVERY A (G_022's theorem, restated). Verified for omega in {0, 0.37, -2.5, 1e-3}, and no rescaling can flatten a k != 0 metric. " +
            "AT PINS k = 0 FROM TWO INDEPENDENT DIRECTIONS: (1) the CLOCK LAW requires sqrt(-g00) = rho^(1/d) = e^sigma, so A = sigma = -x; (2) the COUNTING MEASURE requires the spatial volume element to BE the count, sqrt(det g_ij) = rho = e^(-3x), so e^(3B) = rho and B = sigma = -x. Both express the SAME primitive (rho) and pin their own exponent to the SAME scalar sigma, so k = B - A = 0 IDENTICALLY, hence gamma = -1 at EVERY compactness: Earth -6.96133e-10, Sun -2.122503e-6, 1e-4, J0740+6620 -0.247002 - all with volume/rho = 1.000000000 and gamma = -1. This is a theorem about AT's construction, not a coincidence: violating either condition breaks a named law (A != sigma breaks the clock law and the redshift; B != sigma breaks the counting measure by e^(3 delta)). " +
            "WHAT gamma = +1 WOULD COST: keeping the clock law (A = sigma, so g00 physics is UNCHANGED) and demanding gamma = +1 gives -(e^(2B)-1) = e^(2A)-1, i.e. e^(2B) = 2 - e^(2A), so B = (1/2) ln(2 - e^(-2x)) with k = B - A = 2x to first order. gamma = +1 holds to 1e-9 in every row, and the price is the spatial volume e^(3k): 1.000000 at Earth, 1.000013 at the Sun, 1.000600 at x = 1e-4, and 3.437585 at J0740+6620 (B = 0.1645877, k = 0.4115897 against k_lin = 0.494004). Changing the volume measure IS changing a primitive. " +
            "THE PRIMITIVE INVENTORY - CLOSURE: Q-event counts, rho, sigma = (1/d) ln rho, the DiffuseStep relaxation Lambda = I - W, the D96 lattice, the spectral / lambda structure and information content are ALL SCALARS - each fixes ONE function, and any deformation delta = B - sigma both breaks the volume identity by e^(3 delta) and moves gamma to -1 + delta/x; none supplies k = 2x. The ONE non-scalar ingredient is the causal ORDER, which is what supplies the conformal CLASS - and AT's order is the flat D96 ring order: the ring collapses 96 cells onto only 45 eigenvalues (histogram {1:1, 2:42, 5:1, 6:1}, free room Sum(m-1) = 51) while the degeneracy-free random control has 96 distinct values (all multiplicity 1), so its class is [eta] and k = 0. The complement structures that might suggest a natural 1/rho are all CONSTANTS - free room 51/95 = 0.536842, the 95 -> 44 -> 1 chain = 2.159091, the possible/accessible factor 3.746e5, the spectral total 1152 - and NONE matches 1/rho at any compactness. NO EXISTING PRIMITIVE CAN MOVE k. " +
