            "WHAT gamma = +1 REQUIRES. g_rr = e^(2 beta sigma) gives gamma = -beta: beta = +1 (conformal) -> -1; beta = 0 (flat space) -> 0; beta = -1 (reciprocal) -> +1. So gamma = +1 needs TWO DIFFERENT FACTORS: g00 = -rho^(2/d) = -e^(-2x) (AT's own time sector, untouched) and g_rr = +rho^(-2/d) = +e^(+2x). That metric PASSES EVERY REQUIREMENT THE QUESTION SETS - clock law EXACT, source law EXACT, slow-particle acceleration EXACT, redshift z_AT = e^x - 1 = 0.2801817 identical to G_020, gamma = +1 (Cassini 0.9130 sigma, VLBA 0.6667, Gaia 0.1875) - but it is NOT CONFORMALLY FLAT: g_rr + g00 = e^(2x) - e^(-2x) = 2 sinh(2x) = 1.028687 at x = 0.247002, so the causal-order -> conformal-class step (Malament 1977) does not produce it. TWO FACTORS IS A POSTULATE. " +
            "THE PRICE IS VISIBLE: the native spatial metric is Omega = rho^(1/d), whose volume measure Omega^3 is EXACTLY the counting measure rho; the gamma = +1 sector needs Omega = rho^(-1/d), whose volume measure is Omega^3 = 1/rho - the RECIPROCAL of the counting measure. The choice is not which factor but the counting measure or its reciprocal. " +
            "THE EXCLUSION TABLE: gamma = -1 gives Cassini 8.6957e4, VLBA 6.6660e3, Gaia 124.8125 sigma - REFUTED; gamma = 0 (flat space) gives 4.3479e4, 3.3327e3, 62.3125 sigma - REFUTED; gamma = +1 gives 0.9130, 0.6667, 0.1875 sigma - ALLOWED. " +
