        new("g020", "Neutron-Star Redshift Audit", "Can any currently measured neutron-star redshift exclude AT's exponential clock law?",
            "Sources: NICER masses and radii, X-ray burst redshifts, published uncertainties; compare AT (g00 = -e^(2x)) with GR (g00 = -(1+2x)); output EXCLUDED / ALLOWED / PREFERRED; critical: the precision on z and M/R for 5 sigma. THE FRAMEWORK: with x = GM/(Rc^2) > 0, z_AT = e^x - 1 and z_GR = (1 - 2x)^(-1/2) - 1, Dz = z_GR - z_AT > 0, and S = Dz / sqrt(sigma_z^2 + (dz/dx)^2 sigma_x^2) with dz/dx = (1 - 2x)^(-3/2); AT always predicts the SMALLER redshift and the midpoint decides which law is closer. " +
